WEBVTT

02:07.836 --> 02:10.255
ARE YOU HERE TO KILL ME?

02:17.638 --> 02:20.849
I KNOW WHAT THIS IS.

02:20.891 --> 02:23.602
I'VE SEEN ONE BEFORE...

02:24.812 --> 02:27.773
...MANY, MANY YEARS AGO.

02:27.815 --> 02:33.570
IT BELONGED TO A MAN I MET
IN A HALF-REMEMBERED DREAM.

02:35.489 --> 02:40.661
A MAN POSSESSED
OF SOME RADICAL NOTIONS.

02:44.414 --> 02:46.792
WHAT <i>IS</i>
THE MOST RESILIENT PARASITE?

02:46.834 --> 02:49.252
A BACTERIA?

02:49.294 --> 02:51.379
A VIRUS?

02:51.421 --> 02:52.923
AN INTESTINAL WORM?

02:52.965 --> 02:56.301
UH...WHAT MR. COBB
IS TRYING TO SAY--

02:56.343 --> 02:57.594
AN IDEA.

02:58.595 --> 03:00.597
RESILIENT.
HIGHLY CONTAGIOUS.

03:00.639 --> 03:03.224
ONCE AN IDEA HAS TAKEN HOLD
OF THE BRAIN,

03:03.266 --> 03:05.644
IT'S ALMOST IMPOSSIBLE
TO ERADICATE.

03:05.686 --> 03:08.605
AN IDEA THAT IS FULLY FORMED,
FULLY UNDERSTOOD--

03:08.647 --> 03:09.982
THAT STICKS.

03:10.024 --> 03:11.733
RIGHT IN THERE SOMEWHERE.

03:11.775 --> 03:13.401
FOR SOMEONE LIKE YOU
TO STEAL?

03:13.443 --> 03:14.736
YES.
IN THE DREAM STATE,

03:14.778 --> 03:16.571
YOUR CONSCIOUS DEFENSES
ARE LOWERED,

03:16.613 --> 03:19.158
AND THAT MAKES YOUR THOUGHTS
VULNERABLE TO THEFT.

03:19.198 --> 03:20.659
IT'S CALLED EXTRACTION.

03:20.701 --> 03:23.244
MR. SAITO,
WE CAN TRAIN YOUR SUBCONSCIOUS

03:23.286 --> 03:24.830
TO DEFEND ITSELF

03:24.872 --> 03:26.957
FROM EVEN
THE MOST SKILLED EXTRACTOR.

03:26.999 --> 03:28.542
HOW CAN YOU DO THAT?

03:28.583 --> 03:30.794
BECAUSE I <i>AM</i>
THE MOST SKILLED EXTRACTOR.

03:30.836 --> 03:33.922
I KNOW HOW TO SEARCH YOUR MIND
AND FIND YOUR SECRETS.

03:33.964 --> 03:35.090
I KNOW THE TRICKS.

03:35.132 --> 03:36.925
AND I CAN TEACH THEM
TO YOU,

03:36.967 --> 03:38.385
SO THAT EVEN
WHEN YOU'RE ASLEEP,

03:38.426 --> 03:40.804
YOUR DEFENSE
IS NEVER DOWN.

03:40.846 --> 03:42.305
LOOK, IF YOU WANT MY HELP,

03:42.347 --> 03:45.600
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO BE
COMPLETELY OPEN WITH ME.

03:45.642 --> 03:47.561
I NEED TO KNOW MY WAY
AROUND YOUR THOUGHTS

03:47.602 --> 03:49.229
BETTER THAN YOUR WIFE,

03:49.270 --> 03:51.481
BETTER THAN YOUR THERAPIST,
BETTER THAN ANYONE.

03:51.523 --> 03:52.900
IF THIS IS A DREAM,

03:52.941 --> 03:54.735
AND YOU HAVE A SAFE
FULL OF SECRETS,

03:54.776 --> 03:57.237
I NEED TO KNOW
WHAT'S IN THAT SAFE.

03:57.278 --> 03:58.864
IN ORDER
FOR THIS ALL TO WORK,

03:58.906 --> 04:00.824
YOU NEED TO COMPLETELY
LET ME IN.

04:02.951 --> 04:05.162
ENJOY YOUR EVENING, GENTLEMEN,

04:05.204 --> 04:08.082
AS I CONSIDER
YOUR PROPOSAL.

04:09.666 --> 04:11.835
HE KNOWS.

04:15.172 --> 04:16.381
WHAT'S GOING ON UP THERE?

05:10.518 --> 05:13.230
SAITO KNOWS.
HE'S PLAYING WITH US.

05:13.272 --> 05:15.649
DOESN'T MATTER.
I CAN GET IT HERE. TRUST ME.

05:15.690 --> 05:17.442
THE INFORMATION
IS IN THE SAFE.

05:17.484 --> 05:19.987
HE LOOKED RIGHT AT IT
WHEN I MENTIONED SECRETS.

05:20.028 --> 05:22.322
WHAT'S SHE DOING HERE?

05:24.658 --> 05:26.701
JUST HEAD BACK
TO THE ROOM.

05:26.743 --> 05:28.328
ALL RIGHT?
I'LL TAKE CARE OF THIS.

05:28.369 --> 05:30.330
OKAY, MAKE SURE YOU DO.
WE'RE HERE TO WORK.

05:38.088 --> 05:40.924
IF I JUMPED...

05:40.966 --> 05:43.051
WOULD I SURVIVE?

05:45.344 --> 05:48.890
WITH A CLEAN DIVE,
PERHAPS.

05:48.932 --> 05:50.184
MAL, WHAT ARE YOU
DOING HERE?

05:50.225 --> 05:52.519
I THOUGHT
YOU MIGHT BE MISSING ME.

05:52.560 --> 05:53.895
YOU KNOW THAT I AM.

05:53.937 --> 05:55.814
BUT I...

05:55.856 --> 05:57.941
I CAN'T
TRUST YOU ANYMORE.

05:57.983 --> 06:00.277
SO WHAT?

06:00.319 --> 06:03.071
LOOKS LIKE
ARTHUR'S TASTE.

06:03.113 --> 06:05.364
ACTUALLY,
THE SUBJECT IS PARTIAL

06:05.406 --> 06:07.617
TO POSTWAR
BRITISH PAINTERS.

06:07.659 --> 06:10.996
PLEASE, HAVE A SEAT.

06:18.628 --> 06:20.421
TELL ME...

06:20.463 --> 06:22.132
DO THE CHILDREN MISS ME?

06:25.302 --> 06:28.180
YOU CAN'T IMAGINE.

06:32.267 --> 06:33.476
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

06:33.518 --> 06:35.187
JUST GETTING
SOME FRESH AIR.

06:35.229 --> 06:37.731
STAY WHERE YOU ARE, MAL.

06:50.244 --> 06:52.746
COME ON. DAMN IT.

07:53.098 --> 07:56.184
TURN AROUND!

07:56.226 --> 07:57.477
THE GUN, DOM.

08:06.445 --> 08:07.904
PLEASE.

08:19.707 --> 08:22.419
NOW THE ENVELOPE,
MR. COBB.

08:22.461 --> 08:26.214
DID SHE TELL YOU?
OR HAVE YOU KNOWN ALL ALONG?

08:26.256 --> 08:28.342
THAT YOU'RE HERE
TO STEAL FROM ME

08:28.383 --> 08:31.594
OR THAT WE ARE
ACTUALLY ASLEEP?

08:35.640 --> 08:38.101
I WANT TO KNOW THE NAME
OF YOUR EMPLOYER.

08:39.602 --> 08:42.481
UH, THERE'S NO USE
THREATENING HIM IN A DREAM,

08:42.563 --> 08:44.024
RIGHT, MAL?

08:44.065 --> 08:47.152
THAT DEPENDS
ON WHAT YOU'RE THREATENING.

08:47.194 --> 08:49.946
KILLING HIM
WOULD JUST WAKE HIM UP.

08:49.988 --> 08:51.614
BUT PAIN...

08:53.200 --> 08:55.410
AAH! UGH!

08:55.452 --> 08:57.704
...PAIN IS IN THE MIND.

08:57.745 --> 08:59.289
AND JUDGING BY THE DECOR,

08:59.331 --> 09:01.875
WE'RE IN <i>YOUR</i> MIND,
AREN'T WE, ARTHUR?

09:13.720 --> 09:15.222
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?!
IT'S TOO SOON!

09:15.263 --> 09:16.973
I KNOW.
BUT THE DREAM'S COLLAPSING.

09:17.015 --> 09:19.267
I'M GONNA TRY TO KEEP SAITO
UNDER A LITTLE BIT LONGER.

09:19.309 --> 09:20.519
WE'RE ALMOST THERE.

09:34.282 --> 09:36.576
HE WAS CLOSE.

09:36.617 --> 09:39.079
<i>VERY</i> CLOSE.

09:51.674 --> 09:53.927
AAH! STOP HIM!

10:08.567 --> 10:09.484
AAH!

10:20.245 --> 10:21.746
THIS ISN'T GONNA WORK.
WAKE HIM UP.

10:32.299 --> 10:33.007
AAH!

10:43.268 --> 10:44.811
HE WON'T WAKE!

10:49.690 --> 10:51.109
GIVE HIM THE KICK!
WHAT?

10:51.151 --> 10:52.569
DUNK HIM.

11:28.271 --> 11:29.814
AAH.

11:32.900 --> 11:34.653
NASH!

11:36.321 --> 11:38.365
HE'S OUT.

11:43.537 --> 11:46.623
YOU CAME PREPARED, HMM?

11:46.665 --> 11:48.500
NOT EVEN MY HEAD OF SECURITY
KNOWS THIS APARTMENT.

11:48.542 --> 11:49.959
HOW DID YOU FIND IT?

11:50.001 --> 11:52.379
IT'S VERY DIFFICULT
FOR A MAN OF YOUR POSITION

11:52.420 --> 11:54.422
TO KEEP A LOVE NEST
LIKE THIS SECRET,

11:54.464 --> 11:57.091
PARTICULARLY WHERE THERE'S
A MARRIED WOMAN INVOLVED.

11:57.133 --> 11:58.051
SHE WOULD NEVER.

11:58.092 --> 12:00.178
YET, HERE WE ARE...

12:00.220 --> 12:00.887
WITH A DILEMMA.

12:00.928 --> 12:02.347
THEY'RE GETTING CLOSER.

12:02.389 --> 12:03.764
YOU GOT
WHAT YOU CAME FOR.

12:03.806 --> 12:05.350
WELL, THAT'S NOT TRUE.

12:05.392 --> 12:08.102
YOU LEFT OUT A KEY PIECE
OF INFORMATION, DIDN'T YOU?

12:08.144 --> 12:09.437
YOU HELD SOMETHING BACK,

12:09.479 --> 12:11.481
BECAUSE YOU KNEW
WHAT WE WERE UP TO.

12:11.523 --> 12:13.400
QUESTION IS,
WHY'D YOU LET US IN AT ALL?

12:13.441 --> 12:14.526
AN AUDITION.

12:14.568 --> 12:16.611
AN AUDITION FOR WHAT?

12:16.653 --> 12:18.655
DOESN'T MATTER.
YOU FAILED.

12:18.697 --> 12:21.533
WE EXTRACTED EVERY BIT OF
INFORMATION YOU HAD IN THERE.

12:21.575 --> 12:24.202
BUT YOUR DECEPTION
WAS OBVIOUS.

12:54.691 --> 12:59.778
<i>♪ NON! RIEN DE RIEN... ♪</i>

13:04.992 --> 13:07.746
SO, LEAVE ME AND GO.

13:07.786 --> 13:09.539
YOU DON'T SEEM TO UNDERSTAND,
MR. SAITO.

13:09.581 --> 13:11.249
THAT CORPORATION
THAT HIRED US,

13:11.291 --> 13:13.710
THEY WON'T ACCEPT FAILURE.

13:13.752 --> 13:16.254
WE WON'T LAST TWO DAYS.

13:16.296 --> 13:18.881
COBB?

13:18.923 --> 13:21.384
LOOKS LIKE I'M GONNA HAVE TO
DO THIS A LITTLE MORE SIMPLY.

13:22.719 --> 13:24.763
TELL US WHAT YOU KNOW!

13:24.803 --> 13:26.640
TELL US
WHAT YOU KNOW NOW!

13:29.643 --> 13:32.853
I HAVE ALWAYS HATED
THIS CARPET.

13:32.895 --> 13:37.400
IT'S STAINED AND FRAYED
IN SUCH DISTINCTIVE WAYS.

13:37.442 --> 13:42.113
BUT VERY DEFINITELY
MADE OF WOOL.

13:42.155 --> 13:44.949
RIGHT NOW...

13:44.991 --> 13:47.034
I'M LYING ON POLYESTER.

13:50.829 --> 13:53.374
WHICH MEANS...

13:53.416 --> 13:56.961
I'M NOT LYING ON MY CARPET
IN MY APARTMENT.

13:57.003 --> 14:01.090
YOU HAVE LIVED UP
TO YOUR REPUTATION, MR. COBB.

14:01.132 --> 14:03.551
I'M STILL DREAMING.

14:10.099 --> 14:12.018
HOW'D IT GO?
NOT GOOD.

14:16.439 --> 14:18.899
DREAM WITHIN A DREAM.

14:18.941 --> 14:21.528
AH, I'M IMPRESSED.

14:22.737 --> 14:25.824
BUT IN MY DREAM,
YOU PLAY BY MY RULES.

14:25.865 --> 14:28.785
AH, YES, BUT, YOU SEE,
MR. SAITO...

14:28.827 --> 14:31.245
WE'RE NOT IN YOUR DREAM.
WE'RE IN MINE.

14:36.793 --> 14:40.213
AAH!

14:41.631 --> 14:44.133
ASSHOLE.
HOW DO YOU MESS UP THE CARPET?

14:44.175 --> 14:46.594
IT WASN'T MY FAULT.
YOU'RE THE ARCHITECT.

14:46.636 --> 14:48.471
I DIDN'T KNOW HE WAS GONNA
RUB HIS DAMN CHEEK ON IT!

14:48.513 --> 14:50.181
THAT'S ENOUGH.

14:50.223 --> 14:52.809
AND YOU. WHAT THE HELL
WAS ALL THAT?

14:52.851 --> 14:54.561
I HAVE IT UNDER CONTROL.

14:54.602 --> 14:56.187
I'D HATE TO SEE YOU
<i>OUT</i> OF CONTROL.

14:56.229 --> 14:58.481
ALL RIGHT,
WE DON'T HAVE TIME FOR THIS.

14:58.523 --> 15:00.107
I'M GETTING OFF AT KYOTO.

15:00.149 --> 15:02.151
WHY? HE'S NOT GONNA CHECK
EVERY COMPARTMENT.

15:02.193 --> 15:03.820
WELL, I DON'T LIKE TRAINS.

15:03.862 --> 15:06.823
LISTEN.
EVERY MAN FOR HIMSELF.

16:20.146 --> 16:21.564
YES, HELLO?

16:21.606 --> 16:23.232
Hi, Daddy.

16:23.274 --> 16:25.025
Hi, Dad.

16:25.067 --> 16:27.278
HEY, GUYS. HEY.
HOW ARE YOU?

16:27.320 --> 16:28.822
HOW YOU DOIN', HUH?

16:28.863 --> 16:30.114
Good.

16:30.156 --> 16:31.365
Okay, I guess.

16:31.407 --> 16:33.576
OKAY?

16:33.618 --> 16:35.495
WHO'S JUST OKAY?
IS THAT YOU, JAMES?

16:35.536 --> 16:37.455
Yeah.

16:37.497 --> 16:38.915
When are you
coming home, Dad?

16:40.500 --> 16:43.085
WELL, I CAN'T, SWEETHEART.
I CAN'T.

16:43.127 --> 16:44.963
NOT FOR A WHILE,
REMEMBER?

16:45.004 --> 16:46.631
Why?

16:46.673 --> 16:48.675
LOOK, I...I TOLD YOU.

16:48.716 --> 16:52.052
I'M-- I'M AWAY
BECAUSE I'M WORKING, RIGHT?

16:52.094 --> 16:55.974
Grandma says
you're never coming back.

16:56.015 --> 16:58.685
PHILLIPA, IS THAT YOU?

16:58.726 --> 17:01.437
PUT GRANDMA ON THE PHONE
FOR ME, WILL YOU?

17:01.479 --> 17:03.606
She's shaking her head.

17:05.232 --> 17:08.110
WE'LL JUST HOPE
SHE'S WRONG ABOUT THAT.

17:08.152 --> 17:10.613
Daddy?

17:10.655 --> 17:11.865
YEAH, JAMES?

17:11.906 --> 17:13.700
Is Mommy with you?

17:15.910 --> 17:19.539
JAMES,
WE TALKED ABOUT THIS.

17:19.580 --> 17:22.500
MOMMY'S NOT HERE ANYMORE.

17:22.542 --> 17:25.294
Where?

17:25.336 --> 17:28.506
That's enough, kids.
Say bye-bye.

17:28.548 --> 17:31.133
LISTEN, I'M-- I'M GONNA SEND
SOME PRESENTS WITH GRANDPA.

17:31.175 --> 17:32.385
ALL RIGHT?

17:32.426 --> 17:33.636
AND YOU BE GOOD.
YOU BE...

17:42.102 --> 17:44.689
OUR RIDE'S ON THE ROOF.

17:44.731 --> 17:46.440
RIGHT.

17:53.072 --> 17:54.365
HEY, ARE YOU OKAY?

17:54.407 --> 17:56.325
YEAH.
YEAH, I'M FINE. WHY?

17:56.367 --> 17:58.995
WELL, DOWN IN THE DREAM,
MAL SHOWING UP.

17:59.037 --> 18:00.997
LOOK, I'M, UH,
SORRY ABOUT YOUR LEG.

18:01.039 --> 18:02.415
WON'T HAPPEN AGAIN.

18:02.456 --> 18:04.000
IT'S GETTING WORSE,
ISN'T IT?

18:04.042 --> 18:05.752
ONE APOLOGY'S ALL YOU'RE
GETTING, ALL RIGHT, ARTHUR?

18:05.793 --> 18:07.045
WHERE'S NASH?

18:07.086 --> 18:08.796
HE HASN'T SHOWN.
YOU WANT TO WAIT?

18:08.838 --> 18:11.298
NO, WE WERE SUPPOSED TO
DELIVER SAITO'S EXPANSION PLANS

18:11.340 --> 18:13.009
TO COBOL ENGINEERING
TWO HOURS AGO.

18:13.051 --> 18:14.468
BY NOW,
THEY KNOW WE FAILED.

18:14.510 --> 18:16.470
IT'S TIME WE DISAPPEAR.

18:17.346 --> 18:19.724
WHERE YOU GONNA GO?
BUENOS AIRES.

18:19.766 --> 18:20.934
I CAN LIE LOW THERE,

18:20.975 --> 18:23.019
MAYBE SNIFF OUT A JOB
WHEN THINGS QUIET DOWN.

18:23.061 --> 18:25.396
YOU?
STATESIDE.

18:25.438 --> 18:27.273
SEND MY REGARDS.

18:33.237 --> 18:34.864
HE SOLD YOU OUT.

18:34.906 --> 18:37.241
THOUGHT TO COME TO ME
AND BARGAIN FOR HIS LIFE.

18:37.283 --> 18:41.161
SO, I OFFER YOU
THE SATISFACTION.

18:44.415 --> 18:47.043
IT'S NOT THE WAY
I DEAL WITH THINGS.

18:59.847 --> 19:01.099
WHAT WILL YOU DO
WITH HIM?

19:01.140 --> 19:02.976
NOTHING.

19:03.017 --> 19:06.562
BUT I CAN'T SPEAK
FOR COBOL ENGINEERING.

19:19.700 --> 19:21.535
WHAT DO YOU WANT
FROM US?

19:21.577 --> 19:23.203
INCEPTION.

19:24.413 --> 19:26.582
IS IT POSSIBLE?
OF COURSE NOT.

19:26.624 --> 19:29.669
IF YOU CAN STEAL AN IDEA
FROM SOMEONE'S MIND,

19:29.710 --> 19:31.754
WHY CAN'T YOU
PLANT ONE THERE INSTEAD?

19:31.796 --> 19:33.714
OKAY. HERE'S ME PLANTING
AN IDEA IN YOUR HEAD.

19:33.756 --> 19:35.675
I SAY TO YOU,
"DON'T THINK ABOUT ELEPHANTS."

19:35.716 --> 19:36.968
WHAT ARE YOU
THINKING ABOUT?

19:37.010 --> 19:38.594
ELEPHANTS.

19:38.636 --> 19:40.096
RIGHT. BUT IT'S
NOT <i>YOUR</i> IDEA,

19:40.138 --> 19:42.098
BECAUSE YOU <i>KNOW</i>
I GAVE IT TO YOU.

19:42.140 --> 19:43.683
THE SUBJECT'S
MIND CAN ALWAYS TRACE

19:43.724 --> 19:45.309
THE
GENESIS OF THE IDEA.

19:45.351 --> 19:47.186
TRUE INSPIRATION'S
IMPOSSIBLE TO FAKE.

19:47.227 --> 19:48.187
IT'S NOT TRUE.

19:50.148 --> 19:51.774
CAN YOU DO IT?

19:51.816 --> 19:53.651
ARE YOU OFFERING ME
A CHOICE?

19:53.693 --> 19:56.946
BECAUSE I CAN FIND MY OWN WAY
TO SQUARE THINGS WITH COBOL.

19:56.988 --> 19:59.157
THEN YOU DO
HAVE A CHOICE.

19:59.198 --> 20:01.034
AND I CHOOSE
TO LEAVE, SIR.

20:05.872 --> 20:07.665
TELL THE CREW
WHERE YOU WANT TO GO.

20:12.962 --> 20:14.047
HEY, MR. COBB!

20:16.298 --> 20:18.968
HOW WOULD YOU
LIKE TO GO HOME?

20:19.010 --> 20:20.928
TO AMERICA?

20:20.970 --> 20:23.639
TO YOUR CHILDREN?

20:23.681 --> 20:27.143
YOU CAN'T FIX THAT!
NO ONE CAN!

20:27.185 --> 20:28.853
JUST LIKE INCEPTION.

20:28.895 --> 20:30.354
COBB, COME ON.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.860
HOW COMPLEX IS THE IDEA?

20:35.902 --> 20:37.195
SIMPLE ENOUGH.

20:37.236 --> 20:38.905
NO IDEA IS SIMPLE

20:38.946 --> 20:40.907
WHEN YOU NEED TO PLANT IT
IN SOMEBODY ELSE'S MIND.

20:40.948 --> 20:44.785
MY MAIN COMPETITOR IS AN OLD MAN
IN POOR HEALTH.

20:44.827 --> 20:48.998
HIS SON WILL SOON INHERIT
CONTROL OF THE CORPORATION.

20:49.040 --> 20:53.211
I NEED HIM TO DECIDE TO BREAK UP
HIS FATHER'S EMPIRE.

20:53.252 --> 20:55.379
COBB, WE SHOULD WALK
AWAY FROM THIS.

20:55.421 --> 20:57.673
HOLD ON.

20:57.715 --> 21:01.343
IF I WERE TO DO THIS,
IF...I EVEN <i>COULD</i> DO IT,

21:01.385 --> 21:03.054
I'D NEED A GUARANTEE.

21:03.096 --> 21:05.639
HOW DO I KNOW
YOU CAN DELIVER?

21:05.681 --> 21:07.850
YOU DON'T.

21:07.892 --> 21:09.727
BUT I CAN.

21:09.769 --> 21:14.314
SO, DO YOU WANT
TO TAKE A LEAP OF FAITH...

21:14.356 --> 21:18.945
OR BECOME AN OLD MAN,
FILLED WITH REGRET,

21:18.986 --> 21:21.655
WAITING TO DIE ALONE?

21:24.324 --> 21:26.493
ASSEMBLE YOUR TEAM,
MR. COBB.

21:26.535 --> 21:29.038
AND CHOOSE YOUR PEOPLE
MORE WISELY.

21:37.046 --> 21:39.006
LOOK, I KNOW HOW MUCH
YOU WANT TO GO HOME.

21:41.134 --> 21:43.469
THIS CAN'T BE DONE.

21:43.510 --> 21:47.181
YES, IT CAN.
JUST HAVE TO GO DEEP ENOUGH.

21:47.223 --> 21:49.058
YOU DON'T KNOW THAT.

21:49.100 --> 21:51.894
I'VE DONE IT BEFORE.

21:51.936 --> 21:54.230
WHO'D YOU DO IT TO?

21:58.484 --> 22:02.280
WHY ARE WE GOING
TO PARIS?

22:02.321 --> 22:05.241
WE'RE GONNA NEED
A NEW ARCHITECT.

22:20.047 --> 22:23.717
YOU NEVER <i>DID</i> LIKE
YOUR OFFICE, DID YOU?

22:24.927 --> 22:30.348
NO SPACE TO THINK
IN THAT BROOM CUPBOARD.

22:30.390 --> 22:33.269
IS IT SAFE FOR YOU
TO BE HERE?

22:33.311 --> 22:35.688
EXTRADITION BETWEEN FRANCE
AND THE UNITED STATES

22:35.729 --> 22:36.939
IS A BUREAUCRATIC
NIGHTMARE.

22:36.981 --> 22:38.107
YOU KNOW THAT.

22:38.149 --> 22:39.692
I THINK THEY MIGHT
FIND A WAY

22:39.733 --> 22:41.027
TO MAKE IT WORK
IN <i>YOUR</i> CASE.

22:41.068 --> 22:42.987
LOOK, I, UH...

22:43.029 --> 22:45.239
BROUGHT THESE FOR YOU
TO GIVE TO THE KIDS

22:45.281 --> 22:46.782
WHEN YOU HAVE A CHANCE.

22:46.824 --> 22:49.118
IT'LL TAKE MORE THAN
THE OCCASIONAL STUFFED ANIMAL

22:49.160 --> 22:51.745
TO CONVINCE THOSE CHILDREN
THEY STILL HAVE A FATHER.

22:51.787 --> 22:54.623
I'M JUST DOING WHAT I KNOW.
I'M DOING WHAT <i>YOU</i> TAUGHT ME.

22:54.665 --> 22:57.626
I NEVER TAUGHT YOU
TO BE A THIEF.

22:57.668 --> 22:59.419
NO, YOU TAUGHT ME
TO NAVIGATE PEOPLE'S MINDS.

22:59.461 --> 23:01.005
BUT AFTER WHAT HAPPENED,

23:01.047 --> 23:03.257
THERE WEREN'T A WHOLE LOT
OF LEGITIMATE WAYS

23:03.299 --> 23:04.717
FOR ME TO USE THAT SKILL.

23:08.721 --> 23:11.182
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING HERE, DOM?

23:11.224 --> 23:15.686
I THINK
I FOUND A WAY HOME.

23:15.728 --> 23:19.357
IT'S A JOB FOR SOME
VERY, <i>VERY</i> POWERFUL PEOPLE.

23:19.439 --> 23:24.695
PEOPLE WHO I BELIEVE CAN FIX
MY CHARGES PERMANENTLY.

23:24.737 --> 23:26.113
BUT I NEED YOUR HELP.

23:26.155 --> 23:27.865
YOU'RE HERE TO CORRUPT

23:27.907 --> 23:29.491
ONE OF MY BRIGHTEST
AND BEST.

23:29.533 --> 23:31.327
YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M OFFERING.

23:31.369 --> 23:33.079
YOU HAVE TO LET THEM
DECIDE FOR THEMSELVES.

23:33.120 --> 23:34.830
MONEY.
NOT JUST MONEY.

23:34.872 --> 23:36.540
YOU REMEMBER.

23:36.582 --> 23:40.044
IT'S THE CHANCE TO BUILD
CATHEDRALS, ENTIRE CITIES,

23:40.086 --> 23:41.962
THINGS THAT NEVER EXISTED,

23:42.004 --> 23:45.132
THINGS THAT COULDN'T EXIST
IN THE REAL WORLD.

23:45.174 --> 23:48.135
SO, YOU-- YOU WANT ME
TO LET SOMEONE ELSE

23:48.177 --> 23:50.388
FOLLOW YOU
INTO YOUR FANTASY?

23:50.428 --> 23:51.972
THEY DON'T ACTUALLY
COME INTO THE DREAM.

23:52.014 --> 23:53.515
THEY JUST-- THEY JUST
DESIGN THE LEVELS

23:53.557 --> 23:54.808
AND TEACH THEM
TO THE DREAMERS.

23:54.850 --> 23:56.060
THAT'S ALL.

23:56.102 --> 23:57.311
DESIGN IT YOURSELF.

23:59.521 --> 24:01.481
MAL WON'T LET ME.

24:06.779 --> 24:10.657
COME BACK
TO REALITY, DOM.

24:10.699 --> 24:11.742
PLEASE.

24:11.784 --> 24:13.786
"REALITY."

24:13.827 --> 24:16.663
THOSE KIDS,
YOUR GRANDCHILDREN,

24:16.705 --> 24:19.125
THEY'RE WAITING FOR THEIR FATHER
TO COME BACK HOME.

24:19.166 --> 24:20.918
THAT'S <i>THEIR</i> REALITY.

24:20.960 --> 24:24.213
AND THIS JOB, THIS LAST JOB,
<i>THAT'S</i> HOW I GET THERE.

24:24.255 --> 24:28.342
I WOULD NOT BE STANDING HERE
IF I KNEW ANY OTHER WAY.

24:30.594 --> 24:34.432
I NEED AN ARCHITECT
WHO IS AS GOOD AS I WAS.

24:37.851 --> 24:40.146
I'VE GOT SOMEBODY BETTER.

24:40.187 --> 24:41.814
ARIADNE?

24:43.732 --> 24:46.484
I'D LIKE YOU
TO MEET MR. COBB.

24:46.526 --> 24:47.987
PLEASED TO MEET YOU.

24:48.028 --> 24:49.696
IF YOU HAVE
A FEW MOMENTS,

24:49.738 --> 24:52.950
MR. COBB HAS A JOB OFFER
HE'D LIKE TO DISCUSS WITH YOU.

24:52.992 --> 24:54.534
A WORK PLACEMENT?

24:54.576 --> 24:56.162
NOT EXACTLY.

24:56.203 --> 24:57.871
I HAVE A TEST FOR YOU.

24:57.913 --> 25:00.540
YOU'RE NOT GONNA TELL ME
ANYTHING ABOUT THIS FIRST?

25:00.582 --> 25:04.337
BEFORE I DESCRIBE THE JOB,
I HAVE TO KNOW YOU CAN DO IT.
WHY?

25:04.378 --> 25:06.672
IT'S NOT,
STRICTLY SPEAKING, LEGAL.

25:09.716 --> 25:12.136
YOU HAVE TWO MINUTES
TO DESIGN A MAZE

25:12.178 --> 25:14.472
THAT IT TAKES
ONE MINUTE TO SOLVE.

25:15.681 --> 25:16.932
STOP.

25:19.893 --> 25:21.228
AGAIN.

25:22.562 --> 25:24.023
STOP.

25:27.067 --> 25:30.112
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO DO BETTER
THAN THAT.

25:42.166 --> 25:44.168
THAT'S MORE LIKE IT.

26:03.312 --> 26:05.481
THEY SAY
WE ONLY USE A FRACTION

26:05.523 --> 26:07.316
OF OUR BRAIN'S
TRUE POTENTIAL.

26:07.358 --> 26:09.151
NOW, THAT'S
WHEN WE'RE AWAKE.

26:09.193 --> 26:10.568
WHEN WE'RE ASLEEP,

26:10.610 --> 26:11.820
OUR MIND CAN DO
ALMOST ANYTHING.

26:11.862 --> 26:13.613
SUCH AS?

26:13.655 --> 26:15.657
WELL, IMAGINE YOU'RE DESIGNING
A BUILDING, ALL RIGHT?

26:15.699 --> 26:17.659
YOU CONSCIOUSLY CREATE
EACH ASPECT.

26:17.701 --> 26:20.538
BUT SOMETIMES IT FEELS LIKE
IT'S ALMOST CREATING ITSELF,

26:20.578 --> 26:21.914
IF YOU KNOW WHAT I MEAN.

26:21.955 --> 26:23.790
YEAH. YEAH,
LIKE I'M...DISCOVERING IT.

26:23.832 --> 26:26.085
GENUINE INSPIRATION,
RIGHT?
MM-HMM.

26:26.126 --> 26:29.796
NOW, IN A DREAM, OUR MIND
CONTINUOUSLY DOES THIS.

26:29.838 --> 26:35.344
WE CREATE AND PERCEIVE
OUR WORLD SIMULTANEOUSLY.

26:35.386 --> 26:36.762
AND OUR MIND
DOES THIS SO WELL

26:36.803 --> 26:38.638
THAT WE DON'T EVEN KNOW
IT'S HAPPENING.

26:38.680 --> 26:40.891
THAT ALLOWS US TO GET RIGHT
IN THE MIDDLE OF THAT PROCESS.

26:40.933 --> 26:42.142
HOW?

26:42.184 --> 26:43.810
BY TAKING OVER
THE CREATING PART.

26:43.852 --> 26:45.354
NOW, THIS IS
WHERE I NEED YOU.

26:45.396 --> 26:47.689
YOU CREATE THE WORLD
OF THE DREAM.

26:47.731 --> 26:50.067
WE BRING THE SUBJECT
INTO THAT DREAM,

26:50.109 --> 26:53.446
AND THEY FILL IT
WITH THEIR SUBCONSCIOUS.

26:53.487 --> 26:56.198
HOW COULD I EVER
ACQUIRE ENOUGH DETAIL

26:56.240 --> 26:58.867
TO MAKE THEM THINK
THAT IT'S REALITY?

26:58.909 --> 27:01.828
WELL, DREAMS, THEY FEEL REAL
WHILE WE'RE IN THEM, RIGHT?

27:01.870 --> 27:03.497
IT'S ONLY WHEN WE WAKE UP

27:03.539 --> 27:05.791
THAT WE REALIZE SOMETHING
WAS ACTUALLY STRANGE.

27:05.832 --> 27:07.751
LET ME ASK YOU
A QUESTION.

27:07.793 --> 27:10.379
YOU-- YOU NEVER
REALLY REMEMBER

27:10.421 --> 27:12.256
THE BEGINNING OF A DREAM,
DO YOU?

27:12.298 --> 27:15.092
YOU ALWAYS WIND UP RIGHT IN
THE MIDDLE OF WHAT'S GOING ON.

27:15.134 --> 27:16.634
I GUESS, YEAH.

27:16.676 --> 27:18.345
SO, HOW DID WE
END UP HERE?

27:18.387 --> 27:21.515
WELL, WE JUST CAME
FROM THE...

27:21.557 --> 27:24.477
THINK ABOUT IT, ARIADNE.
HOW DID YOU GET <i>HERE?</i>

27:24.518 --> 27:26.312
WHERE ARE YOU RIGHT NOW?

27:29.731 --> 27:31.442
WE'RE DREAMING?

27:31.484 --> 27:32.859
YOU'RE ACTUALLY
IN THE MIDDLE

27:32.901 --> 27:34.487
OF THE WORKSHOP RIGHT NOW,
SLEEPING.

27:34.528 --> 27:36.405
THIS IS YOUR FIRST LESSON
IN SHARED DREAMING.

27:36.447 --> 27:38.574
STAY CALM.

28:14.401 --> 28:16.362
IF IT'S JUST A DREAM,
THEN WHY ARE YOU PROTEC--

28:17.695 --> 28:20.032
BECAUSE IT'S NEVER
<i>JUST</i> A DREAM, IS IT?

28:20.073 --> 28:21.408
AND A FACE FULL OF GLASS
HURTS LIKE HELL.

28:21.450 --> 28:23.827
WHEN YOU'RE IN IT,
IT FEELS REAL.

28:23.869 --> 28:25.663
THAT'S WHY THE MILITARY
DEVELOPED DREAM SHARING.

28:25.703 --> 28:27.373
IT WAS A TRAINING
PROGRAM FOR SOLDIERS

28:27.414 --> 28:29.542
TO SHOOT AND STAB
AND STRANGLE EACH OTHER

28:29.583 --> 28:30.584
AND THEN WAKE UP.

28:30.626 --> 28:33.128
HOW DID ARCHITECTS
BECOME INVOLVED?

28:33.170 --> 28:36.423
WELL, SOMEONE HAD TO DESIGN
THE DREAMS, RIGHT?

28:36.465 --> 28:39.552
WHY DON'T YOU GIVE US
ANOTHER FIVE MINUTES?

28:39.593 --> 28:41.136
FIVE MINUTES?!

28:41.178 --> 28:44.473
WHAT-- WE WERE TALKING
FOR LIKE AT LEAST AN HOUR.

28:44.515 --> 28:46.642
IN A DREAM, YOUR MIND
FUNCTIONS MORE QUICKLY.

28:46.684 --> 28:50.103
THEREFORE, TIME SEEMS
TO FEEL MORE SLOW.

28:50.145 --> 28:51.271
FIVE MINUTES IN
THE REAL WORLD

28:51.313 --> 28:53.899
GIVES YOU AN HOUR
IN THE DREAM.

28:53.940 --> 28:57.194
WHY DON'T YOU SEE
WHAT YOU CAN GET UP TO
IN FIVE MINUTES?

29:02.700 --> 29:04.493
YOU'VE GOT
THE BASIC LAYOUT.

29:04.535 --> 29:06.078
THE BOOKSTORE, THE CAFÉ.

29:06.119 --> 29:07.787
ALMOST EVERYTHING ELSE
IS HERE, TOO.

29:07.829 --> 29:09.039
WHO ARE THE PEOPLE?

29:09.081 --> 29:10.957
PROJECTIONS
OF MY SUBCONSCIOUS.

29:10.999 --> 29:13.001
YOURS?
YES.

29:13.043 --> 29:15.212
REMEMBER, YOU ARE THE DREAMER.
YOU BUILD THIS WORLD.

29:15.254 --> 29:17.673
I AM THE SUBJECT.
MY MIND POPULATES IT.

29:17.715 --> 29:19.883
YOU CAN LITERALLY TALK
TO MY SUBCONSCIOUS.

29:19.925 --> 29:21.801
THAT'S ONE OF THE WAYS
WE EXTRACT INFORMATION

29:21.843 --> 29:23.053
FROM THE SUBJECT.

29:23.095 --> 29:24.304
HOW ELSE DO YOU DO IT?

29:24.346 --> 29:26.139
BY CREATING
SOMETHING SECURE

29:26.181 --> 29:28.726
LIKE A-- LIKE A BANK VAULT
OR A JAIL.

29:28.767 --> 29:30.977
THE MIND AUTOMATICALLY
FILLS IT WITH INFORMATION

29:31.019 --> 29:32.396
IT'S TRYING TO PROTECT.

29:32.438 --> 29:33.647
YOU UNDERSTAND?

29:33.689 --> 29:35.232
THEN YOU BREAK IN
AND STEAL IT.

29:35.274 --> 29:36.692
WELL...

29:36.734 --> 29:39.194
I GUESS I THOUGHT
THAT THE DREAM SPACE

29:39.236 --> 29:41.321
WOULD BE ALL
ABOUT THE VISUAL,

29:41.363 --> 29:43.657
BUT IT'S MORE
ABOUT THE FEEL OF IT.

29:43.699 --> 29:44.950
MY QUESTION IS,

29:44.991 --> 29:46.285
WHAT HAPPENS
WHEN YOU START MESSING

29:46.326 --> 29:49.121
WITH THE PHYSICS
OF IT ALL?

30:29.453 --> 30:30.870
IT'S SOMETHING,
ISN'T IT?

30:31.747 --> 30:33.290
YES, IT IS.

30:56.647 --> 30:58.732
WHY ARE THEY
ALL LOOKING AT ME?

30:58.774 --> 31:00.317
BECAUSE MY
SUBCONSCIOUS FEELS

31:00.359 --> 31:02.402
THAT SOMEONE ELSE
IS CREATING THIS WORLD.

31:02.444 --> 31:04.029
THE MORE
YOU CHANGE THINGS,

31:04.070 --> 31:06.490
THE QUICKER THE PROJECTIONS
START TO CONVERGE ON YOU.

31:06.532 --> 31:08.033
"CONVERGE"?

31:08.074 --> 31:10.410
THEY SENSE THE FOREIGN NATURE
OF THE DREAMER.

31:10.452 --> 31:13.372
THEY ATTACK LIKE WHITE BLOOD
CELLS FIGHTING AN INFECTION.

31:13.413 --> 31:14.707
LIKE THEY'RE GONNA
ATTACK US?

31:14.748 --> 31:15.957
NO, NO.

31:15.999 --> 31:18.293
JUST YOU.

31:22.005 --> 31:23.799
THIS IS GREAT,
BUT I'M TELLING YOU,

31:23.841 --> 31:25.592
IF YOU KEEP CHANGING THINGS
LIKE THIS...

31:29.262 --> 31:30.806
GEEZ.

31:30.848 --> 31:33.183
MIND TELLING YOUR SUBCONSCIOUS
TO TAKE IT EASY?

31:33.225 --> 31:35.769
IT'S MY SUBCONSCIOUS.
REMEMBER? I CAN'T CONTROL IT.

32:29.030 --> 32:30.783
VERY IMPRESSIVE.

32:41.668 --> 32:46.131
I KNOW THIS BRIDGE.
THIS PLACE IS REAL, ISN'T IT?

32:46.172 --> 32:48.634
YEAH, I CROSS IT EVERY DAY
TO GET TO THE COLLEGE.

32:48.675 --> 32:50.469
NEVER RE-CREATE PLACES
FROM YOUR MEMORY.

32:50.510 --> 32:52.220
ALWAYS IMAGINE
NEW PLACES.

32:52.262 --> 32:54.222
WELL, YOU GOTTA DRAW FROM
STUFF YOU KNOW, RIGHT?

32:54.264 --> 32:57.350
ONLY USE DETAILS--
A-A STREETLAMP OR A PHONE BOOTH.

32:57.392 --> 32:58.602
NEVER ENTIRE AREAS.

32:58.644 --> 33:00.103
WHY NOT?

33:00.145 --> 33:01.688
'CAUSE BUILDING A DREAM
FROM YOUR MEMORY

33:01.730 --> 33:03.148
IS THE EASIEST WAY
TO LOSE YOUR GRASP

33:03.189 --> 33:04.524
ON WHAT'S REAL
AND WHAT IS A DREAM.

33:04.566 --> 33:05.776
IS THAT WHAT HAPPENED
TO YOU?

33:05.818 --> 33:07.360
HEY, LISTEN TO ME.

33:07.402 --> 33:08.987
THIS HAS NOTHING TO DO WITH ME,
YOU UNDERSTAND?

33:09.028 --> 33:11.114
IS THAT WHY YOU NEED ME
TO BUILD YOUR DREAMS?

33:11.156 --> 33:13.158
HEY, GET OFF OF HER.
BACK UP. BACK UP!

33:13.199 --> 33:14.576
COBB! COBB!

33:14.618 --> 33:16.244
GET OFF OF HER!
COBB! LET ME GO!

33:16.286 --> 33:17.704
MAL!
LET ME GO!

33:17.746 --> 33:18.831
MAL!

33:18.872 --> 33:20.332
WAKE ME UP!
MAL!

33:20.373 --> 33:22.292
WAKE ME UP!
MAL, NO! NO!

33:22.334 --> 33:23.961
WAKE ME UP!

33:25.545 --> 33:27.547
HEY. HEY.
HEY. LOOK AT ME.

33:27.589 --> 33:29.299
YOU'RE OKAY.

33:29.341 --> 33:30.968
WHY--

33:31.009 --> 33:32.761
WHY WOULDN'T I WAKE UP?

33:32.803 --> 33:34.805
'CAUSE THERE WAS STILL
SOME TIME ON THE CLOCK,

33:34.847 --> 33:37.557
AND YOU CAN'T WAKE UP FROM
WITHIN THE DREAM UNLESS YOU DIE.

33:37.599 --> 33:38.642
SHE'LL NEED A TOTEM.

33:38.684 --> 33:39.601
WHAT?!

33:39.643 --> 33:41.436
A TOTEM,
IT'S A SMALL PERSONAL...

33:41.478 --> 33:43.689
THAT'S SOME SUBCONSCIOUS
YOU'VE GOT ON YOU, COBB!

33:43.730 --> 33:45.315
SHE'S A REAL CHARMER!

33:45.357 --> 33:47.025
OH. I SEE
YOU MET <i>MRS.</i> COBB.

33:47.066 --> 33:48.568
SHE'S HIS WIFE?

33:48.610 --> 33:49.611
YEAH.

33:49.653 --> 33:50.737
SO, A TOTEM.

33:50.779 --> 33:51.989
YOU NEED A SMALL OBJECT,
POTENTIALLY HEAVY,

33:52.030 --> 33:54.199
SOMETHING YOU CAN HAVE
ON YOU ALL THE TIME

33:54.240 --> 33:55.826
THAT NO ONE ELSE KNOWS.
WHAT, LIKE A COIN?

33:55.868 --> 33:57.828
NO. IT NEEDS TO BE
MORE UNIQUE THAN THAT.

33:57.870 --> 34:01.247
LIKE, THIS IS A...
LOADED DIE.

34:02.624 --> 34:03.917
I CAN'T LET YOU TOUCH IT.

34:03.959 --> 34:05.669
THAT WOULD DEFEAT
THE PURPOSE.

34:05.711 --> 34:07.420
SEE, ONLY I KNOW THE BALANCE
AND THE WEIGHT

34:07.462 --> 34:09.631
OF THIS PARTICULAR
LOADED DIE.

34:09.673 --> 34:11.633
THAT WAY,
WHEN YOU LOOK AT <i>YOUR</i> TOTEM,

34:11.675 --> 34:12.759
YOU KNOW BEYOND A DOUBT

34:12.801 --> 34:14.511
THAT YOU'RE NOT
IN SOMEONE ELSE'S DREAM.

34:18.223 --> 34:20.851
I-I DON'T KNOW IF YOU CAN'T
SEE WHAT'S GOING ON,

34:20.893 --> 34:22.644
OR IF YOU JUST
DON'T WANT TO,

34:22.686 --> 34:24.730
BUT COBB HAS SOME
SERIOUS PROBLEMS

34:24.771 --> 34:26.231
THAT HE'S TRIED
TO BURY DOWN THERE.

34:26.272 --> 34:28.901
AND I'M NOT ABOUT
TO JUST OPEN MY MIND

34:28.942 --> 34:30.402
TO SOMEONE LIKE THAT.

34:35.198 --> 34:37.617
SHE'LL BE BACK.

34:37.659 --> 34:39.995
I'VE NEVER SEEN ANYONE PICK
IT UP THAT QUICKLY BEFORE.

34:40.037 --> 34:42.455
REALITY'S NOT GONNA BE ENOUGH
FOR HER NOW,

34:42.497 --> 34:44.624
AND WHEN SHE COMES BACK

34:44.666 --> 34:46.001
WHEN SHE COMES BACK,

34:46.043 --> 34:48.003
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
HER BUILDING MAZES.

34:48.045 --> 34:49.462
WHERE ARE <i>YOU</i> GONNA BE?

34:49.504 --> 34:51.172
I GOTTA GO VISIT EAMES.

34:51.214 --> 34:53.759
EAMES? NO, HE'S IN MOMBASA.
IT'S COBOL'S BACKYARD.

34:53.800 --> 34:55.510
IT'S A NECESSARY RISK.

34:55.552 --> 34:57.220
WELL, THERE'S PLENTY
OF GOOD THIEVES.

34:57.262 --> 34:59.932
WE DON'T JUST NEED A THIEF.

34:59.973 --> 35:01.266
WE NEED A FORGER.

35:09.399 --> 35:11.484
YOU CAN RUB THEM TOGETHER
ALL YOU WANT,

35:11.526 --> 35:12.611
THEY'RE NOT GONNA BREED.

35:12.652 --> 35:14.153
YOU NEVER KNOW.

35:15.447 --> 35:18.075
LET ME GET YOU A DRINK.

35:18.116 --> 35:20.660
YOU'RE BUYING.

35:26.541 --> 35:27.960
YOUR SPELLING
HASN'T IMPROVED.

35:28.001 --> 35:29.294
PISS OFF.

35:29.335 --> 35:30.796
HOW'S YOUR HANDWRITING?

35:30.837 --> 35:32.297
IT'S VERSATILE.

35:32.338 --> 35:33.590
GOOD.

35:33.632 --> 35:35.008
THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

35:35.050 --> 35:36.509
INCEPTION.

35:36.551 --> 35:37.886
NOW, BEFORE YOU BOTHER

35:37.928 --> 35:40.097
TELLING ME IT'S IMPOSSIBLE,
LET ME--

35:40.138 --> 35:42.975
NO, IT'S PERFECTLY POSSIBLE.
IT'S JUST BLOODY DIFFICULT.

35:43.016 --> 35:44.935
INTERESTING.

35:44.977 --> 35:47.020
'CAUSE ARTHUR KEEPS TELLING ME
IT CAN'T BE DONE.

35:47.062 --> 35:48.981
HMM. ARTHUR.

35:49.022 --> 35:50.356
YOU STILL WORKING
WITH THAT STICK IN THE MUD?

35:50.398 --> 35:51.817
WELL, HE IS GOOD
AT WHAT HE DOES, RIGHT?

35:51.858 --> 35:53.318
OH, HE'S THE BEST.

35:53.359 --> 35:54.778
HE HAS NO IMAGINATION.

35:54.820 --> 35:55.988
NOT LIKE YOU.

35:56.029 --> 35:57.656
LISTEN, IF YOU'RE GONNA
PERFORM INCEPTION,

35:57.697 --> 35:59.240
YOU <i>NEED</i> IMAGINATION.

35:59.282 --> 36:01.159
LET ME ASK YOU SOMETHING.

36:01.200 --> 36:03.036
HAVE YOU DONE IT BEFORE?

36:03.078 --> 36:04.663
WE TRIED IT.

36:04.704 --> 36:06.414
WE GOT THE IDEA IN PLACE,
BUT IT DIDN'T TAKE.

36:06.456 --> 36:08.083
YOU DIDN'T PLANT IT
DEEP ENOUGH?

36:08.125 --> 36:09.584
NO, IT'S NOT
JUST ABOUT DEPTH.

36:09.626 --> 36:11.670
YOU NEED THE SIMPLEST
VERSION OF THE IDEA

36:11.711 --> 36:13.005
IN ORDER FOR IT
TO GROW NATURALLY

36:13.046 --> 36:14.255
IN YOUR SUBJECT'S MIND.

36:14.297 --> 36:15.924
IT'S A VERY SUBTLE ART.

36:15.966 --> 36:18.718
SO, WHAT IS THIS IDEA
THAT YOU NEED TO PLANT?

36:18.760 --> 36:21.054
WE NEED THE HEIR
OF A MAJOR CORPORATION

36:21.096 --> 36:23.015
TO DISSOLVE
HIS FATHER'S EMPIRE.

36:23.056 --> 36:24.474
WELL, YOU SEE,
RIGHT THERE,

36:24.516 --> 36:26.018
YOU HAVE VARIOUS
POLITICAL MOTIVATIONS

36:26.059 --> 36:27.144
AND ANTI-MONOPOLISTIC
SENTIMENTS AND SO FORTH.

36:27.185 --> 36:29.270
BUT ALL OF
THAT STUFF IS...

36:29.312 --> 36:32.649
IT'S REALLY AT THE MERCY OF
YOUR SUBJECT'S PREJUDICE,
YOU SEE?

36:32.691 --> 36:34.860
AND WHAT YOU HAVE
TO DO IS START AT
THE ABSOLUTE BASIC.

36:34.901 --> 36:36.444
WHICH IS WHAT?

36:36.486 --> 36:39.572
THE RELATIONSHIP
WITH THE FATHER.

36:41.324 --> 36:43.952
DO YOU HAVE A CHEMIST?
NO, NOT YET.

36:43.994 --> 36:46.830
RIGHT. OKAY, WELL,
THERE'S A MAN HERE. YUSUF.

36:46.872 --> 36:50.333
HE, UH, HE FORMULATES HIS
OWN VERSIONS OF THE COMPOUNDS.

36:50.375 --> 36:52.210
WHY DON'T YOU
TAKE ME THERE?

36:52.251 --> 36:55.047
ONCE YOU'VE LOST YOUR TAIL.
THE MAN AT THE BAR.

36:55.088 --> 36:56.673
COBOL ENGINEERING.

36:56.715 --> 36:59.176
THAT PRICE ON MY HEAD--
WAS THAT DEAD OR ALIVE?

36:59.217 --> 37:01.469
DON'T REMEMBER. LET'S SEE
IF HE STARTS SHOOTING.

37:01.511 --> 37:03.180
RUN INTERFERENCE.

37:03.221 --> 37:05.223
I'LL MEET YOU DOWNSTAIRS IN
THE BAR IN, SAY, HALF AN HOUR?

37:05.264 --> 37:07.851
THEN BACK HERE?
THIS IS THE LAST PLACE
THEY'D SUSPECT.

37:07.893 --> 37:09.602
MM.

37:09.644 --> 37:11.730
ALL RIGHT.

37:11.771 --> 37:14.733
FREDDY! FREDDY SIMMONDS.

37:14.774 --> 37:16.317
MY GOD, IT'S YOU,
ISN'T IT?

37:17.736 --> 37:19.278
WHO?

37:19.320 --> 37:21.614
NO, IT <i>ISN'T</i> YOU.

37:21.656 --> 37:23.158
YOU'RE NOT DREAMING NOW,
ARE YOU?

37:37.839 --> 37:39.716
OHH!

37:41.760 --> 37:42.969
THERE!

38:02.072 --> 38:04.241
CAFÉ. ONE CAFÉ.

38:08.620 --> 38:09.996
Shh!

38:15.668 --> 38:18.755
ONE CAFÉ.

38:18.797 --> 38:20.381
CAFÉ.

38:41.069 --> 38:42.487
OHH!

39:15.061 --> 39:16.437
CARE FOR A LIFT, MR. COBB?

39:16.479 --> 39:19.524
WHAT ARE YOU DOING
IN MOMBASA?!

39:19.565 --> 39:22.152
I'M HERE TO PROTECT
MY INVESTMENT.

39:24.487 --> 39:27.573
AH, SO THIS IS YOUR IDEA
OF <i>LOSING</i> A TAIL, HUH?

39:27.615 --> 39:28.741
DIFFERENT TAIL.

39:36.582 --> 39:39.294
COBB SAID YOU'D BE BACK.

39:39.336 --> 39:41.880
YEAH, WELL,
I TRIED NOT TO COME, BUT...

39:41.921 --> 39:43.506
BUT THERE'S NOTHING
QUITE LIKE IT.

39:43.548 --> 39:44.799
IT'S JUST...

39:46.676 --> 39:49.470
...PURE CREATION.

39:49.512 --> 39:51.764
SHALL WE TAKE A LOOK AT SOME
PARADOXICAL ARCHITECTURE?

39:51.806 --> 39:53.308
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE TO MASTER
A FEW TRICKS

39:53.350 --> 39:54.851
IF YOU'RE GONNA BUILD
THREE COMPLETE DREAM LEVELS.

39:54.893 --> 39:56.644
EXCUSE ME.

39:56.686 --> 39:59.356
WHAT KIND OF TRICKS?

39:59.397 --> 40:01.066
IN A DREAM,
YOU CAN CHEAT ARCHITECTURE

40:01.107 --> 40:02.400
INTO IMPOSSIBLE SHAPES.

40:02.441 --> 40:04.443
THAT LETS YOU CREATE
CLOSED LOOPS,

40:04.485 --> 40:07.155
LIKE THE PENROSE STEPS.

40:07.197 --> 40:08.740
THE INFINITE STAIRCASE.

40:11.368 --> 40:13.161
SEE?

40:17.498 --> 40:18.750
PARADOX.

40:18.791 --> 40:20.501
SO, A CLOSED LOOP
LIKE THAT

40:20.543 --> 40:22.754
WILL HELP YOU DISGUISE
THE BOUNDARIES

40:22.795 --> 40:24.172
OF THE DREAM YOU CREATE.

40:24.214 --> 40:25.882
BUT HOW BIG DO THESE LEVELS
HAVE TO BE?

40:25.924 --> 40:28.176
WELL, IT COULD BE ANYTHING
FROM THE FLOOR OF A BUILDING

40:28.218 --> 40:29.635
TO AN ENTIRE CITY.

40:29.677 --> 40:31.096
BUT THEY HAVE TO BE
COMPLICATED ENOUGH

40:31.137 --> 40:32.513
THAT WE CAN HIDE
FROM THE PROJECTIONS.

40:32.555 --> 40:33.848
A MAZE.
RIGHT, A MAZE.

40:33.890 --> 40:35.516
AND THE BETTER
THE MAZE...

40:35.558 --> 40:38.228
THEN THE LONGER WE HAVE
BEFORE THE PROJECTIONS CATCH US?

40:38.270 --> 40:39.396
EXACTLY.

40:40.730 --> 40:42.148
MY SUBCONSCIOUS SEEMS POLITE
ENOUGH.

40:42.190 --> 40:43.608
YOU WAIT.
THEY'LL TURN UGLY.

40:43.649 --> 40:45.402
NO ONE LIKES TO FEEL
SOMEONE ELSE

40:45.443 --> 40:46.736
MESSING AROUND
IN THEIR MIND.

40:46.778 --> 40:49.072
COBB CAN'T BUILD ANYMORE,
CAN HE?

40:51.574 --> 40:53.326
WELL, I DON'T KNOW
IF HE <i>CAN'T,</i> BUT HE <i>WON'T.</i>

40:53.368 --> 40:55.828
HE THINKS IT'S SAFER
IF HE DOESN'T KNOW THE LAYOUTS.

40:55.870 --> 40:57.622
WHY?
HE WON'T TELL ME.

40:57.663 --> 40:59.582
BUT I THINK IT'S MAL.

40:59.624 --> 41:01.000
HIS EX-WIFE?

41:01.042 --> 41:02.252
NO, NOT HIS EX.

41:02.294 --> 41:03.711
THEY'RE STILL TOGETHER?

41:03.753 --> 41:06.505
NO...

41:06.547 --> 41:07.840
SHE'S DEAD.

41:10.176 --> 41:12.345
WHAT YOU SEE IN THERE
IS JUST HIS PROJECTION OF HER.

41:15.640 --> 41:18.017
WHAT WAS SHE LIKE
IN REAL LIFE?

41:18.059 --> 41:20.186
SHE WAS LOVELY.

41:23.231 --> 41:26.318
YOU ARE SEEKING A CHEMIST?
YES.

41:26.359 --> 41:28.611
TO FORMULATE COMPOUNDS
FOR A JOB?

41:28.653 --> 41:31.156
AND TO GO INTO THE FIELD
WITH US.

41:31.197 --> 41:33.950
NO, I RARELY GO INTO THE FIELD,
MR. COBB.

41:33.992 --> 41:35.410
WELL, WE'D NEED YOU THERE

41:35.452 --> 41:37.454
TO TAILOR COMPOUNDS
SPECIFIC TO OUR NEEDS.

41:37.495 --> 41:39.705
WHICH ARE?
GREAT DEPTH.

41:39.747 --> 41:43.126
A DREAM WITHIN A DREAM.
TWO LEVELS.

41:45.086 --> 41:46.963
THREE.

41:47.005 --> 41:48.506
NOT POSSIBLE.

41:48.547 --> 41:50.300
THAT MANY DREAMS WITHIN DREAMS
IS TOO UNSTABLE.

41:50.342 --> 41:52.427
IT <i>IS</i> POSSIBLE.

41:52.469 --> 41:54.846
YOU JUST HAVE TO ADD
A SEDATIVE.

41:54.887 --> 41:57.640
A <i>POWERFUL</i> SEDATIVE.

41:58.683 --> 42:00.768
HOW MANY TEAM MEMBERS?

42:00.810 --> 42:02.561
FIVE.
SIX.

42:02.603 --> 42:06.858
THE ONLY WAY TO KNOW
YOU'VE DONE THE JOB

42:06.899 --> 42:09.319
IS IF I GO IN WITH YOU.

42:09.361 --> 42:11.779
THERE'S NO ROOM FOR TOURISTS
ON A JOB LIKE THIS, MR. SAITO.

42:11.821 --> 42:14.324
THIS TIME, IT SEEMS THERE IS.

42:14.366 --> 42:17.452
THIS, I THINK, IS
A GOOD PLACE TO START.

42:17.494 --> 42:18.953
I USE IT EVERY DAY.

42:18.995 --> 42:20.288
WHAT FOR?

42:20.330 --> 42:23.082
HERE, I'LL SHOW YOU.

42:24.750 --> 42:27.295
PERHAPS YOU WILL NOT
WANT TO SEE.

42:29.714 --> 42:31.007
AFTER YOU.

42:39.640 --> 42:42.643
10...12.

42:42.685 --> 42:44.270
ALL CONNECTED.
BLOODY HELL.

42:44.312 --> 42:46.064
THEY COME EVERY DAY
TO SHARE THE DREAM.

42:49.025 --> 42:51.694
YOU SEE?
<i>VERY</i> STABLE.

42:56.699 --> 42:58.784
HOW LONG
DO THEY DREAM FOR?

42:58.826 --> 43:00.953
THREE, FOUR HOURS,
EACH DAY.

43:00.995 --> 43:02.788
AND DREAM TIME?

43:02.830 --> 43:04.707
WITH THIS COMPOUND?

43:04.749 --> 43:06.625
ABOUT 40 HOURS,
EACH AND EVERY DAY.

43:06.667 --> 43:08.836
WHY DO THEY DO IT?

43:08.878 --> 43:10.755
TELL HIM, MR. COBB.

43:10.796 --> 43:14.092
AFTER A WHILE, IT BECOMES
THE ONLY WAY YOU <i>CAN</i> DREAM.

43:14.133 --> 43:16.177
DO <i>YOU</i> STILL DREAM,
MR. COBB?

43:16.219 --> 43:18.637
THEY COME HERE EVERY DAY
TO SLEEP?

43:18.679 --> 43:20.890
Elderly man: NO.

43:20.932 --> 43:24.643
THEY COME TO BE WOKEN UP.

43:24.685 --> 43:28.898
THE DREAM HAS BECOME
THEIR REALITY.

43:28.940 --> 43:32.277
WHO ARE YOU
TO SAY OTHERWISE, SIR?

43:34.404 --> 43:36.155
LET'S SEE
WHAT YOU CAN DO.

43:47.041 --> 43:49.835
YOU KNOW HOW
TO FIND ME.

43:51.254 --> 43:53.381
YOU KNOW
WHAT YOU HAVE TO DO.

43:57.718 --> 43:59.678
SHARP, NO?

44:15.069 --> 44:17.905
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT,
MR. COBB?

44:17.947 --> 44:20.366
YEAH. YEAH.

44:20.408 --> 44:22.368
EVERYTHING'S JUST FINE.

44:30.042 --> 44:31.710
ROBERT FISCHER,

44:31.752 --> 44:34.547
HEIR TO THE FISCHER MORROW
ENERGY CONGLOMERATE.

44:34.589 --> 44:36.633
WHAT'S YOUR PROBLEM
WITH THIS MR. FISCHER?

44:36.674 --> 44:38.384
THAT'S NOT YOUR CONCERN.

44:38.426 --> 44:40.219
MR. SAITO, THIS

44:40.261 --> 44:43.181
THIS ISN'T YOUR TYPICAL
CORPORATE ESPIONAGE.

44:43.222 --> 44:45.057
YOU ASKED ME
FOR INCEPTION.

44:45.099 --> 44:48.269
I DO HOPE YOU UNDERSTAND
THE GRAVITY OF THAT REQUEST.

44:48.311 --> 44:51.230
NOW, THE SEED THAT WE PLANT
IN THIS MAN'S MIND

44:51.272 --> 44:52.649
WILL GROW INTO AN IDEA.

44:52.689 --> 44:54.651
THIS IDEA WILL DEFINE HIM.

44:54.691 --> 44:56.528
IT MAY COME TO CHANGE...

44:56.569 --> 44:59.113
WELL, IT MAY COME TO CHANGE
EVERYTHING ABOUT HIM.

44:59.155 --> 45:00.865
WE'RE THE LAST COMPANY
STANDING

45:00.906 --> 45:03.618
BETWEEN THEM
AND TOTAL ENERGY DOMINANCE.

45:03.660 --> 45:06.496
AND WE CAN
NO LONGER COMPETE.

45:06.538 --> 45:09.499
SOON, THEY'LL CONTROL THE ENERGY
SUPPLY OF HALF THE WORLD.

45:09.541 --> 45:11.417
IN EFFECT,
THEY BECOME A NEW SUPERPOWER.

45:13.294 --> 45:16.381
THE WORLD NEEDS ROBERT FISCHER
TO CHANGE HIS MIND.

45:16.422 --> 45:18.508
THAT'S WHERE WE COME IN.

45:18.550 --> 45:21.927
HOW IS ROBERT FISCHER'S
RELATIONSHIP WITH HIS FATHER?

45:21.969 --> 45:24.847
RUMOR IS THE RELATIONSHIP
IS QUITE COMPLICATED.

45:24.889 --> 45:27.517
WELL, WE CAN'T WORK BASED
SOLELY ON RUMOR, CAN WE?

45:27.559 --> 45:29.602
CAN YOU GET ME ACCESS
TO THIS MAN HERE?

45:29.644 --> 45:30.978
BROWNING.

45:31.020 --> 45:33.481
FISCHER SENIOR'S
RIGHT-HAND MAN...

45:33.523 --> 45:35.233
FISCHER JUNIOR'S GODFATHER.

45:35.274 --> 45:36.568
IT SHOULD BE POSSIBLE,

45:36.609 --> 45:38.653
IF YOU CAN GET
THE RIGHT REFERENCES.

45:38.695 --> 45:43.282
REFERENCES ARE SOMETHING OF
A SPECIALTY FOR ME, MR. SAITO.

45:43.324 --> 45:46.077
I'M NOT SMELLING
SETTLEMENT HERE.

45:46.118 --> 45:47.704
TAKE THEM DOWN.

45:47.744 --> 45:49.746
MR. BROWNING,
MAURICE FISCHER'S POLICY

45:49.788 --> 45:51.748
IS ALWAYS ONE
OF AVOIDING LITIGATION.

45:54.252 --> 45:56.879
WELL, SHALL WE VOICE
YOUR CONCERNS

45:56.921 --> 45:59.131
WITH MAURICE DIRECTLY?

45:59.173 --> 46:00.757
I'M NOT SURE
THAT'S NECESSARY.

46:00.799 --> 46:03.261
NO, NO, NO.
I-I THINK WE SHOULD.

46:24.198 --> 46:26.659
HOW IS HE?

46:26.701 --> 46:30.037
I DON'T WANT TO BOTHER HIM
UNNECESSARILY, BUT--

46:30.079 --> 46:33.374
ROBERT, I TOLD YOU
KEEP OUT THE DAMN...

46:34.125 --> 46:36.961
WAIT, SO DO IT! GET--

46:37.002 --> 46:38.713
Shh.
PUT IT THROUGH!

46:38.755 --> 46:40.797
NEVER! NEVER.

46:40.839 --> 46:43.008
HAVEN'T YOU,
THE SAME AS I ASKED.

46:43.050 --> 46:45.637
LEAVE THAT.

46:53.645 --> 46:55.730
MUST BE A CHERISHED
MEMORY OF HIS.

46:55.772 --> 46:59.066
<i>I</i> PUT IT BESIDE HIS BED.

46:59.108 --> 47:01.360
HE HASN'T EVEN NOTICED.

47:01.402 --> 47:03.112
ROBERT...

47:04.905 --> 47:07.992
...WE <i>NEED</i> TO TALK
ABOUT A POWER OF ATTORNEY.

47:08.033 --> 47:09.826
I KNOW THIS IS
HARD ON YOU--
NOT NOW, UNCLE PETER.

47:09.868 --> 47:12.121
BUT IT'S IMPERATIVE
THAT WE START TO...

47:15.416 --> 47:16.751
THE VULTURES ARE CIRCLING.

47:16.793 --> 47:19.253
AND THE SICKER
MAURICE FISCHER BECOMES,

47:19.295 --> 47:21.838
THE MORE POWERFUL
PETER BROWNING BECOMES.

47:21.880 --> 47:24.383
I'VE HAD AMPLE OPPORTUNITY
TO OBSERVE BROWNING,

47:24.425 --> 47:27.762
ADOPT HIS PHYSICAL PRESENCE,
STUDY HIS MANNERISMS,

47:27.804 --> 47:29.388
AND SO ON AND SO FORTH.

47:29.430 --> 47:31.349
SO NOW IN THE FIRST LAYER
OF THE DREAM,

47:31.390 --> 47:33.058
I CAN IMPERSONATE BROWNING

47:33.100 --> 47:36.853
AND SUGGEST CONCEPTS
TO FISCHER'S CONSCIOUS MIND.

47:36.895 --> 47:38.731
THEN, WHEN WE TAKE HIM
A LEVEL DEEPER,

47:38.773 --> 47:40.692
HIS OWN PROJECTION
OF BROWNING SHOULD--

47:40.733 --> 47:42.527
<i>SHOULD</i> FEED THAT
RIGHT BACK TO HIM.

47:42.568 --> 47:44.612
SO HE GIVES <i>HIMSELF</i>
THE IDEA.

47:44.654 --> 47:46.197
PRECISELY.

47:46.238 --> 47:47.699
THAT'S THE ONLY WAY
IT WILL STICK.

47:47.740 --> 47:49.033
IT HAS TO SEEM
SELF-GENERATED.

47:49.074 --> 47:50.660
EAMES...

47:50.702 --> 47:52.578
I AM IMPRESSED.

47:52.620 --> 47:54.997
YOUR CONDESCENSION, AS ALWAYS,
IS MUCH APPRECIATED,

47:55.039 --> 47:56.290
ARTHUR, THANK YOU.

48:16.769 --> 48:19.689
WERE YOU GOING UNDER
ON YOUR OWN?

48:19.731 --> 48:21.023
NO, NO, I WAS JUST--

48:21.065 --> 48:23.317
I WAS JUST RUNNING
SOME EXPERIMENTS.

48:23.359 --> 48:25.486
I DIDN'T REALIZE
ANYONE WAS HERE.

48:25.528 --> 48:28.322
YEAH, I WAS JUST-- I WAS
WORKING ON MY TOTEM, ACTUALLY.

48:28.364 --> 48:29.657
HERE.
LET ME TAKE A LOOK.

48:29.699 --> 48:31.158
AH--

48:31.200 --> 48:33.118
SO YOU'RE LEARNING, HUH?

48:33.160 --> 48:36.706
AN ELEGANT SOLUTION
FOR KEEPING TRACK OF REALITY.

48:36.748 --> 48:38.499
WAS IT YOUR IDEA?

48:38.541 --> 48:40.959
NO, IT WAS...
IT WAS MAL'S, ACTUALLY.

48:41.001 --> 48:42.670
THIS...

48:42.712 --> 48:44.004
THIS ONE WAS HERS.

48:44.046 --> 48:45.339
SHE'D SPIN IT
IN THE DREAM,

48:45.381 --> 48:46.758
AND IT WOULD
NEVER TOPPLE.

48:46.799 --> 48:48.008
JUST...

48:48.050 --> 48:49.719
SPIN AND SPIN.

48:49.761 --> 48:53.138
ARTHUR TOLD ME
SHE PASSED AWAY.

48:54.473 --> 48:57.142
HOW ARE THE MAZES
COMING ALONG?

48:57.184 --> 48:58.895
EACH LEVEL
RELATES TO THE PART

48:58.935 --> 49:00.646
OF THE SUBJECT'S
SUBCONSCIOUS

49:00.688 --> 49:02.356
THAT WE ARE TRYING
TO ACCESS.

49:02.398 --> 49:04.483
SO, I'M MAKING THE BOTTOM
LEVEL A HOSPITAL

49:04.525 --> 49:06.402
SO FISCHER
WILL BRING HIS FATHER.

49:06.444 --> 49:09.405
UM, YOU KNOW, ACTUALLY,

49:09.447 --> 49:10.989
I HAVE A QUESTION
ABOUT THIS LAYOUT.

49:11.031 --> 49:13.200
NO, NO, NO. DON'T--
DON'T SHOW ME SPECIFICS.

49:13.242 --> 49:15.119
ONLY THE DREAMER
SHOULD KNOW THE LAYOUT.

49:15.160 --> 49:17.580
WHY IS THAT
SO IMPORTANT?

49:17.622 --> 49:19.457
IN CASE ONE OF US
BRINGS IN OUR PROJECTIONS.

49:19.498 --> 49:21.500
WE DON'T WANT THEM KNOWING
THE DETAILS OF THE MAZE.

49:21.542 --> 49:25.379
YOU MEAN
IN CASE YOU BRING MAL IN.

49:25.421 --> 49:28.173
YOU CAN'T KEEP HER OUT,
CAN YOU?

49:28.215 --> 49:29.508
RIGHT.

49:29.550 --> 49:31.135
YOU CAN'T BUILD BECAUSE,

49:31.176 --> 49:33.846
IF YOU KNOW THE MAZE,
THEN <i>SHE</i> KNOWS IT.

49:33.888 --> 49:36.223
WELL, SHE'D SABOTAGE
THE WHOLE OPERATION.

49:36.265 --> 49:37.850
COBB, DO THE OTHERS KNOW?

49:37.892 --> 49:39.435
NO. NO, THEY DON'T.

49:39.477 --> 49:41.646
YOU'VE GOTTA WARN THEM
IF THIS IS GETTING WORSE.

49:41.687 --> 49:42.939
NO ONE SAID
IT'S GETTING WORSE.

49:44.022 --> 49:45.483
I NEED TO GET HOME.

49:45.524 --> 49:48.193
THAT'S ALL I CARE ABOUT
RIGHT NOW.

49:48.235 --> 49:51.113
WHY CAN'T YOU GO HOME?

49:53.574 --> 49:57.620
BECAUSE THEY THINK
I KILLED HER.

49:58.621 --> 50:00.915
THANK YOU.

50:00.957 --> 50:02.207
FOR WHAT?

50:02.249 --> 50:04.042
FOR NOT ASKING
WHETHER I DID.

50:04.585 --> 50:06.838
"I WILL SPLIT UP
MY FATHER'S EMPIRE."

50:06.879 --> 50:08.589
NOW, THIS IS
OBVIOUSLY AN IDEA

50:08.631 --> 50:10.925
THAT ROBERT HIMSELF
WOULD CHOOSE TO REJECT.

50:10.967 --> 50:14.261
WHICH IS WHY WE NEED TO PLANT IT
DEEP IN HIS SUBCONSCIOUS.

50:14.303 --> 50:17.389
THE SUBCONSCIOUS IS MOTIVATED
BY EMOTION, RIGHT?

50:17.431 --> 50:18.390
NOT REASON.
WE NEED

50:18.432 --> 50:19.767
TO FIND A WAY
TO TRANSLATE THIS

50:19.809 --> 50:21.560
INTO AN EMOTIONAL CONCEPT.

50:21.602 --> 50:24.188
HOW DO YOU TRANSLATE A BUSINESS
STRATEGY INTO AN EMOTION?

50:24.229 --> 50:25.815
THAT'S WHAT WE'RE HERE
TO FIGURE OUT, RIGHT?

50:25.857 --> 50:28.400
NOW, ROBERT'S RELATIONSHIP
WITH HIS FATHER

50:28.442 --> 50:29.652
IS STRESSED, TO SAY THE LEAST.

50:29.694 --> 50:30.987
WELL,
CAN WE RUN WITH THAT?

50:31.027 --> 50:32.237
WE COULD SUGGEST TO HIM

50:32.279 --> 50:33.781
BREAKING UP
HIS FATHER'S COMPANY

50:33.823 --> 50:35.366
AS A "SCREW YOU"
TO THE OLD MAN.

50:35.407 --> 50:36.826
NO, BECAUSE I THINK
POSITIVE EMOTION

50:36.868 --> 50:38.243
TRUMPS NEGATIVE EMOTION
EVERY TIME.

50:38.285 --> 50:40.746
WE ALL YEARN
FOR RECONCILIATION,

50:40.788 --> 50:42.289
FOR CATHARSIS.

50:42.331 --> 50:43.916
WE NEED ROBERT FISCHER

50:43.958 --> 50:46.293
TO HAVE A POSITIVE
EMOTIONAL REACTION TO ALL THIS.

50:46.335 --> 50:48.004
ALL RIGHT,
WELL, TRY THIS.

50:48.044 --> 50:51.215
UM, "MY FATHER ACCEPTS THAT
I WANT TO CREATE FOR MYSELF,

50:51.256 --> 50:53.217
NOT FOLLOW
IN HIS FOOTSTEPS."

50:53.258 --> 50:54.677
THAT MIGHT WORK.

50:54.719 --> 50:56.428
"MIGHT"?

50:56.470 --> 50:58.263
WE'RE GONNA NEED TO DO
A LITTLE BETTER THAN "MIGHT."

50:58.305 --> 51:00.349
OH. THANK YOU FOR
YOUR CONTRIBUTION, ARTHUR.

51:00.391 --> 51:02.476
FORGIVE ME FOR WANTING
A LITTLE SPECIFICITY, EAMES.

51:02.518 --> 51:04.562
SPECIFICITY?

51:04.603 --> 51:06.772
INCEPTION'S
NOT ABOUT BEING SPECIFIC.

51:06.814 --> 51:08.357
WHEN WE GET INSIDE HIS MIND,

51:08.399 --> 51:10.234
WE'RE GONNA HAVE TO WORK
WITH WHAT WE FIND.

51:11.777 --> 51:13.320
ON THE TOP LEVEL,

51:13.362 --> 51:15.113
WE OPEN UP HIS RELATIONSHIP
WITH HIS FATHER,

51:15.155 --> 51:18.074
AND SAY, "I WILL NOT FOLLOW
IN MY FATHER'S FOOTSTEPS."

51:18.116 --> 51:19.535
THEN THE NEXT LEVEL DOWN,

51:19.577 --> 51:20.995
WE FEED HIM,

51:21.037 --> 51:22.997
"I WILL CREATE SOMETHING
FOR MYSELF."

51:23.039 --> 51:24.957
THEN, BY THE TIME
WE HIT THE BOTTOM LEVEL,

51:24.999 --> 51:26.667
WE BRING OUT THE BIG GUNS.

51:26.709 --> 51:29.127
"MY FATHER DOESN'T WANT ME
TO BE HIM."
EXACTLY.

51:29.169 --> 51:33.049
THREE LAYERS DOWN,
THE DREAMS ARE GONNA COLLAPSE

51:33.089 --> 51:34.508
WITH THE SLIGHTEST DISTURBANCE.

51:34.550 --> 51:35.843
SEDATION.

51:35.885 --> 51:37.511
FOR SLEEP STABLE ENOUGH

51:37.553 --> 51:39.513
TO CREATE THREE LAYERS
OF DREAMING,

51:39.555 --> 51:41.015
WE'LL HAVE TO COMBINE IT

51:41.057 --> 51:42.892
WITH AN <i>EXTREMELY</i>
POWERFUL SEDATIVE.

51:53.819 --> 51:55.446
GOOD NIGHT.

51:55.487 --> 51:57.823
THE COMPOUND WE'LL BE USING
TO SHARE THE DREAM

51:57.865 --> 52:00.325
CREATES A VERY CLEAR CONNECTION
BETWEEN DREAMERS

52:00.367 --> 52:02.369
WHILST ACTUALLY ACCELERATING
BRAIN FUNCTION.

52:02.411 --> 52:04.747
IN OTHER WORDS, IT GIVES US
MORE TIME ON EACH LEVEL.

52:04.789 --> 52:07.959
BRAIN FUNCTION IN THE DREAM
WILL BE ABOUT 20 TIMES NORMAL.

52:08.000 --> 52:10.335
WHEN YOU ENTER A DREAM
WITHIN THAT DREAM,

52:10.377 --> 52:11.754
THE EFFECT IS COMPOUNDED.

52:11.796 --> 52:13.380
IT'S 3 DREAMS--
THAT'S 10 HOURS TIMES--

52:13.422 --> 52:15.049
I'M SORRY, MATH WAS NEVER
MY STRONG SUBJECT.

52:15.091 --> 52:16.592
H-HOW MUCH TIME IS THAT?

52:16.634 --> 52:20.471
IT'S A WEEK,
THE FIRST LEVEL DOWN,

52:20.512 --> 52:22.389
SIX MONTHS,
THE SECOND LEVEL DOWN,

52:22.431 --> 52:23.641
AND THE THIRD LEVEL...

52:23.682 --> 52:25.017
IT'S 10 YEARS.

52:27.352 --> 52:29.855
WHO WOULD WANT TO BE STUCK
IN A DREAM FOR 10 YEARS?

52:29.897 --> 52:31.523
DEPENDS ON THE DREAM.

52:31.565 --> 52:33.609
SO, ONCE WE'VE MADE THE PLANT,
HOW DO WE GET OUT?

52:33.651 --> 52:35.987
AND I'M HOPING YOU HAVE
SOMETHING MORE ELEGANT IN MIND

52:36.028 --> 52:37.404
THAN SHOOTING ME
IN THE HEAD.

52:37.446 --> 52:38.656
A KICK.

52:38.697 --> 52:40.491
WHAT'S A KICK?

52:40.532 --> 52:42.827
<i>THIS,</i> ARIADNE,
WOULD BE A KICK.

52:45.871 --> 52:48.040
IT'S THAT FEELING OF FALLING
YOU GET THAT JOLTS YOU AWAKE.

52:48.082 --> 52:49.792
IT
SNAPS YOU OUT OF THE DREAM.

52:49.834 --> 52:51.543
ARE WE GONNA FEEL A KICK
WITH THIS KIND OF SEDATION?

52:51.585 --> 52:52.837
OH, THAT'S THE CLEVER PART.

52:52.878 --> 52:54.338
I CUSTOMIZED THE SEDATIVE

52:54.379 --> 52:56.715
TO LEAVE INNER EAR FUNCTION
UNIMPAIRED.

52:56.757 --> 52:58.801
THAT WAY,
HOWEVER DEEP THE SLEEP,

52:58.843 --> 53:00.636
THE SLEEPER
STILL FEELS FALLING.

53:00.678 --> 53:02.596
OR TIPPING.

53:04.264 --> 53:06.350
THE TRICK IS
TO SYNCHRONIZE A KICK

53:06.391 --> 53:08.560
THAT CAN PENETRATE
ALL THREE LEVELS.

53:08.602 --> 53:10.146
WE COULD USE
THE MUSICAL COUNTDOWN

53:10.186 --> 53:11.772
TO SYNCHRONIZE
THE DIFFERENT KICKS.

53:20.781 --> 53:22.825
HE HASN'T GOT
ANY SURGERY SCHEDULED.

53:22.867 --> 53:24.535
THERE'S NO DENTAL,
NOTHING.

53:24.576 --> 53:26.202
WASN'T HE SUPPOSED
TO HAVE A KNEE OPERATION?

53:26.244 --> 53:28.580
NOTHING. NOTHING THAT THEY'D
PUT HIM UNDER FOR, ANYWAY.

53:28.622 --> 53:31.083
AND WE NEED-- WE NEED
AT LEAST A GOOD 10 HOURS.

53:31.125 --> 53:33.169
SYDNEY TO LOS ANGELES.

53:34.419 --> 53:37.048
ONE OF THE LONGEST FLIGHTS
IN THE WORLD.

53:37.089 --> 53:38.799
HE MAKES IT EVERY TWO WEEKS.

53:38.841 --> 53:41.135
HE MUST BE
FLYING PRIVATE, THEN.

53:41.177 --> 53:44.805
NOT IF THERE WERE UNEXPECTED
MAINTENANCE WITH HIS PLANE.

53:44.847 --> 53:46.640
IT WOULD HAVE TO BE A 747.

53:46.682 --> 53:47.265
WHY'S THAT?

53:47.307 --> 53:48.184
BECAUSE ON A 747,

53:48.224 --> 53:49.351
THE PILOT IS UP TOP,

53:49.393 --> 53:50.811
AND THE FIRST-CLASS CABIN
IS IN THE NOSE,

53:50.853 --> 53:52.354
SO NO ONE
WOULD WALK THROUGH.

53:52.396 --> 53:54.106
BUT YOU'D HAVE TO BUY OUT
THE ENTIRE CABIN

53:54.148 --> 53:55.900
<i>AND</i> THE FIRST-CLASS
FLIGHT ATTENDANT.

53:55.941 --> 53:57.568
I BOUGHT THE AIRLINE.

53:59.070 --> 54:00.905
IT SEEMED NEATER.

54:02.280 --> 54:05.910
WELL, LOOKS LIKE
WE HAVE OUR 10 HOURS.

54:05.951 --> 54:07.703
ARIADNE?

54:07.745 --> 54:09.163
TERRIFIC WORK,
BY THE WAY.

54:56.210 --> 55:00.089
YOU KNOW HOW TO FIND ME.

55:00.131 --> 55:02.258
YOU KNOW
WHAT YOU HAVE TO DO.

55:05.594 --> 55:09.681
YOU REMEMBER WHEN YOU ASKED ME
TO MARRY YOU?

55:09.723 --> 55:13.435
OF COURSE I DO.

55:13.477 --> 55:15.896
YOU SAID YOU HAD A DREAM.

55:18.816 --> 55:22.527
THAT WE'D GROW OLD
TOGETHER.

55:22.569 --> 55:25.405
AND WE CAN.

55:31.536 --> 55:32.955
YOU SHOULDN'T BE HERE.

55:37.001 --> 55:39.003
I JUST WANTED TO SEE
WHAT KIND OF "TESTS"

55:39.044 --> 55:40.879
YOU'RE DOING ON YOUR OWN
EVERY NIGHT.

55:40.921 --> 55:42.589
ALL RIGHT, WELL, THIS
HAS NOTHING TO DO WITH YOU.

55:42.631 --> 55:44.049
THIS HAS <i>EVERYTHING</i>
TO DO WITH ME.

55:44.091 --> 55:45.634
YOU'VE ASKED ME TO SHARE DREAMS
WITH YOU.

55:45.676 --> 55:47.303
NOT <i>THESE.</i>

55:47.343 --> 55:50.097
THESE ARE <i>MY</i> DREAMS.

56:00.899 --> 56:03.401
WHY DO YOU DO THIS
TO YOURSELF?

56:03.443 --> 56:06.530
IT'S THE ONLY WAY
I CAN STILL DREAM.

56:06.571 --> 56:10.575
WHY IS IT SO IMPORTANT
TO DREAM?

56:10.617 --> 56:13.620
IN MY DREAMS,
WE'RE STILL TOGETHER.

56:27.259 --> 56:29.427
THESE AREN'T JUST DREAMS.

56:31.429 --> 56:32.848
THESE ARE MEMORIES.

56:32.890 --> 56:34.474
AND-- AND YOU SAID
NEVER TO USE MEMORIES.

56:34.516 --> 56:35.809
I KNOW I DID.

56:35.851 --> 56:38.394
YOU'RE TRYING
TO KEEP HER ALIVE.

56:38.436 --> 56:40.480
YOU CAN'T LET HER GO.

56:40.522 --> 56:42.191
YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND.

56:42.233 --> 56:44.943
THESE ARE MOMENTS
I REGRET.

56:44.985 --> 56:46.904
THEY'RE MEMORIES
THAT I <i>HAVE</i> TO CHANGE.

56:46.945 --> 56:50.824
WELL, WHAT'S DOWN <i>THERE</i>
THAT YOU REGRET?

56:50.866 --> 56:52.408
LISTEN,
THERE'S ONLY ONE THING

56:52.450 --> 56:54.078
YOU NEED TO UNDERSTAND
ABOUT ME.

57:01.919 --> 57:04.046
THIS IS YOUR HOUSE?

57:04.088 --> 57:07.341
MINE AND MAL'S, YES.

57:07.383 --> 57:09.676
WHERE IS SHE?

57:09.718 --> 57:11.595
SHE'S ALREADY GONE.

57:15.933 --> 57:18.143
THAT'S MY SON, JAMES.

57:18.185 --> 57:20.896
HE'S DIGGING FOR SOMETHING,
MAYBE A WORM.

57:22.189 --> 57:23.941
THAT'S PHILLIPA.

57:23.982 --> 57:26.360
SEE, I THOUGHT
ABOUT CALLING OUT TO THEM,

57:26.402 --> 57:29.154
SO THEY'D TURN AND SMILE
AND I COULD SEE THOSE...

57:29.196 --> 57:31.531
THOSE BEAUTIFUL FACES
OF THEIRS.

57:31.573 --> 57:33.033
BUT...

57:33.075 --> 57:35.577
IT'S ALL TOO LATE.

57:35.619 --> 57:37.621
RIGHT NOW...
OR NEVER, COBB.

57:42.459 --> 57:44.378
THEN I START TO PANIC.

57:44.420 --> 57:47.256
I REALIZE I'M GONNA REGRET
THIS MOMENT,

57:47.298 --> 57:50.342
THAT I NEED TO SEE THEIR FACES
ONE LAST TIME.

57:50.384 --> 57:51.676
JAMES! PHILLIPA!

57:51.718 --> 57:53.553
COME ON IN!

57:53.595 --> 57:56.807
BUT THE MOMENT'S PAST.

57:56.848 --> 58:00.227
AND WHATEVER I DO,
I CAN'T CHANGE THIS MOMENT.

58:00.269 --> 58:04.148
AS I'M ABOUT TO CALL OUT
TO THEM...

58:04.189 --> 58:06.024
THEY RUN AWAY.

58:07.567 --> 58:10.112
IF I'M EVER GONNA SEE
THEIR FACES AGAIN,

58:10.154 --> 58:12.030
I'VE GOTTA
GET BACK HOME...

58:12.990 --> 58:13.991
...TO THE REAL WORLD.

58:56.074 --> 58:57.659
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

58:57.701 --> 58:59.036
MY NAME IS--

58:59.077 --> 59:00.912
I KNOW WHO YOU ARE.

59:00.954 --> 59:02.956
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

59:10.755 --> 59:13.675
I'M JUST TRYING
TO UNDERSTAND.

59:13.717 --> 59:16.428
HOW COULD YOU
UNDERSTAND?

59:16.470 --> 59:19.264
DO YOU KNOW WHAT IT IS
TO BE A LOVER?

59:21.183 --> 59:23.435
TO BE HALF OF A WHOLE?

59:23.477 --> 59:25.603
NO.

59:27.022 --> 59:29.733
I'LL TELL YOU A RIDDLE.

59:29.774 --> 59:33.695
YOU'RE WAITING
FOR A TRAIN,

59:33.737 --> 59:37.366
A TRAIN THAT WILL TAKE YOU
FAR AWAY.

59:39.034 --> 59:42.413
YOU KNOW WHERE YOU HOPE
THIS TRAIN WILL TAKE YOU,

59:42.454 --> 59:45.332
BUT YOU DON'T KNOW
FOR SURE.

59:45.374 --> 59:47.418
BUT IT DOESN'T MATTER.

59:47.459 --> 59:50.504
HOW CAN IT
NOT MATTER TO YOU

59:50.546 --> 59:52.381
WHERE THAT TRAIN
WILL TAKE YOU?

59:52.423 --> 59:53.965
BECAUSE WE'LL BE TOGETHER.

59:54.007 --> 59:56.552
HOW COULD YOU
BRING HER HERE, DOM?

59:56.593 --> 59:57.844
WHAT IS THIS PLACE?

59:57.886 --> 59:59.221
THIS IS THE HOTEL SUITE

59:59.263 --> 01:00:01.432
WHERE WE USED TO SPEND
OUR ANNIVERSARY.

01:00:01.473 --> 01:00:02.891
WHAT HAPPENED HERE?

01:00:04.768 --> 01:00:06.270
YOU PROMISED!

01:00:06.311 --> 01:00:08.439
YOU PROMISED
WE'D BE TOGETHER!

01:00:08.480 --> 01:00:10.148
PLEASE, I NEED YOU TO STAY HERE
JUST FOR NOW!

01:00:10.190 --> 01:00:11.733
YOU SAID
WE'D BE TOGETHER!

01:00:11.775 --> 01:00:13.693
YOU SAID WE'D
GROW OLD TOGETHER!

01:00:13.735 --> 01:00:16.196
I'LL COME BACK FOR YOU.
I PROMISE.

01:00:33.547 --> 01:00:37.634
DO YOU THINK
YOU CAN JUST BUILD A PRISON

01:00:37.675 --> 01:00:39.303
OF MEMORIES
TO LOCK HER IN?

01:00:40.720 --> 01:00:42.806
DO YOU REALLY THINK THAT
THAT'S GONNA CONTAIN HER?

01:00:42.847 --> 01:00:44.891
IT'S TIME.

01:00:46.059 --> 01:00:48.270
MAURICE FISCHER JUST DIED
IN SYDNEY.

01:00:48.312 --> 01:00:49.854
WHEN'S THE FUNERAL?

01:00:49.896 --> 01:00:50.439
THURSDAY.

01:00:50.481 --> 01:00:51.815
IN LOS ANGELES.

01:00:51.856 --> 01:00:53.191
ROBERT SHOULD
ACCOMPANY THE BODY

01:00:53.233 --> 01:00:54.318
NO LATER THAN TUESDAY.
WE SHOULD MOVE.

01:00:54.359 --> 01:00:56.361
RIGHT.

01:00:56.403 --> 01:00:57.571
COBB,
I'M COMING WITH YOU.

01:00:57.613 --> 01:00:59.573
I PROMISED MILES. NO.

01:00:59.615 --> 01:01:01.366
THE TEAM NEEDS SOMEONE
WHO UNDERSTANDS

01:01:01.408 --> 01:01:02.826
WHAT YOU'RE
STRUGGLING WITH.

01:01:05.745 --> 01:01:07.623
A-AND IT DOESN'T
HAVE TO BE ME,

01:01:07.664 --> 01:01:11.042
BUT THEN YOU HAVE TO SHOW
ARTHUR WHAT I JUST SAW.

01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:18.550
GET US ANOTHER SEAT
ON THE PLANE.

01:01:22.846 --> 01:01:24.181
IF I GET ON THIS PLANE

01:01:24.222 --> 01:01:25.682
AND YOU DON'T HONOR
OUR AGREEMENT...

01:01:25.723 --> 01:01:29.394
WHEN WE LAND, I GO TO JAIL
FOR THE REST OF MY LIFE.

01:01:29.436 --> 01:01:31.313
COMPLETE THE JOB EN ROUTE,

01:01:31.355 --> 01:01:34.941
I MAKE <i>ONE</i> PHONE CALL
FROM THE PLANE,

01:01:34.983 --> 01:01:38.028
YOU HAVE NO TROUBLE
GETTING THROUGH IMMIGRATION.

01:01:51.249 --> 01:01:52.792
I'M SORRY.

01:01:52.834 --> 01:01:55.212
OH, YEAH, I'M SORRY.
MY BAD.

01:02:28.870 --> 01:02:31.373
EXCUSE ME,
I THINK THIS IS YOURS?

01:02:31.415 --> 01:02:33.083
YOU MUST HAVE
DROPPED IT.

01:02:33.124 --> 01:02:34.876
WOULD YOU GENTLEMEN
CARE FOR A DRINK?

01:02:34.918 --> 01:02:36.127
UH, WATER, PLEASE.

01:02:36.169 --> 01:02:38.963
UM, SAME, PLEASE.

01:02:39.005 --> 01:02:41.299
UM...

01:02:41.341 --> 01:02:43.093
THANK YOU.

01:02:43.134 --> 01:02:45.011
YOU KNOW,
I COULDN'T HELP BUT NOTICE,

01:02:45.053 --> 01:02:47.180
BUT YOU WOULDN'T HAPPEN
TO BE RELATED TO...

01:02:47.222 --> 01:02:48.890
<i>THE</i> MAURICE FISCHER,
WOULD YOU?

01:02:48.932 --> 01:02:50.808
YES, HE, UM...

01:02:50.850 --> 01:02:53.937
HE WAS MY FATHER.

01:02:53.978 --> 01:02:55.855
WELL, HE WAS
A VERY INSPIRING FIGURE.

01:02:55.897 --> 01:02:57.482
I'M SORRY FOR YOUR LOSS.

01:03:00.277 --> 01:03:01.486
HERE YOU GO.

01:03:01.528 --> 01:03:02.654
THANK YOU.

01:03:02.696 --> 01:03:04.281
HEY.

01:03:04.322 --> 01:03:05.949
TO YOUR FATHER.

01:03:05.990 --> 01:03:08.702
MAY HE REST IN PEACE, HUH?

01:04:17.312 --> 01:04:18.855
COULDN'T HAVE PEED
<i>BEFORE</i> YOU WENT UNDER?

01:04:18.896 --> 01:04:20.231
SORRY.

01:04:20.273 --> 01:04:22.025
BIT TOO MUCH FREE CHAMPAGNE
BEFORE TAKEOFF, EH, YUSUF?

01:04:22.066 --> 01:04:23.109
HA HA BLOODY HA.

01:04:23.151 --> 01:04:24.235
WELL, WE KNOW HE'S
GONNA BE LOOKING

01:04:24.277 --> 01:04:25.529
FOR A TAXI IN
<i>THIS</i> WEATHER.

01:04:37.165 --> 01:04:38.916
ASSHOLE!

01:04:38.958 --> 01:04:40.627
HEY, MAN,
WHY DON'T YOU TRY--

01:04:40.669 --> 01:04:42.086
WALK AWAY.

01:04:57.853 --> 01:04:59.437
JUST HAVE HIM--
I GOTTA GO.

01:04:59.479 --> 01:05:01.648
ALL RIGHT. TAXI!
THANK YOU.

01:05:03.983 --> 01:05:07.904
ALL RIGHT, THIRD AND MARKET.
SNAPPY.

01:05:07.945 --> 01:05:09.072
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

01:05:09.113 --> 01:05:10.407
OH, I'M SORRY.
I THOUGHT IT WAS FREE.

01:05:10.448 --> 01:05:11.157
WELL, IT'S <i>NOT.</i>

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:12.450
MAYBE WE COULD SHARE.

01:05:12.492 --> 01:05:15.328
YEAH, MAYBE NOT. CAN YOU
PULL OVER AND GET THIS...

01:05:17.914 --> 01:05:18.665
GREAT.

01:05:23.587 --> 01:05:24.671
COME ON!

01:05:36.516 --> 01:05:37.851
THERE'S $500 IN THERE,

01:05:37.893 --> 01:05:39.519
AND THE WALLET'S
WORTH MORE THAN THAT.

01:05:39.561 --> 01:05:41.062
SO YOU MIGHT AT LEAST
DROP ME AT MY STOP.

01:05:41.104 --> 01:05:42.647
I'M AFRAID
IT DOESN'T...

01:05:42.689 --> 01:05:44.357
BULLET!

01:05:52.240 --> 01:05:54.075
COVER HIM!
DOWN! DOWN NOW!

01:05:54.117 --> 01:05:55.368
WHAT THE HELL
IS GOING ON?!

01:06:00.123 --> 01:06:01.958
THIS WASN'T IN THE DESIGN.

01:06:01.999 --> 01:06:04.001
COBB?

01:06:04.043 --> 01:06:05.503
COBB?!

01:06:48.839 --> 01:06:50.340
AAH!

01:06:56.304 --> 01:06:57.597
READY?!

01:07:04.187 --> 01:07:07.440
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?!
YEAH, I-I'M OKAY.
I'M OKAY.

01:07:07.482 --> 01:07:10.193
FISCHER'S OKAY,
UNLESS HE GETS CARSICK.

01:07:10.234 --> 01:07:11.528
SAITO?

01:07:30.380 --> 01:07:32.215
GET FISCHER
IN THE BACK ROOM NOW!

01:07:32.256 --> 01:07:34.467
GET HIM IN THE BACK ROOM.
MOVE!

01:07:35.927 --> 01:07:37.220
HAS HE BEEN SHOT?
I-IS HE DYING?

01:07:37.261 --> 01:07:38.722
I DON'T KNOW.
JESUS CHRIST.

01:07:38.763 --> 01:07:40.056
WHERE WERE YOU?
WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

01:07:40.097 --> 01:07:41.432
WE WERE BLOCKED
BY A FREIGHT TRAIN.

01:07:41.474 --> 01:07:42.976
WHY WOULD YOU PUT
A TRAIN CROSSING

01:07:43.018 --> 01:07:44.352
IN THE MIDDLE
OF A DOWNTOWN INTERSECTION?

01:07:44.394 --> 01:07:45.269
WELL, I DIDN'T.

01:07:45.311 --> 01:07:46.270
WELL,
WHERE'D IT COME FROM?

01:07:46.312 --> 01:07:47.313
WELL, LET ME ASK <i>YOU</i>
A QUESTION!

01:07:47.355 --> 01:07:48.565
WHY THE HELL
WERE WE AMBUSHED, HUH?!

01:07:48.606 --> 01:07:49.774
THOSE WERE NOT
NORMAL PROJECTIONS!

01:07:49.816 --> 01:07:50.859
THEY'D BEEN TRAINED,
FOR GOD'S SAKES!

01:07:50.901 --> 01:07:51.693
YOU'RE RIGHT.

01:07:51.735 --> 01:07:52.903
HOW COULD HE BE TRAINED?!

01:07:52.944 --> 01:07:54.362
FISCHER
HAD AN EXTRACTOR

01:07:54.404 --> 01:07:56.113
TEACH HIS SUBCONSCIOUS
TO DEFEND ITSELF.

01:07:56.155 --> 01:07:58.324
SO HIS SUBCONSCIOUS
IS MILITARIZED.

01:07:58.366 --> 01:08:00.076
IT SHOULD'VE SHOWN
IN THE RESEARCH. I'M SORRY.

01:08:00.117 --> 01:08:01.953
SO WHY THE HELL
<i>DIDN'T</i> IT?
CALM DOWN.

01:08:01.995 --> 01:08:03.830
<i>DON'T</i> TELL ME
TO CALM DOWN!

01:08:03.872 --> 01:08:05.289
THIS WAS YOUR JOB,
GODDAMN IT!

01:08:05.331 --> 01:08:06.958
THIS WAS
YOUR RESPONSIBILITY!

01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:09.044
YOU WERE MEANT TO CHECK
FISCHER'S BACKGROUND THOROUGHLY!

01:08:09.085 --> 01:08:11.046
WE ARE <i>NOT</i> PREPARED
FOR THIS TYPE OF VIOLENCE!

01:08:11.087 --> 01:08:13.172
WE <i>HAVE</i> DEALT
WITH SUB-SECURITY BEFORE!

01:08:13.214 --> 01:08:14.841
WE'LL BE A LITTLE MORE CAREFUL,
AND WE'RE GONNA BE FINE!

01:08:14.883 --> 01:08:17.134
THIS WAS NOT A PART OF THE PLAN!
HE'S DYING, FOR GOD'S SAKES!

01:08:17.176 --> 01:08:18.053
PUT HIM
OUT OF HIS MISERY.

01:08:18.094 --> 01:08:19.345
NO, DON'T DO THAT!

01:08:19.387 --> 01:08:20.055
HEY, HEY.

01:08:20.096 --> 01:08:21.138
<i>DON'T</i> DO THAT.

01:08:21.180 --> 01:08:23.474
HE'S IN AGONY.
I'M WAKING HIM UP.

01:08:23.516 --> 01:08:25.476
NO.
IT WON'T WAKE HIM UP.

01:08:25.518 --> 01:08:26.853
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
IT <i>WON'T</i> WAKE HIM UP?

01:08:26.895 --> 01:08:27.896
IT <i>WON'T</i> WAKE HIM UP.

01:08:27.938 --> 01:08:29.355
WHEN WE DIE IN A DREAM,
WE WAKE UP.

01:08:29.397 --> 01:08:30.732
NOT FROM THIS.

01:08:30.774 --> 01:08:33.026
WE'RE TOO HEAVILY SEDATED
TO WAKE UP THAT WAY.

01:08:33.068 --> 01:08:35.653
RIGHT. SO, WHAT HAPPENS
WHEN WE DIE?

01:08:35.695 --> 01:08:36.780
WE DROP INTO LIMBO.

01:08:36.821 --> 01:08:37.614
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

01:08:37.655 --> 01:08:38.782
LIMBO?!

01:08:38.823 --> 01:08:40.491
UNCONSTRUCTED
DREAM SPACE.

01:08:40.533 --> 01:08:41.743
WELL, WHAT THE HELL
IS DOWN THERE?

01:08:41.785 --> 01:08:43.202
JUST RAW,
INFINITE SUBCONSCIOUS.

01:08:43.244 --> 01:08:44.746
<i>NOTHING</i> IS DOWN THERE,

01:08:44.788 --> 01:08:46.623
EXCEPT FOR WHATEVER MIGHT HAVE
BEEN LEFT BEHIND

01:08:46.664 --> 01:08:48.124
BY ANYONE
SHARING THE DREAM

01:08:48.165 --> 01:08:49.793
WHO'S BEEN TRAPPED
THERE BEFORE.

01:08:49.834 --> 01:08:52.253
WHICH, IN OUR CASE,
IS JUST <i>YOU.</i>

01:08:52.295 --> 01:08:53.880
WELL, HOW LONG
COULD WE BE STUCK THERE?

01:08:53.922 --> 01:08:55.506
CAN'T EVEN THINK
ABOUT TRYING TO ESCAPE

01:08:55.548 --> 01:08:57.133
UNTIL THE SEDATION
HAS EASED.

01:08:57.174 --> 01:08:58.384
HOW LONG, YUSUF?
DECADES.

01:08:58.426 --> 01:08:59.970
IT COULD BE INFINITE.
I DON'T KNOW. ASK HIM.

01:09:00.011 --> 01:09:01.387
HE'S THE ONE
WHO'S BEEN THERE.

01:09:01.429 --> 01:09:02.472
LET'S JUST
GET HIM UPSTAIRS.

01:09:03.974 --> 01:09:05.558
GREAT.

01:09:05.600 --> 01:09:07.102
THANK YOU.

01:09:07.143 --> 01:09:09.562
SO, NOW WE'RE TRAPPED
IN FISCHER'S MIND,

01:09:09.604 --> 01:09:11.355
BATTLING HIS OWN
PRIVATE ARMY.

01:09:11.397 --> 01:09:12.983
AND IF WE GET KILLED,

01:09:13.024 --> 01:09:14.358
WE'LL BE LOST IN LIMBO

01:09:14.400 --> 01:09:16.945
TILL OUR BRAINS TURN
TO SCRAMBLED EGG, HMM?

01:09:23.534 --> 01:09:24.911
SOMEONE GOT FIRST AID?

01:09:28.247 --> 01:09:29.206
SO, YOU KNEW
ABOUT THESE RISKS,

01:09:29.248 --> 01:09:30.416
AND YOU DIDN'T TELL US?

01:09:30.458 --> 01:09:31.501
THERE WEREN'T MEANT
TO BE ANY RISKS.

01:09:31.542 --> 01:09:32.836
I DIDN'T KNOW WE'D BE DEALING

01:09:32.877 --> 01:09:33.795
WITH A LOAD OF GUNFIRE.

01:09:33.837 --> 01:09:34.462
YOU HAD NO RIGHT.

01:09:34.504 --> 01:09:35.296
THIS WAS THE ONLY WAY

01:09:35.338 --> 01:09:36.464
TO GO THREE LAYERS DEEP.

01:09:36.506 --> 01:09:38.174
AND YOU.

01:09:38.215 --> 01:09:39.634
YOU KNEW ABOUT THIS
AND WENT ALONG WITH IT?

01:09:39.676 --> 01:09:40.635
I TRUSTED HIM!

01:09:40.677 --> 01:09:41.678
YOU <i>TRUSTED</i> HIM?
WHEN?

01:09:41.719 --> 01:09:42.553
WHEN HE PROMISED YOU
HALF HIS SHARE?

01:09:42.595 --> 01:09:44.681
NO. HIS <i>WHOLE</i> SHARE.

01:09:44.722 --> 01:09:46.432
BESIDES, HE SAID HE'D
DONE IT BEFORE.

01:09:46.474 --> 01:09:47.684
OH, HE'D DONE IT BEFORE.
WHAT, WITH MAL?

01:09:47.725 --> 01:09:48.601
'CAUSE <i>THAT</i> WORKED
SO GOOD?

01:09:48.643 --> 01:09:49.894
THAT HAS NOTHING TO DO
WITH IT.

01:09:49.936 --> 01:09:52.063
I DID WHAT I HAD TO DO
TO GET BACK TO MY CHILDREN.

01:09:52.105 --> 01:09:53.272
SO YOU LED US
INTO A WAR ZONE

01:09:53.314 --> 01:09:54.273
WITH NO WAY OUT.

01:09:54.315 --> 01:09:55.859
THERE IS A WAY OUT.
ALL RIGHT?

01:09:55.900 --> 01:09:57.360
WE CONTINUE ON
WITH THE JOB,

01:09:57.401 --> 01:09:59.070
AND WE DO IT
AS FAST AS POSSIBLE,

01:09:59.112 --> 01:10:01.405
AND WE GET OUT USING THE KICK,
JUST LIKE BEFORE.

01:10:01.447 --> 01:10:03.491
FORGET IT. WE GO ANY DEEPER,
WE JUST RAISE THE STAKES.

01:10:03.533 --> 01:10:05.409
I AM SITTING THIS ONE OUT
ON THIS LEVEL, BOYS.

01:10:05.451 --> 01:10:07.871
FISCHER'S SECURITY
IS SURROUNDING
THIS PLACE AS WE SPEAK.

01:10:07.912 --> 01:10:10.331
10 HOURS OF FLIGHT TIME
IS A WEEK AT THIS LEVEL.

01:10:10.373 --> 01:10:12.750
THAT MEANS EACH AND EVERY ONE
OF US WILL BE KILLED.

01:10:12.792 --> 01:10:14.210
THAT I CAN GUARANTEE YOU.

01:10:14.251 --> 01:10:16.462
WE HAVE NO OTHER CHOICE
BUT TO CONTINUE ON

01:10:16.504 --> 01:10:18.214
AND DO IT
AS FAST AS POSSIBLE.

01:10:19.924 --> 01:10:22.552
DOWNWARDS IS
THE ONLY WAY FORWARDS.

01:10:24.095 --> 01:10:25.763
GET READY.

01:10:25.805 --> 01:10:27.640
YOU, COME ON.
LET'S GO SHAKE HIM UP.

01:10:32.145 --> 01:10:35.231
I'M INSURED AGAINST KIDNAPPING
FOR UP TO 10 MILLION.

01:10:35.272 --> 01:10:36.941
THIS SHOULD BE VERY SIMPLE.

01:10:36.983 --> 01:10:38.526
SHUT UP!
IT <i>WON'T</i> BE.

01:10:38.568 --> 01:10:40.361
IN YOUR FATHER'S OFFICE,
BELOW THE BOOKSHELVES,

01:10:40.403 --> 01:10:41.821
IS HIS PERSONAL SAFE.

01:10:41.863 --> 01:10:43.656
WE NEED THE COMBINATION.

01:10:43.698 --> 01:10:46.034
I DON'T KNOW ANY SAFE.

01:10:46.076 --> 01:10:48.661
THAT DOESN'T MEAN
YOU DON'T KNOW THE COMBINATION.

01:10:50.163 --> 01:10:52.123
TELL US WHAT IT IS.

01:10:52.165 --> 01:10:54.959
I DON'T KNOW.

01:10:59.547 --> 01:11:01.799
WE HAVE IT ON GOOD AUTHORITY
YOU <i>DO</i> KNOW.

01:11:01.841 --> 01:11:04.301
YEAH? WHOSE AUTHORITY?

01:11:04.343 --> 01:11:07.263
$500, THIS COST?

01:11:07.304 --> 01:11:09.182
WHAT'S INSIDE IT?

01:11:09.224 --> 01:11:11.392
CASH, CARDS, I.D...

01:11:11.434 --> 01:11:13.103
AND THIS.

01:11:17.648 --> 01:11:19.901
USEFUL?

01:11:19.943 --> 01:11:21.652
MAYBE.

01:11:21.694 --> 01:11:24.155
YOU'RE ON.
YOU'VE GOT AN HOUR.

01:11:24.197 --> 01:11:26.490
AN HOUR?

01:11:26.532 --> 01:11:28.952
I WAS SUPPOSED TO HAVE ALL
NIGHT TO CRACK THIS.

01:11:28.993 --> 01:11:31.287
AND SAITO WASN'T SUPPOSED
TO BE SHOT IN THE CHEST.

01:11:31.328 --> 01:11:32.663
YOU'VE GOT ONE HOUR.

01:11:32.705 --> 01:11:35.041
NOW, GET US SOMETHING
USEFUL, PLEASE.

01:11:37.627 --> 01:11:38.836
WHAT'S THAT?

01:11:38.878 --> 01:11:40.004
GOOD AUTHORITY.

01:11:43.633 --> 01:11:45.760
UNCLE PETER.

01:11:45.802 --> 01:11:48.263
JUST--
JUST MAKE THEM STOP.

01:11:48.304 --> 01:11:49.847
THE COMBINATION.

01:11:49.889 --> 01:11:51.390
I DON'T KNOW IT.

01:11:51.432 --> 01:11:53.559
WHY DOES BROWNING
SAY YOU DO?

01:11:53.601 --> 01:11:54.685
I DON'T KNOW.

01:11:54.727 --> 01:11:56.854
JUST LET ME TALK TO HIM,
AND I'LL FIND OUT.

01:11:59.649 --> 01:12:01.985
YOU HAVE ONE HOUR!
START TALKING.

01:12:03.278 --> 01:12:04.654
AHH.
YOU ALL RIGHT?

01:12:04.695 --> 01:12:06.906
AAH.

01:12:06.948 --> 01:12:08.283
YOU OKAY?

01:12:11.410 --> 01:12:14.705
THOSE BASTARDS HAVE HAD
AT ME FOR TWO DAYS.

01:12:16.332 --> 01:12:18.251
THEY HAVE SOMEONE WITH ACCESS
TO YOUR FATHER'S OFFICE,

01:12:18.293 --> 01:12:20.086
AND THEY'RE TRYING
TO OPEN HIS SAFE.

01:12:20.128 --> 01:12:21.420
YEAH.

01:12:21.462 --> 01:12:22.546
THEY THOUGHT <i>I'D</i> KNOW
THE COMBINATION,

01:12:22.588 --> 01:12:23.756
BUT I DON'T KNOW IT.

01:12:23.798 --> 01:12:25.382
YEAH, WELL,
NEITHER DO I, SO...

01:12:25.424 --> 01:12:26.717
WHAT?

01:12:26.759 --> 01:12:29.512
MAURICE TOLD ME
THAT WHEN HE PASSED,

01:12:29.553 --> 01:12:31.347
YOU WERE THE ONLY ONE
THAT WOULD BE ABLE TO OPEN IT.

01:12:31.388 --> 01:12:33.432
NO, HE NEVER-- HE NEVER
GAVE ME ANY COMBINATION.

01:12:33.474 --> 01:12:35.268
MAYBE HE DID.

01:12:35.310 --> 01:12:38.313
MAYBE YOU JUST DIDN'T KNOW
IT WAS THE COMBINATION.

01:12:38.354 --> 01:12:39.438
WELL, WHAT, THEN?

01:12:39.480 --> 01:12:40.523
I DON'T KNOW.

01:12:40.564 --> 01:12:42.233
SOME MEANINGFUL
COMBINATION OF NUMBERS

01:12:42.275 --> 01:12:45.820
BASED ON YOUR--
YOUR EXPERIENCES WITH MAURICE.

01:12:47.613 --> 01:12:49.907
WE DIDN'T HAVE
VERY MANY, UM...

01:12:49.949 --> 01:12:52.118
MEANINGFUL EXPERIENCES
TOGETHER.

01:12:52.160 --> 01:12:54.287
PERHAPS
AFTER YOUR MOTHER DIED.

01:12:57.040 --> 01:12:58.457
AFTER MY MOTHER DIED,

01:12:58.499 --> 01:12:59.709
YOU KNOW WHAT HE TOLD ME?

01:12:59.750 --> 01:13:03.504
"ROBERT,
THERE'S REALLY...

01:13:03.546 --> 01:13:06.341
<i>NOTHING</i> TO BE SAID."

01:13:06.382 --> 01:13:08.843
OH, WELL,
HE WAS BAD WITH EMOTION.

01:13:08.885 --> 01:13:11.721
I WAS 11, UNCLE PETER.

01:13:11.762 --> 01:13:13.056
HOW'S HE DOIN'?

01:13:13.097 --> 01:13:15.183
HE'S IN A LOT OF PAIN.

01:13:15.225 --> 01:13:17.101
WHEN WE GET DOWN
TO THE LOWER LEVELS,

01:13:17.143 --> 01:13:18.811
THE PAIN WILL BE
LESS INTENSE.

01:13:18.853 --> 01:13:20.897
AND IF HE DIES?

01:13:20.938 --> 01:13:22.690
WORST-CASE SCENARIO?

01:13:22.732 --> 01:13:26.610
WHEN HE WAKES UP,
HIS MIND IS COMPLETELY GONE.

01:13:26.652 --> 01:13:28.445
COBB...

01:13:28.487 --> 01:13:31.032
I'LL STILL HONOR
THE ARRANGEMENT.

01:13:31.074 --> 01:13:32.491
I APPRECIATE THAT, SAITO.

01:13:32.533 --> 01:13:34.410
BUT WHEN YOU WAKE UP,

01:13:34.451 --> 01:13:36.204
YOU WON'T EVEN REMEMBER
THAT WE <i>HAD</i> AN ARRANGEMENT.

01:13:36.246 --> 01:13:38.581
LIMBO IS GONNA BECOME
YOUR REALITY.

01:13:38.622 --> 01:13:40.791
YOU'RE GONNA BE LOST
DOWN THERE SO LONG

01:13:40.833 --> 01:13:42.877
THAT YOU'RE GONNA
BECOME AN OLD MAN.

01:13:42.919 --> 01:13:44.670
FILLED WITH REGRET?

01:13:44.712 --> 01:13:47.215
WAITING TO DIE ALONE.

01:13:47.257 --> 01:13:49.133
NO.

01:13:49.175 --> 01:13:51.177
I'LL COME BACK.

01:13:51.219 --> 01:13:54.555
AND WE'LL BE YOUNG MEN
TOGETHER AGAIN.

01:14:00.103 --> 01:14:01.687
BREATHE.

01:14:01.729 --> 01:14:03.147
THESE PEOPLE
ARE GONNA KILL US

01:14:03.189 --> 01:14:04.481
IF WE DON'T GIVE THEM
THE COMBINATION.

01:14:04.523 --> 01:14:05.858
THEY JUST
WANT TO RANSOM US.

01:14:05.900 --> 01:14:07.735
I <i>HEARD</i> THEM.

01:14:07.777 --> 01:14:09.404
THEY'RE GONNA LOCK US
IN THAT VAN,

01:14:09.445 --> 01:14:11.030
AND THEN DRIVE IT
INTO THE RIVER.

01:14:11.072 --> 01:14:12.656
ALL RIGHT.
WHAT IS IN THE SAFE?

01:14:12.698 --> 01:14:14.951
SOMETHING FOR YOU.

01:14:14.992 --> 01:14:16.452
MAURICE ALWAYS SAID

01:14:16.493 --> 01:14:19.705
IT WAS HIS MOST PRECIOUS GIFT
TO YOU--

01:14:19.747 --> 01:14:21.582
A WILL.

01:14:21.624 --> 01:14:23.334
MAURICE'S WILL
IS WITH PORT AND DUNN.

01:14:23.376 --> 01:14:25.002
THAT'S AN ALTERNATE.

01:14:25.044 --> 01:14:27.463
THIS WOULD SUPERSEDE THE OTHER
IF YOU WANT IT TO.

01:14:27.504 --> 01:14:30.258
IT SPLITS UP THE COMPONENT
BUSINESSES OF FISCHER MORROW.

01:14:30.300 --> 01:14:34.137
IT'D BE THE END OF THE ENTIRE
EMPIRE AS WE KNOW IT.

01:14:34.178 --> 01:14:37.390
DESTROYING
MY WHOLE INHERITANCE.

01:14:37.432 --> 01:14:40.059
WHY WOULD HE SUGGEST
SUCH A THING?

01:14:40.101 --> 01:14:41.560
I JUST DON'T KNOW.

01:14:43.646 --> 01:14:46.482
HE LOVED YOU, ROBERT.

01:14:46.523 --> 01:14:48.109
IN HIS OWN WAY.

01:14:48.151 --> 01:14:50.903
"IN HIS OWN WAY"?

01:14:50.945 --> 01:14:53.530
AT THE END...

01:14:53.572 --> 01:14:56.409
HE CALLED ME IN
TO HIS DEATHBED.

01:14:56.451 --> 01:14:59.245
HE COULD BARELY SPEAK.

01:14:59.287 --> 01:15:04.334
BUT HE TOOK THE TROUBLE
TO TELL ME ONE LAST THING.

01:15:06.043 --> 01:15:08.504
HE PULLED ME CLOSE.

01:15:10.340 --> 01:15:14.010
AND I COULD ONLY
MAKE OUT...

01:15:14.051 --> 01:15:15.761
ONE WORD.

01:15:18.555 --> 01:15:21.851
"DISAPPOINTED."

01:15:26.939 --> 01:15:28.232
WHEN WERE YOU IN LIMBO?

01:15:29.733 --> 01:15:31.610
YOU MIGHT HAVE THE REST
OF THE TEAM CONVINCED

01:15:31.652 --> 01:15:32.862
TO CARRY ON
WITH THIS JOB,

01:15:32.903 --> 01:15:34.238
BUT THEY DON'T KNOW
THE TRUTH.

01:15:34.280 --> 01:15:35.656
TRUTH? WHAT TRUTH?

01:15:35.698 --> 01:15:37.783
THE TRUTH THAT,
AT ANY MINUTE,

01:15:37.825 --> 01:15:40.036
YOU MIGHT BRING A FREIGHT TRAIN
THROUGH THE WALL.

01:15:40.077 --> 01:15:44.457
THE TRUTH THAT MAL IS BURSTING
THROUGH YOUR SUBCONSCIOUS.

01:15:44.499 --> 01:15:47.043
AND THE TRUTH THAT,
AS WE GO DEEPER INTO FISCHER,

01:15:47.084 --> 01:15:49.003
WE'RE ALSO GOING DEEPER
INTO YOU.

01:15:49.045 --> 01:15:53.049
AND...I'M NOT SURE
WE'RE GONNA LIKE WHAT WE FIND.

01:15:56.219 --> 01:15:57.928
WE WERE WORKING TOGETHER.

01:15:57.970 --> 01:16:01.391
WE WERE EXPLORING THE CONCEPT
OF A DREAM WITHIN A DREAM.

01:16:01.432 --> 01:16:02.850
I KEPT PUSHING THINGS.

01:16:02.892 --> 01:16:05.144
I WANTED TO GO DEEPER
AND DEEPER.

01:16:05.186 --> 01:16:07.021
I WANTED TO GO...FURTHER.

01:16:07.063 --> 01:16:09.815
I JUST DIDN'T UNDERSTAND
THE CONCEPT

01:16:09.857 --> 01:16:12.735
THAT HOURS COULD TURN
INTO YEARS DOWN THERE,

01:16:12.776 --> 01:16:16.072
THAT WE COULD GET TRAPPED
SO DEEP THAT WHEN WE...

01:16:16.113 --> 01:16:20.993
WHEN WE WOUND UP ON THE SHORE
OF OUR OWN SUBCONSCIOUS,

01:16:21.035 --> 01:16:23.579
WE LOST SIGHT
OF WHAT WAS REAL.

01:16:28.584 --> 01:16:31.921
WE CREATED, WE BUILT THE WORLD
FOR OURSELVES.

01:16:31.962 --> 01:16:36.509
WE DID THAT FOR YEARS.

01:16:36.551 --> 01:16:39.845
WE BUILT OUR <i>OWN</i> WORLD.

01:16:39.887 --> 01:16:41.722
HOW LONG
WERE YOU STUCK THERE?

01:16:41.764 --> 01:16:45.560
SOMETHING LIKE 50 YEARS.

01:16:47.686 --> 01:16:50.856
JESUS.

01:16:50.898 --> 01:16:53.192
HOW COULD YOU STAND IT?

01:16:53.234 --> 01:16:56.737
IT WASN'T SO BAD AT FIRST,
FEELING LIKE GODS.

01:16:56.779 --> 01:16:59.407
THE PROBLEM WAS KNOWING
THAT NONE OF IT WAS REAL.

01:16:59.449 --> 01:17:01.867
EVENTUALLY,
IT JUST BECAME IMPOSSIBLE

01:17:01.909 --> 01:17:03.869
FOR ME TO LIVE LIKE THAT.

01:17:03.911 --> 01:17:05.413
AND WHAT ABOUT FOR HER?

01:17:07.248 --> 01:17:10.209
SHE HAD LOCKED
SOMETHING AWAY,

01:17:10.251 --> 01:17:14.046
SOMETHING
DEEP INSIDE HER.

01:17:14.088 --> 01:17:17.341
A TRUTH THAT SHE HAD
ONCE KNOWN, BUT...

01:17:17.383 --> 01:17:19.302
BUT CHOSE TO FORGET.

01:17:22.054 --> 01:17:25.724
LIMBO BECAME HER REALITY.

01:17:25.766 --> 01:17:28.018
WHAT HAPPENED
WHEN YOU WOKE UP?

01:17:28.060 --> 01:17:29.812
WELL, TO WAKE UP
FROM THAT

01:17:29.853 --> 01:17:32.231
AFTER-- AFTER YEARS,
AFTER DECADES...

01:17:32.273 --> 01:17:35.318
TO BECOME OLD SOULS

01:17:35.359 --> 01:17:37.736
THROWN BACK INTO YOUTH
LIKE THAT?

01:17:37.778 --> 01:17:40.239
I KNEW SOMETHING WAS WRONG
WITH HER.

01:17:40.281 --> 01:17:43.493
SHE JUST
WOULDN'T ADMIT IT.

01:17:43.534 --> 01:17:46.370
EVENTUALLY,
SHE TOLD ME THE TRUTH.

01:17:46.412 --> 01:17:49.915
SHE WAS POSSESSED
BY AN IDEA--

01:17:49.957 --> 01:17:55.963
THIS ONE VERY SIMPLE IDEA
THAT CHANGED EVERYTHING.

01:17:56.005 --> 01:17:59.258
THAT OUR WORLD
WASN'T REAL.

01:17:59.300 --> 01:18:03.053
THAT SHE NEEDED TO WAKE UP
TO COME BACK TO REALITY,

01:18:03.095 --> 01:18:04.555
THAT...

01:18:04.597 --> 01:18:07.683
IN ORDER
TO GET BACK HOME...

01:18:07.724 --> 01:18:10.060
WE HAD TO KILL OURSELVES.

01:18:16.400 --> 01:18:18.735
WHAT ABOUT YOUR CHILDREN?

01:18:18.777 --> 01:18:20.530
SHE THOUGHT
THEY WERE PROJECTIONS,

01:18:20.571 --> 01:18:22.406
THAT OUR REAL CHILDREN
WERE WAITING FOR US

01:18:22.448 --> 01:18:23.658
UP THERE SOMEWHERE.

01:18:23.699 --> 01:18:24.908
I'M THEIR MOTHER!

01:18:24.950 --> 01:18:26.369
CALM DOWN.

01:18:26.410 --> 01:18:27.911
DON'T YOU THINK
I CAN TELL THE DIFFERENCE?

01:18:27.953 --> 01:18:29.539
IF THIS IS MY DREAM,
WHY CAN'T I CONTROL THIS?

01:18:29.580 --> 01:18:31.165
BECAUSE YOU DON'T KNOW
YOU'RE DREAMING!

01:18:31.207 --> 01:18:33.792
SHE WAS CERTAIN THERE WAS
NOTHING I COULD DO,

01:18:33.834 --> 01:18:35.461
NO MATTER HOW MUCH
I BEGGED,

01:18:35.503 --> 01:18:37.630
NO MATTER HOW MUCH
I PLEADED.

01:18:39.923 --> 01:18:43.886
SHE WANTED TO DO IT,
BUT SHE COULD NOT DO IT ALONE.

01:18:43.927 --> 01:18:46.514
SHE LOVED ME TOO MUCH,
SO...

01:18:46.556 --> 01:18:50.518
SHE CAME UP WITH A PLAN
ON OUR ANNIVERSARY.

01:19:15.959 --> 01:19:17.920
SWEETHEART,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

01:19:17.961 --> 01:19:19.922
JOIN ME.

01:19:19.963 --> 01:19:22.216
JUST-- JUST STEP BACK INSIDE.
ALL RIGHT?

01:19:22.258 --> 01:19:23.842
JUST STEP BACK INSIDE NOW.
COME ON.

01:19:23.884 --> 01:19:25.553
NO.

01:19:25.595 --> 01:19:28.180
I'M GOING TO JUMP,
AND YOU'RE COMING WITH ME.

01:19:28.222 --> 01:19:30.224
NO, I'M NOT.

01:19:30.266 --> 01:19:32.184
N-NOW, YOU LISTEN TO ME.

01:19:32.226 --> 01:19:35.605
IF YOU JUMP, YOU'RE NOT
GONNA WAKE UP, REMEMBER?

01:19:35.646 --> 01:19:36.939
YOU'RE GONNA DIE.

01:19:36.980 --> 01:19:39.191
NOW, JUST--
JUST STEP BACK INSIDE.

01:19:39.233 --> 01:19:40.901
COME ON.

01:19:40.943 --> 01:19:42.903
STEP BACK INSIDE
SO WE CAN TALK ABOUT THIS.

01:19:42.945 --> 01:19:45.364
WE'VE TALKED ENOUGH.

01:19:46.156 --> 01:19:47.617
MAL.

01:19:47.658 --> 01:19:49.952
COME OUT ONTO THE LEDGE,
OR I'LL JUMP RIGHT NOW.

01:19:49.993 --> 01:19:51.245
OKAY.

01:19:54.123 --> 01:19:57.543
WE'RE GONNA TALK ABOUT THIS.

01:19:57.585 --> 01:19:59.253
ALL RIGHT?

01:19:59.295 --> 01:20:02.172
I'M ASKING YOU
TO TAKE A LEAP OF FAITH.

01:20:02.214 --> 01:20:04.425
NO, HONEY.

01:20:04.467 --> 01:20:06.761
NO, I CA--

01:20:06.802 --> 01:20:08.887
YOU KNOW I CAN'T DO THAT.

01:20:08.929 --> 01:20:11.432
TAKE A SECOND,
THINK ABOUT OUR CHILDREN.

01:20:11.474 --> 01:20:14.435
THINK ABOUT JAMES.

01:20:14.477 --> 01:20:16.061
THINK ABOUT PHILLIPA NOW.

01:20:16.103 --> 01:20:18.773
IF I GO WITHOUT YOU,
THEY'LL TAKE THEM AWAY ANYWAY.

01:20:18.814 --> 01:20:20.441
WHAT DOES <i>THAT</i> MEAN?

01:20:20.483 --> 01:20:22.276
I FILED A LETTER
WITH OUR ATTORNEY,

01:20:22.318 --> 01:20:25.362
EXPLAINING HOW I'M FEARFUL
FOR MY SAFETY.

01:20:28.532 --> 01:20:30.326
HOW YOU'VE THREATENED
TO KILL ME.

01:20:32.995 --> 01:20:34.371
WHY DID YOU DO THIS?

01:20:34.413 --> 01:20:35.831
I LOVE YOU, DOM.

01:20:35.872 --> 01:20:38.542
WHY DID YOU--
WHY WOULD YOU DO THIS TO ME?

01:20:38.584 --> 01:20:40.795
I'VE FREED YOU FROM THE GUILT
OF CHOOSING TO LEAVE THEM.

01:20:40.836 --> 01:20:44.006
WE'RE GOING HOME
TO OUR <i>REAL</i> CHILDREN.

01:20:44.047 --> 01:20:46.258
OH, NO, NO, NO. MAL,
YOU LISTEN TO ME, ALL RIGHT?

01:20:46.300 --> 01:20:47.677
MAL, LOOK AT ME,
PLEASE?!

01:20:47.718 --> 01:20:49.261
YOU'RE WAITING
FOR A TRAIN.

01:20:49.303 --> 01:20:51.096
MAL, GODDAMN IT,
DON'T DO THIS!

01:20:51.138 --> 01:20:53.766
A TRAIN THAT WILL TAKE YOU
FAR AWAY.

01:20:53.808 --> 01:20:55.934
JAMES AND PHILLIPA
ARE WAITING FOR US!

01:20:55.976 --> 01:20:57.728
YOU KNOW WHERE YOU HOPE
THIS TRAIN WILL TAKE YOU.

01:20:57.770 --> 01:20:58.521
THEY'RE WAITING FOR US!

01:20:58.562 --> 01:20:59.480
YOU CAN'T KNOW FOR SURE.

01:20:59.522 --> 01:21:00.856
MAL, LOOK AT ME!

01:21:00.897 --> 01:21:01.982
BUT IT DOESN'T MATTER.

01:21:02.024 --> 01:21:03.442
MAL, GODDAMN IT!

01:21:03.484 --> 01:21:04.610
BECAUSE YOU'LL BE TOGETHER.

01:21:04.652 --> 01:21:05.486
MAL, LISTEN TO ME!

01:21:05.528 --> 01:21:07.613
SWEETHEART!
LOOK AT ME!

01:21:07.655 --> 01:21:09.281
MAL, NO!!

01:21:09.323 --> 01:21:10.825
JESUS CHRIST!

01:21:14.662 --> 01:21:16.079
SHE HAD HERSELF
DECLARED SANE

01:21:16.121 --> 01:21:17.623
BY THREE DIFFERENT
PSYCHIATRISTS.

01:21:17.665 --> 01:21:19.333
IT MADE IT IMPOSSIBLE

01:21:19.375 --> 01:21:21.918
FOR ME TO TRY TO EXPLAIN
THE NATURE OF HER MADNESS.

01:21:21.960 --> 01:21:23.879
SO, I RAN.

01:21:25.172 --> 01:21:27.883
RIGHT NOW...
OR NEVER, COBB.

01:21:33.930 --> 01:21:36.392
JAMES! PHILLIPA!

01:21:36.433 --> 01:21:38.644
COME ON IN! COME ON!

01:21:38.686 --> 01:21:40.270
ALL RIGHT, LET'S GO.

01:21:40.312 --> 01:21:42.398
I LEFT
MY CHILDREN BEHIND,

01:21:42.439 --> 01:21:44.608
AND I'VE BEEN TRYING TO BUY
MY WAY BACK EVER SINCE.

01:21:44.650 --> 01:21:47.152
YOUR GUILT DEFINES HER.

01:21:47.194 --> 01:21:49.071
IT'S WHAT POWERS HER.

01:21:49.112 --> 01:21:52.533
BUT YOU ARE NOT RESPONSIBLE
FOR THE IDEA THAT DESTROYED HER.

01:21:52.575 --> 01:21:56.328
AND IF WE ARE GONNA SUCCEED
IN THIS...

01:21:56.370 --> 01:21:58.706
YOU HAVE
TO FORGIVE YOURSELF...

01:21:58.748 --> 01:22:01.458
AND YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
TO CONFRONT HER.

01:22:01.500 --> 01:22:03.168
BUT YOU DON'T HAVE
TO DO THAT ALONE.

01:22:03.210 --> 01:22:04.461
NO, NO, YOU'RE NOT--

01:22:04.503 --> 01:22:05.962
I'M DOING IT
FOR THE OTHERS.

01:22:06.004 --> 01:22:09.425
BECAUSE THEY HAVE NO IDEA
THE RISK THEY'VE TAKEN

01:22:09.466 --> 01:22:11.635
COMING DOWN HERE
WITH YOU.

01:22:16.014 --> 01:22:17.474
WE HAVE TO MOVE.

01:22:17.516 --> 01:22:19.476
TIME'S UP.

01:22:19.518 --> 01:22:21.687
ALL RIGHT.
I DON'T KNOW ANY COMBINATION.

01:22:21.729 --> 01:22:23.021
NOT CONSCIOUSLY, ANYWAY.

01:22:23.063 --> 01:22:24.774
HOW ABOUT INSTINCTIVELY,
HUH?

01:22:24.815 --> 01:22:27.735
I GOT SOMEBODY STANDING IN
YOUR FATHER'S OFFICE RIGHT NOW

01:22:27.777 --> 01:22:29.570
READY TO TAP IN
THE COMBINATION.

01:22:29.612 --> 01:22:31.280
GIVE ME
THE FIRST SIX NUMBERS

01:22:31.321 --> 01:22:33.198
THAT COME TO YOUR HEAD
RIGHT NOW.

01:22:33.240 --> 01:22:35.785
I HAVE NO IDEA.
RIGHT NOW!

01:22:35.826 --> 01:22:38.161
I SAID, RIGHT NOW!
RIGHT NOW!

01:22:38.203 --> 01:22:40.539
FIVE, TWO, EIGHT...

01:22:40.581 --> 01:22:42.040
FOUR, NINE, ONE.

01:22:44.126 --> 01:22:47.087
YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
TO DO BETTER THAN THAT.

01:22:47.129 --> 01:22:49.465
ALL RIGHT. BAG 'EM.

01:22:49.506 --> 01:22:51.467
YOU'RE GOING FOR A RIDE.

01:22:55.471 --> 01:22:57.598
WE'RE WORTH
MORE TO YOU ALIVE.

01:22:57.640 --> 01:22:59.683
YOU HEAR ME?

01:23:04.104 --> 01:23:05.439
WHAT'D YOU GET?

01:23:07.149 --> 01:23:08.484
THAT BOY'S RELATIONSHIP
WITH HIS FATHER

01:23:08.525 --> 01:23:09.735
IS EVEN WORSE
THAN WE IMAGINED.

01:23:09.777 --> 01:23:11.111
THIS HELPS US HOW?

01:23:11.153 --> 01:23:12.571
THE STRONGER THE ISSUES,

01:23:12.613 --> 01:23:14.740
THE MORE POWERFUL
THE CATHARSIS.

01:23:14.782 --> 01:23:17.534
HOW ARE WE GONNA RECONCILE THEM
IF THEY'RE SO ESTRANGED?

01:23:17.576 --> 01:23:19.495
WELL, I'M WORKING ON THAT,
AREN'T I?
WORK FASTER.

01:23:19.536 --> 01:23:21.914
THE PROJECTIONS
ARE CLOSING IN QUICK.

01:23:21.956 --> 01:23:25.292
WE GOTTA BREAK OUT OF HERE
BEFORE WE'RE TOTALLY BOXED IN.

01:24:01.411 --> 01:24:05.207
WE MUSTN'T BE AFRAID TO DREAM
A LITTLE BIGGER, DARLING.

01:24:21.264 --> 01:24:23.225
NOW WE NEED TO SHIFT HIS
ANIMOSITY FROM HIS FATHER

01:24:23.266 --> 01:24:25.019
TO HIS GODFATHER.

01:24:25.060 --> 01:24:26.729
YOU'RE GONNA DESTROY HIS <i>ONE</i>
POSITIVE RELATIONSHIP?

01:24:26.770 --> 01:24:28.981
NO, WE REPAIR HIS RELATIONSHIP
WITH HIS FATHER

01:24:29.023 --> 01:24:31.149
WHILST EXPOSING
HIS GODFATHER'S TRUE NATURE.

01:24:31.191 --> 01:24:34.110
WE SHOULD CHARGE FISCHER
A LOT MORE THAN SAITO
FOR <i>THIS</i> JOB.

01:24:34.152 --> 01:24:36.030
WHAT ABOUT HIS SECURITY?

01:24:36.071 --> 01:24:37.531
IT'S GONNA GET WORSE
AS WE GO DEEPER.

01:24:37.573 --> 01:24:39.992
I THINK WE RUN
WITH MR. CHARLES.
NO.

01:24:40.034 --> 01:24:41.410
WHO'S MR. CHARLES?

01:24:41.451 --> 01:24:42.411
BAD IDEA.

01:24:42.452 --> 01:24:43.537
THE SECOND WE GET
INTO THAT HOTEL

01:24:43.579 --> 01:24:44.580
AND APPROACH FISCHER,

01:24:44.621 --> 01:24:45.998
HIS SECURITY
IS GONNA BE ALL OVER US.

01:24:46.040 --> 01:24:48.166
WE RUN WITH MR. CHARLES
LIKE WE DID ON THE STEIN JOB.

01:24:48.208 --> 01:24:50.293
SO YOU'VE DONE IT BEFORE?
YEAH, AND IT DIDN'T WORK!

01:24:50.335 --> 01:24:52.087
THE SUBJECT REALIZED
HE WAS DREAMING,

01:24:52.128 --> 01:24:53.964
AND HIS SUBCONSCIOUS
TORE US TO PIECES.

01:24:54.006 --> 01:24:56.174
EXCELLENT.
BUT YOU LEARNED A LOT, RIGHT?

01:24:56.216 --> 01:24:58.134
I'M GONNA NEED
SOME KIND OF DISTRACTION.
NO PROBLEM.

01:24:58.176 --> 01:25:00.804
HOW ABOUT A LOVELY LADY
WHO I'VE USED BEFORE?

01:25:00.846 --> 01:25:02.932
LISTEN TO ME. YOU DRIVE
CAREFULLY, ALL RIGHT?
YEAH.

01:25:02.973 --> 01:25:05.642
EVERYTHING DOWN THERE
IS GONNA BE UNSTABLE AS HELL.

01:25:09.479 --> 01:25:11.440
DON'T JUMP TOO SOON.

01:25:11.481 --> 01:25:13.275
WE ONLY GOT ONE SHOT AT
THAT KICK. WE GOTTA MAKE IT.

01:25:13.316 --> 01:25:14.902
I'LL PLAY THE MUSIC
TO LET YOU KNOW IT'S COMING.

01:25:14.944 --> 01:25:17.071
THE REST IS ON YOU.

01:25:17.112 --> 01:25:18.196
YOU READY?
READY!

01:25:20.156 --> 01:25:21.366
SWEET DREAMS.

01:25:21.408 --> 01:25:23.911
AM I BORING YOU?

01:25:23.953 --> 01:25:25.495
I WAS TELLING YOU
MY STORY.

01:25:25.537 --> 01:25:27.957
I GUESS IT WASN'T
TO YOUR LIKING.

01:25:27.998 --> 01:25:29.750
UH...

01:25:29.792 --> 01:25:32.461
UM, I HAVE A LOT
ON MY MIND.

01:25:32.502 --> 01:25:35.547
THERE GOES MR. CHARLES.

01:25:39.927 --> 01:25:42.930
MR. FISCHER, RIGHT?

01:25:42.972 --> 01:25:45.557
PLEASURE TO SEE YOU AGAIN.
ROD GREEN FROM MARKETING.

01:25:45.599 --> 01:25:47.350
I...HMM.

01:25:47.392 --> 01:25:48.644
AND YOU MUST BE?

01:25:48.685 --> 01:25:49.895
LEAVING.

01:25:53.649 --> 01:25:55.067
IN CASE YOU GET BORED.

01:26:00.114 --> 01:26:01.698
SHE MUST'VE BLOWN YOU OFF.

01:26:01.740 --> 01:26:03.283
THAT IS,
UNLESS HER PHONE NUMBER

01:26:03.325 --> 01:26:04.576
REALLY <i>IS</i> ONLY SIX DIGITS.

01:26:05.786 --> 01:26:07.997
FUNNY WAY TO MAKE FRIENDS,

01:26:08.038 --> 01:26:10.540
SOMEONE STEALING YOUR WALLET
LIKE THAT.

01:26:15.420 --> 01:26:17.255
GODDAMN IT. THE WALLET ALONE
IS WORTH AT LEAST FIVE--

01:26:17.297 --> 01:26:18.590
ABOUT $500, RIGHT?

01:26:18.632 --> 01:26:20.009
LISTEN,
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.

01:26:20.050 --> 01:26:21.927
MY PEOPLE ARE ALREADY ON IT,
AS WE SPEAK.

01:26:21.969 --> 01:26:23.804
WHO OR WHAT
IS MR. CHARLES?

01:26:23.846 --> 01:26:26.473
IT'S A GAMBIT
DESIGNED TO TURN FISCHER

01:26:26.515 --> 01:26:28.183
AGAINST
HIS OWN SUBCONSCIOUS.

01:26:28.224 --> 01:26:29.977
AND WHY
DON'T YOU APPROVE?

01:26:30.019 --> 01:26:31.728
BECAUSE IT INVOLVES TELLING
THE MARK THAT HE'S DREAMING,

01:26:31.770 --> 01:26:34.272
WHICH INVOLVES ATTRACTING
A LOT OF ATTENTION TO US.

01:26:34.314 --> 01:26:36.066
DIDN'T COBB SAY
NEVER TO DO THAT?

01:26:36.108 --> 01:26:38.276
MM. SO NOW YOU'VE NOTICED
HOW MUCH TIME

01:26:38.318 --> 01:26:40.612
COBB SPENDS DOING THINGS
HE SAYS NEVER TO DO.

01:26:43.406 --> 01:26:45.241
MR. SAITO,
CAN I HAVE A MOMENT?

01:26:45.283 --> 01:26:46.660
I-I'M SORRY, BUT...

01:26:46.702 --> 01:26:47.870
HOLD ON! WAIT!

01:26:47.911 --> 01:26:50.497
YOU LOOK A BIT PERKIER.

01:26:50.539 --> 01:26:52.958
VERY AMUSING, MR. EAMES.

01:26:59.089 --> 01:27:00.883
TURBULENCE ON THE PLANE?

01:27:00.924 --> 01:27:02.592
NO, IT'S MUCH CLOSER.

01:27:02.634 --> 01:27:04.427
THAT'S YUSUF'S DRIVING.

01:27:12.186 --> 01:27:14.646
UH, I'M SORRY.
WHO DID YOU SAY YOU WERE?

01:27:14.688 --> 01:27:16.690
ROD GREEN
FROM MARKETING.

01:27:16.732 --> 01:27:19.234
BUT THAT'S NOT TRUE AT ALL,
IS IT?

01:27:20.652 --> 01:27:24.114
MY NAME IS MR. CHARLES.
YOU REMEMBER ME, DON'T YOU?

01:27:24.156 --> 01:27:26.992
I'M THE HEAD OF YOUR SECURITY
DOWN HERE.

01:27:28.160 --> 01:27:30.079
GET OUT ON A DIFFERENT FLOOR
AND KEEP MOVING.

01:27:30.120 --> 01:27:31.454
DUMP THE WALLET.

01:27:31.496 --> 01:27:33.165
SECURITY WILL BE
LOOKING FOR THAT.

01:27:33.207 --> 01:27:34.332
OKAY.

01:27:34.374 --> 01:27:36.126
WE NEED TO BUY COBB
A LITTLE MORE TIME.

01:27:39.922 --> 01:27:43.217
SECURITY, HUH?

01:27:43.258 --> 01:27:45.177
YOU WORK FOR THE HOTEL?

01:27:45.219 --> 01:27:46.803
NO, NO.

01:27:46.845 --> 01:27:50.473
I SPECIALIZE IN A VERY
SPECIFIC TYPE OF SECURITY.

01:27:50.515 --> 01:27:53.060
SUBCONSCIOUS SECURITY.

01:27:53.102 --> 01:27:55.311
YOU'RE TALKING
ABOUT DREAMS?

01:27:55.353 --> 01:27:57.064
ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT,
UM...

01:27:57.106 --> 01:27:58.356
EXTRACTION?

01:27:58.398 --> 01:28:01.359
I AM HERE TO PROTECT YOU.
YOU...

01:28:13.496 --> 01:28:16.792
MR. FISCHER, I'M HERE TO
PROTECT YOU IN THE EVENT

01:28:16.833 --> 01:28:19.795
THAT SOMEONE TRIES TO ACCESS
YOUR MIND THROUGH YOUR DREAMS.

01:28:19.836 --> 01:28:23.132
YOU'RE <i>NOT</i> SAFE HERE.

01:28:23.173 --> 01:28:25.508
THEY'RE COMING FOR YOU.

01:28:37.729 --> 01:28:39.314
OHH!

01:28:43.359 --> 01:28:45.904
STRANGE WEATHER,
ISN'T IT?

01:28:49.741 --> 01:28:51.868
YOU FEEL THAT?

01:28:53.411 --> 01:28:54.997
WHAT'S HAPPENING?

01:28:55.038 --> 01:28:56.414
COBB IS DRAWING
FISCHER'S ATTENTION

01:28:56.456 --> 01:28:57.749
TO THE STRANGENESS
OF THE DREAM,

01:28:57.791 --> 01:28:59.417
WHICH IS MAKING
HIS SUBCONSCIOUS

01:28:59.459 --> 01:29:00.961
LOOK FOR THE DREAMER.

01:29:01.003 --> 01:29:02.462
FOR ME.

01:29:02.504 --> 01:29:04.006
QUICK, GIVE ME A KISS.

01:29:08.969 --> 01:29:11.387
THEY'RE STILL
LOOKING AT US.

01:29:11.429 --> 01:29:13.723
YEAH,
IT WAS WORTH A SHOT.

01:29:13.765 --> 01:29:15.851
WE SHOULD PROBABLY
GET OUT OF HERE.

01:29:30.032 --> 01:29:32.408
YOU FEEL THAT?

01:29:32.450 --> 01:29:35.204
YOU'VE ACTUALLY BEEN TRAINED
FOR THIS, MR. FISCHER.

01:29:35.245 --> 01:29:37.956
PAY ATTENTION TO THE STRANGENESS
OF THE WEATHER...

01:29:37.998 --> 01:29:39.374
THE SHIFT IN GRAVITY.

01:29:39.415 --> 01:29:41.210
NONE OF THIS IS REAL.

01:29:41.251 --> 01:29:42.669
YOU'RE IN A DREAM.

01:29:46.673 --> 01:29:49.509
NOW, THE EASIEST WAY FOR YOU
TO TEST YOURSELF

01:29:49.551 --> 01:29:52.137
IS TO TRY AND REMEMBER
HOW YOU ARRIVED AT THIS HOTEL.

01:29:52.179 --> 01:29:53.889
CAN YOU DO THAT?

01:29:53.930 --> 01:29:56.141
YEAH, I, I...

01:29:56.183 --> 01:29:58.518
NOW, BREATHE, BREATHE.
REMEMBER YOUR TRAINING.

01:29:58.560 --> 01:30:00.603
ACCEPT THE FACT
THAT YOU'RE IN A DREAM,

01:30:00.645 --> 01:30:02.189
AND I'M HERE
TO PROTECT YOU.

01:30:02.231 --> 01:30:03.648
GO ON.

01:30:05.650 --> 01:30:07.277
MM-HMM.

01:30:09.445 --> 01:30:12.199
YOU'RE NOT REAL?

01:30:12.241 --> 01:30:13.658
NO, NO.

01:30:13.700 --> 01:30:15.327
I'M A PROJECTION
OF YOUR SUBCONSCIOUS.

01:30:15.369 --> 01:30:16.745
I WAS SENT HERE
TO PROTECT YOU

01:30:16.786 --> 01:30:18.621
IN THE EVENT
THAT EXTRACTORS

01:30:18.663 --> 01:30:20.623
TRIED TO PULL YOU
INTO A DREAM.

01:30:20.665 --> 01:30:24.460
AND I BELIEVE THAT'S WHAT'S
GOING ON RIGHT NOW, MR. FISCHER.

01:30:24.502 --> 01:30:26.004
YEAH.

01:30:26.046 --> 01:30:28.090
OKAY.

01:30:28.131 --> 01:30:31.218
OKAY.

01:30:32.719 --> 01:30:34.012
CAN YOU GET ME
OUT OF HERE?

01:30:35.638 --> 01:30:37.224
RIGHT AWAY.

01:30:37.266 --> 01:30:38.308
FOLLOW ME.

01:30:52.446 --> 01:30:53.865
HOLD ON A SECOND!

01:30:58.703 --> 01:31:00.663
JESUS CHRIST!
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?!

01:31:00.705 --> 01:31:03.125
THESE MEN WERE SENT HERE
TO ABDUCT YOU, ALL RIGHT?

01:31:03.166 --> 01:31:05.752
IF YOU WANT MY HELP,
YOU HAVE TO REMAIN CALM.

01:31:06.920 --> 01:31:09.839
I NEED YOU TO WORK WITH ME,
MR. FISCHER.

01:31:20.976 --> 01:31:22.518
IF THIS IS A DREAM,

01:31:22.560 --> 01:31:24.896
I SHOULD JUST KILL MYSELF
TO WAKE UP, RIGHT?

01:31:24.938 --> 01:31:27.481
I WOULDN'T DO THAT
IF I WERE YOU, MR. FISCHER.

01:31:27.523 --> 01:31:29.067
I BELIEVE
THEY HAVE YOU SEDATED,

01:31:29.109 --> 01:31:30.610
AND IF YOU PULL
THAT TRIGGER...

01:31:30.652 --> 01:31:32.486
YOU MAY NOT WAKE UP.

01:31:32.528 --> 01:31:35.240
YOU MAY GO
INTO A FURTHER DREAM STATE.

01:31:35.282 --> 01:31:37.909
NOW, YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M TALKING ABOUT.

01:31:37.951 --> 01:31:41.913
YOU REMEMBER THE TRAINING.

01:31:41.955 --> 01:31:44.458
REMEMBER WHAT I SAID
TO YOU.

01:31:44.498 --> 01:31:46.460
GIVE ME THE GUN.

01:31:58.180 --> 01:31:59.639
THIS ROOM
SHOULD BE DIRECTLY BELOW 528?

01:31:59.681 --> 01:32:01.766
YEAH.

01:32:10.150 --> 01:32:12.694
THINK, MR. FISCHER,
THINK.

01:32:12.735 --> 01:32:15.071
WHAT DO YOU REMEMBER
FROM BEFORE THIS DREAM?

01:32:15.113 --> 01:32:16.865
UH...THERE WAS, UM...

01:32:16.906 --> 01:32:18.616
THERE WAS A LOT
OF GUNFIRE.

01:32:18.658 --> 01:32:21.244
THERE WAS...RAIN.

01:32:21.286 --> 01:32:23.705
UNCLE PETER.

01:32:23.746 --> 01:32:25.665
OH, MY GOD,
WE'VE BEEN KIDNAPPED.

01:32:25.707 --> 01:32:27.167
WHERE WERE THEY
HOLDING YOU?

01:32:27.209 --> 01:32:29.669
UH...

01:32:29.711 --> 01:32:32.088
THEY HAD US IN THE
BACK OF A VAN.

01:32:32.130 --> 01:32:33.798
THAT EXPLAINS
THE GRAVITY SHIFTS.

01:32:33.840 --> 01:32:36.176
YOU'RE IN THE BACK OF A VAN
RIGHT NOW. KEEP GOING.

01:32:36.218 --> 01:32:38.803
IT HAD SOMETHING TO DO
WITH, UM...

01:32:38.845 --> 01:32:42.349
SOMETHING TO DO
WITH A...A SAFE?

01:32:42.391 --> 01:32:44.393
GOD, WHY IS IT SO HARD
TO REMEMBER?

01:32:44.434 --> 01:32:47.479
IT'S LIKE TRYING TO REMEMBER
A DREAM AFTER YOU'VE WOKEN UP.

01:32:47.521 --> 01:32:49.523
LISTEN,
IT TAKES YEARS OF PRACTICE.

01:32:49.563 --> 01:32:52.150
YOU AND BROWNING HAVE BEEN
PULLED INTO THIS DREAM

01:32:52.192 --> 01:32:54.652
BECAUSE THEY'RE TRYING TO STEAL
SOMETHING FROM YOUR MIND.

01:32:54.694 --> 01:32:58.365
I NEED YOU TO FOCUS AND TRY
AND REMEMBER WHAT THAT IS.

01:32:58.407 --> 01:32:59.908
WHAT IS IT, MR. FISCHER?
THINK!

01:32:59.949 --> 01:33:01.701
OH, A C-COMBINATION.

01:33:01.743 --> 01:33:04.246
THEY DEMANDED THE FIRST NUMBERS
TO POP INTO MY HEAD.

01:33:04.287 --> 01:33:06.998
THEY'RE TRYING TO EXTRACT A
NUMBER FROM YOUR SUBCONSCIOUS.

01:33:07.040 --> 01:33:08.624
IT CAN REPRESENT
ANYTHING.

01:33:08.666 --> 01:33:11.002
WE'RE IN A HOTEL
RIGHT NOW.

01:33:11.044 --> 01:33:12.586
WE SHOULD TRY HOTEL ROOMS.

01:33:12.628 --> 01:33:14.714
WHAT WAS THE NUMBER,
MR. FISCHER?

01:33:14.756 --> 01:33:17.591
TRY AND REMEMBER FOR ME.
THIS IS VERY IMPORTANT.

01:33:17.633 --> 01:33:19.386
FIVE.

01:33:19.428 --> 01:33:22.347
FIVE, TWO...
IT WAS SOMETHING...

01:33:22.389 --> 01:33:25.058
IT WAS A LONG NUMBER.
WELL, THAT'S GOOD ENOUGH.
WE CAN START THERE. FIFTH FLOOR.

01:33:25.100 --> 01:33:26.268
YEP.

01:33:26.309 --> 01:33:27.601
SO DO YOU USE A TIMER?

01:33:27.643 --> 01:33:29.812
NO, I HAVE TO JUDGE IT
FOR MYSELF.

01:33:29.854 --> 01:33:32.065
WHILE YOU'RE ALL ASLEEP
IN 528,

01:33:32.107 --> 01:33:33.858
I WAIT FOR YUSUF'S KICK.

01:33:33.900 --> 01:33:36.236
WELL, HOW WILL YOU KNOW?
HIS MUSIC WARNS ME.

01:33:36.278 --> 01:33:38.780
AND THEN WHEN THE VAN HITS
THE BARRIER OF THE BRIDGE,

01:33:38.821 --> 01:33:40.323
THAT SHOULD BE
UNMISTAKABLE.

01:33:40.365 --> 01:33:43.410
SO WE GET A NICE,
SYNCHRONIZED KICK.

01:33:43.452 --> 01:33:46.455
IF IT'S TOO SOON,
WE WON'T GET PULLED OUT.

01:33:46.496 --> 01:33:49.707
BUT IF IT'S TOO LATE,
I WON'T BE ABLE TO DROP US.

01:33:49.749 --> 01:33:51.334
WELL, WHY NOT?

01:33:51.376 --> 01:33:53.420
'CAUSE THE VAN
WILL BE IN FREE FALL.

01:33:53.462 --> 01:33:55.671
CAN'T DROP YOU
WITHOUT GRAVITY.

01:33:55.713 --> 01:33:57.048
RIGHT.

01:34:01.928 --> 01:34:03.388
THEY'RE WITH ME.

01:34:03.430 --> 01:34:04.638
GO ON.

01:34:28.788 --> 01:34:30.290
MR. CHARLES.

01:34:30.332 --> 01:34:31.916
DO YOU KNOW WHAT THAT IS,
MR. FISCHER?

01:34:31.958 --> 01:34:33.460
YEAH, I-I THINK SO.
YEAH.

01:34:33.502 --> 01:34:35.378
THEY WERE TRYING
TO PUT YOU UNDER.

01:34:35.420 --> 01:34:37.172
I'M ALREADY UNDER.

01:34:37.213 --> 01:34:38.381
UNDER <i>AGAIN.</i>

01:34:38.423 --> 01:34:40.883
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
A DREAM WITHIN A DREAM?

01:34:40.925 --> 01:34:43.970
HEY.
I SEE YOU'VE CHANGED.

01:34:44.012 --> 01:34:46.097
I'M SORRY?

01:34:46.139 --> 01:34:48.766
OH, I'M SORRY.
I M-MISTOOK YOU FOR A FRIEND.

01:34:50.352 --> 01:34:53.062
WELL, GOOD-LOOKING FELLOW,
I'M SURE.

01:34:53.104 --> 01:34:54.356
AH.

01:34:54.397 --> 01:34:55.898
NO, NO, NO, NO.

01:34:55.940 --> 01:34:57.651
THAT'S FISCHER'S
PROJECTION OF BROWNING.

01:34:57.691 --> 01:34:59.361
LET'S FOLLOW HIM
AND SEE HOW HE BEHAVES.

01:34:59.402 --> 01:35:00.778
WHY?

01:35:00.820 --> 01:35:02.364
BECAUSE HOW HE ACTS
WILL TELL US

01:35:02.405 --> 01:35:03.906
IF FISCHER IS STARTING
TO SUSPECT HIS MOTIVES

01:35:03.948 --> 01:35:05.158
THE WAY WE WANT HIM TO.

01:35:05.200 --> 01:35:05.950
Shh!

01:35:10.121 --> 01:35:11.540
UNCLE PETER?

01:35:11.581 --> 01:35:13.625
YOU SAID YOU WERE
KIDNAPPED TOGETHER?

01:35:13.667 --> 01:35:16.252
WELL, N-NOT EXACTLY.
THEY-- THEY ALREADY HAD HIM.

01:35:16.294 --> 01:35:17.379
THEY WERE
TORTURING HIM.

01:35:17.420 --> 01:35:18.672
AND YOU <i>SAW</i> THEM
TORTURE HIM?

01:35:25.554 --> 01:35:28.097
THE KIDNAPPERS
ARE WORKING FOR YOU?

01:35:28.139 --> 01:35:30.475
OH, ROBERT.

01:35:30.517 --> 01:35:32.726
YOU'RE TRYING TO GET
THAT SAFE OPEN?

01:35:32.768 --> 01:35:34.479
TO GET
THE ALTERNATE WILL?

01:35:34.521 --> 01:35:37.106
FISCHER MORROW HAS BEEN
MY ENTIRE LIFE.

01:35:37.148 --> 01:35:39.108
I CAN'T LET YOU
DESTROY IT.

01:35:39.150 --> 01:35:41.653
I'M NOT GONNA THROW AWAY
MY INHERITANCE! WHY WOULD I?!

01:35:41.695 --> 01:35:45.990
I COULDN'T LET YOU RISE
TO YOUR FATHER'S LAST TAUNT.

01:35:46.032 --> 01:35:47.492
WHAT TAUNT?

01:35:47.534 --> 01:35:49.827
THE WILL, ROBERT.
THAT WILL?

01:35:49.869 --> 01:35:51.538
THAT'S HIS LAST INSULT.

01:35:51.580 --> 01:35:55.625
A CHALLENGE FOR YOU TO BUILD
SOMETHING FOR YOURSELF

01:35:55.667 --> 01:35:59.753
BY TELLING YOU YOU'RE NOT WORTHY
OF HIS ACCOMPLISHMENTS.

01:36:05.176 --> 01:36:08.471
WHAT, BUT THAT-- THAT HE WAS,
UM, DISAPPOINTED?

01:36:08.513 --> 01:36:09.389
HMM?

01:36:09.431 --> 01:36:10.432
I'M SORRY.

01:36:11.516 --> 01:36:13.184
BUT...

01:36:13.226 --> 01:36:15.103
HE'S WRONG.

01:36:15.144 --> 01:36:17.939
YOU CAN BUILD A BETTER COMPANY
THAN HE EVER DID.

01:36:17.980 --> 01:36:19.691
MR. FISCHER?

01:36:19.733 --> 01:36:21.150
HE'S LYING.

01:36:21.192 --> 01:36:22.860
HOW DO YOU KNOW?

01:36:22.902 --> 01:36:24.613
TRUST ME, IT'S WHAT I DO.
HE'S HIDING SOMETHING,

01:36:24.654 --> 01:36:26.364
AND WE NEED TO FIND OUT
WHAT THAT IS.

01:36:27.907 --> 01:36:29.492
I NEED YOU TO DO
THE SAME THING TO HIM

01:36:29.534 --> 01:36:30.952
THAT HE WAS
GOING TO DO TO YOU.

01:36:33.455 --> 01:36:34.956
WE'LL ENTER
HIS SUBCONSCIOUS

01:36:34.997 --> 01:36:36.832
AND FIND OUT WHAT
HE DOESN'T WANT YOU TO KNOW.

01:36:38.418 --> 01:36:39.835
ALL RIGHT.

01:36:45.799 --> 01:36:47.719
HE'S OUT.
WAIT.

01:36:47.761 --> 01:36:49.137
<i>WHOSE</i> SUBCONSCIOUS
ARE WE GOING INTO EXACTLY?

01:36:49.178 --> 01:36:50.804
WE'RE GOING
INTO FISCHER'S.

01:36:50.846 --> 01:36:52.181
BUT I TOLD HIM
IT WAS BROWNING'S

01:36:52.223 --> 01:36:54.309
SO HE'D COME BE A PART
OF OUR TEAM.

01:36:54.350 --> 01:36:57.811
HE'S GONNA HELP US BREAK
INTO HIS OWN SUBCONSCIOUS.
THAT'S RIGHT.

01:36:57.853 --> 01:37:00.690
SECURITY'S GONNA RUN
YOU DOWN HARD.

01:37:00.732 --> 01:37:03.192
AND I WILL LEAD THEM
ON A MERRY CHASE.

01:37:03.234 --> 01:37:05.153
JUST BE BACK
BEFORE THE KICK.

01:37:05.194 --> 01:37:06.362
GO TO SLEEP, MR. EAMES.

01:37:09.823 --> 01:37:13.202
YOU GOOD?

01:37:15.246 --> 01:37:17.373
HEY. YOU READY?

01:37:17.415 --> 01:37:19.041
YES, YES.
I'M-- I'M FINE.

01:37:19.083 --> 01:37:20.960
I'M-- I'M READY.

01:37:32.555 --> 01:37:34.932
COBB?

01:37:34.974 --> 01:37:36.518
COBB.

01:37:36.559 --> 01:37:38.019
WHAT'S DOWN THERE?

01:37:40.814 --> 01:37:43.483
HOPEFULLY, THE TRUTH
WE WANT FISCHER TO LEARN.

01:37:43.525 --> 01:37:46.068
I MEAN,
WHAT'S DOWN THERE FOR <i>YOU?</i>

01:37:55.704 --> 01:37:58.122
OHH!

01:38:20.228 --> 01:38:21.229
WHOA!

01:38:42.542 --> 01:38:43.543
OHH!

01:40:22.057 --> 01:40:23.726
DID YOU SEE THAT?

01:40:43.078 --> 01:40:44.789
EAMES, THIS IS YOUR DREAM.

01:40:44.831 --> 01:40:46.624
I NEED YOU TO DRAW THE SECURITY
AWAY FROM THE COMPLEX.

01:40:46.666 --> 01:40:47.876
YOU UNDERSTAND?

01:40:47.917 --> 01:40:49.126
WHO GUIDES FISCHER IN?

01:40:49.168 --> 01:40:50.503
NOT ME.

01:40:50.545 --> 01:40:52.672
IF I KNOW THE ROUTE,
EVERYTHING COULD BE COMPROMISED.

01:40:52.714 --> 01:40:54.131
I-I DESIGNED THE PLACE.

01:40:54.173 --> 01:40:55.383
NO, YOU'RE WITH ME.

01:40:55.424 --> 01:40:57.343
I COULD DO IT.

01:40:57.385 --> 01:40:59.762
ALL RIGHT. YOU BRIEF HIM
ON THE ROUTE INTO THE COMPLEX.

01:40:59.804 --> 01:41:02.055
FISCHER,
YOU'LL BE GOING WITH HIM.

01:41:02.097 --> 01:41:02.932
ALL RIGHT.

01:41:02.974 --> 01:41:04.308
WHAT ABOUT YOU?

01:41:04.350 --> 01:41:06.394
YOU KEEP THIS LIVE.

01:41:06.435 --> 01:41:08.021
I'LL BE LISTENING IN
THE WHOLE TIME.

01:41:08.061 --> 01:41:09.438
THE WINDOWS ON THAT UPPER
FLOOR ARE BIG ENOUGH

01:41:09.480 --> 01:41:11.607
FOR ME TO COVER YOU FROM
THAT SOUTH TOWER. YOU SEE IT?

01:41:11.649 --> 01:41:13.484
YEAH.
YOU'RE NOT COMING IN?

01:41:13.526 --> 01:41:15.319
IN ORDER TO FIND OUT THE TRUTH
ABOUT YOUR FATHER,

01:41:15.361 --> 01:41:16.821
YOU'RE GONNA NEED TO BREAK
INTO BROWNING'S MIND

01:41:16.863 --> 01:41:17.780
ON YOUR OWN.

01:41:19.532 --> 01:41:22.535
COME ON, FISCHER!

01:42:16.089 --> 01:42:18.633
SOUND THE ALARM!

01:42:18.674 --> 01:42:19.759
GO, GO, GO!

01:42:19.801 --> 01:42:21.552
MOVE!

01:42:22.678 --> 01:42:24.137
GO!

01:42:39.278 --> 01:42:40.404
SOD IT!

01:42:51.082 --> 01:42:53.292
I HOPE YOU'RE READY.

01:43:02.175 --> 01:43:03.761
NO, IT'S TOO SOON.

01:43:09.684 --> 01:43:11.519
COBB, DO YOU HEAR THAT?

01:43:11.560 --> 01:43:13.688
I first noticed it
about 20 minutes ago.

01:43:13.729 --> 01:43:15.230
I THOUGHT IT WAS
THE WIND UP HERE.

01:43:15.272 --> 01:43:17.650
YEAH, I HEAR IT.
IT'S MUSIC.

01:43:17.692 --> 01:43:19.443
SO, WHAT DO WE DO?

01:43:19.485 --> 01:43:21.362
WE MOVE FAST.

01:43:26.784 --> 01:43:28.369
YUSUF IS 10 SECONDS
FROM THE JUMP.

01:43:30.913 --> 01:43:32.498
WHICH GIVES ARTHUR
THREE MINUTES.

01:43:34.207 --> 01:43:36.919
HEY!
THAT'S HIM!

01:43:36.961 --> 01:43:38.838
WHICH GIVES US WHAT?
60 MINUTES.

01:43:38.880 --> 01:43:40.506
CAN THEY MAKE THAT ROUTE
IN UNDER AN HOUR?

01:43:40.548 --> 01:43:42.341
THEY STILL HAVE TO CLIMB DOWN
TO THE MIDDLE TERRACE.

01:43:42.383 --> 01:43:44.259
WELL, THEN, THEY NEED A NEW
ROUTE, A MORE DIRECT ROUTE.

01:43:56.147 --> 01:43:57.523
IT'S DESIGNED
AS A LABYRINTH.

01:43:57.565 --> 01:43:58.983
THERE MUST BE ACCESS ROUTES

01:43:59.025 --> 01:44:00.568
THAT CUT THROUGH THE MAZE,
RIGHT?

01:44:00.609 --> 01:44:01.861
EAMES?

01:44:25.676 --> 01:44:26.969
DID EAMES
ADD ANY FEATURES?

01:44:27.011 --> 01:44:28.846
I DON'T THINK
I SHOULD TELL YOU.

01:44:28.888 --> 01:44:31.015
IF MAL FINDS OUT,
THEN--
WE DON'T HAVE TIME FOR THIS!
DID HE ADD ANYTHING?

01:44:31.057 --> 01:44:34.227
HE ADDED AN AIR-DUCT SYSTEM
THAT CAN CUT THROUGH THE MAZE.

01:44:34.267 --> 01:44:35.603
GOOD.
EXPLAIN IT TO THEM.

01:44:35.644 --> 01:44:36.938
Saito?
GO AHEAD.

01:44:47.740 --> 01:44:48.908
AH!

01:45:03.672 --> 01:45:05.340
LOOK.

01:45:09.178 --> 01:45:11.639
PARADOX.

01:46:21.625 --> 01:46:22.543
WHAT WAS THAT?

01:46:22.584 --> 01:46:23.836
THE KICK.

01:46:23.878 --> 01:46:26.339
COBB! COBB,
DID WE MISS IT?

01:46:26.379 --> 01:46:28.216
YEAH, WE MISSED IT.

01:46:28.257 --> 01:46:30.092
MAN.

01:46:30.134 --> 01:46:33.470
COULDN'T SOMEONE HAVE
DREAMT OF A GODDAMN BEACH?!

01:46:33.512 --> 01:46:36.057
HUH?
MM-HMM.

01:46:36.098 --> 01:46:37.683
What the hell
do we do now?!

01:46:37.725 --> 01:46:39.434
WE FINISH THE JOB

01:46:39.476 --> 01:46:41.394
before the next kick.
<i>WHAT</i> NEXT KICK?

01:46:41.436 --> 01:46:43.231
WHEN THE VAN HITS THE WATER.

01:47:05.418 --> 01:47:07.129
Female computerized voice:
<i>IF YOU'D LIKE TO MAKE A CALL,</i>

01:47:07.171 --> 01:47:08.505
<i>PLEASE HANG UP AND TRY AGAIN.</i>

01:47:08.547 --> 01:47:10.258
<i>IF YOU NEED HELP, HANG UP...</i>

01:47:10.299 --> 01:47:14.427
HOW DO I DROP YOU
WITHOUT GRAVITY?

01:47:16.638 --> 01:47:19.600
ARTHUR HAS A COUPLE MINUTES,
AND WE HAVE ABOUT 20.

01:47:42.164 --> 01:47:44.708
YOU OKAY?

01:47:48.421 --> 01:47:51.673
RUN! TURN AROUND!
MOVE TO BASE!

01:47:51.715 --> 01:47:54.093
MOVE TO BASE!

01:47:56.845 --> 01:47:58.513
THERE'S SOMETHING WRONG.

01:47:58.555 --> 01:47:59.807
THEY'RE HEADING YOUR WAY
LIKE THEY KNOW SOMETHING.

01:48:01.600 --> 01:48:04.728
JUST-- JUST BUY US MORE TIME,
ALL RIGHT? COME ON!

01:48:04.770 --> 01:48:06.105
ON MY WAY.

01:48:06.147 --> 01:48:07.940
COME ON! MOVE!

01:49:45.746 --> 01:49:48.665
THAT'S THE ANTECHAMBER
OUTSIDE THE STRONG ROOM.

01:49:48.707 --> 01:49:50.459
DOES THE STRONG ROOM
HAVE ANY WINDOWS?

01:49:50.501 --> 01:49:52.336
NO, I MEAN, IT WOULDN'T BE
VERY STRONG IF IT DID.

01:49:52.378 --> 01:49:54.713
WELL, LET'S HOPE FISCHER
LIKES WHAT HE FINDS IN THERE.

01:49:56.257 --> 01:49:58.467
ARE THOSE PROJECTIONS JUST
A PART OF HIS SUBCONSCIOUS?

01:49:58.509 --> 01:50:00.135
YES.

01:50:00.177 --> 01:50:01.803
ARE YOU DESTROYING THOSE
PARTS OF HIS MIND?

01:50:01.845 --> 01:50:03.222
NO, NO.
THEY'RE JUST PROJECTIONS.

01:50:29.248 --> 01:50:30.541
WE'RE HERE.

01:50:30.583 --> 01:50:32.000
YOU'RE CLEAR, BUT HURRY.

01:50:32.042 --> 01:50:33.294
THERE'S AN ENTIRE ARMY
HEADED YOUR WAY.

01:51:00.112 --> 01:51:01.113
I'M IN.

01:51:06.619 --> 01:51:07.869
THERE HE IS!

01:51:50.371 --> 01:51:51.622
THERE'S SOMEONE ELSE
IN THERE.

01:51:51.664 --> 01:51:53.165
FISCHER, IT'S A TRAP.
GET OUT!

01:51:54.249 --> 01:51:56.877
COME ON.
COME ON, A LITTLE LOWER.

01:52:01.965 --> 01:52:04.968
COBB. NO.

01:52:05.010 --> 01:52:07.012
SHE-- SHE IS <i>NOT</i> REAL.

01:52:07.054 --> 01:52:08.847
HOW DO YOU KNOW THAT?

01:52:08.889 --> 01:52:10.349
SHE'S JUST A PROJECTION.

01:52:10.391 --> 01:52:12.601
FISCHER.
FISCHER IS REAL!

01:52:16.188 --> 01:52:18.731
HELLO.

01:52:22.486 --> 01:52:26.031
EAMES! EAMES,
GET TO THE ANTECHAMBER NOW!

01:53:09.324 --> 01:53:10.534
WHAT HAPPENED?

01:53:10.576 --> 01:53:13.370
MAL KILLED FISCHER.

01:53:14.996 --> 01:53:17.165
I COULDN'T SHOOT HER.

01:53:17.207 --> 01:53:19.126
LOOK, THERE'S NO USE
IN REVIVING HIM.

01:53:19.167 --> 01:53:21.169
HIS MIND'S ALREADY
TRAPPED DOWN THERE.

01:53:21.211 --> 01:53:22.421
IT'S ALL OVER.

01:53:22.463 --> 01:53:25.798
SO THAT'S IT, THEN?
WE FAILED?

01:53:25.840 --> 01:53:28.594
WE'RE DONE. I'M SORRY.

01:53:32.556 --> 01:53:33.474
WELL, IT'S NOT <i>ME</i> THAT DOESN'T

01:53:33.515 --> 01:53:34.807
GET BACK TO MY FAMILY, IS IT?

01:53:35.976 --> 01:53:37.352
IT'S A SHAME.
I REALLY WANTED TO KNOW

01:53:37.394 --> 01:53:39.480
WHAT WAS GONNA HAPPEN IN THERE.
I SWEAR WE HAD THIS ONE.

01:53:39.521 --> 01:53:41.940
LET'S SET THE CHARGES.

01:53:41.982 --> 01:53:45.235
NO, THERE'S STILL ANOTHER WAY.

01:53:46.445 --> 01:53:48.113
WE JUST HAVE TO FOLLOW FISCHER
DOWN THERE.

01:53:48.155 --> 01:53:49.990
NOT ENOUGH TIME.

01:53:50.031 --> 01:53:53.952
NO, BUT THERE WILL <i>BE</i>
ENOUGH TIME DOWN THERE.

01:53:53.994 --> 01:53:55.496
AND WE WILL <i>FIND</i> HIM.

01:53:55.537 --> 01:53:57.623
OKAY, AS SOON
AS ARTHUR'S MUSIC KICKS IN,

01:53:57.665 --> 01:53:59.583
JUST USE THE DEFIBRILLATOR
TO REVIVE HIM.

01:53:59.625 --> 01:54:02.377
WE CAN GIVE HIM HIS OWN KICK
DOWN BELOW.

01:54:02.419 --> 01:54:04.338
LOOK, YOU GET HIM IN THERE.

01:54:04.379 --> 01:54:08.133
AS SOON AS THE MUSIC ENDS,
YOU BLOW UP THE HOSPITAL,

01:54:08.175 --> 01:54:11.386
AND WE ALL RIDE THE KICK
BACK UP THE LAYERS.

01:54:11.428 --> 01:54:13.972
WELL, IT'S WORTH A SHOT,

01:54:14.014 --> 01:54:17.100
IF SAITO CAN HOLD THE GUARDS OFF
WHILE I SET THE CHARGES.

01:54:17.142 --> 01:54:18.769
SAITO WILL NEVER MAKE IT,
WILL HE?

01:54:20.562 --> 01:54:22.523
COBB, COME ON.
WE'VE GOTTA TRY THIS.

01:54:22.564 --> 01:54:24.107
GO FOR IT.

01:54:24.149 --> 01:54:25.776
BUT IF YOU ARE NOT BACK
BEFORE THE KICK,

01:54:25.818 --> 01:54:27.235
I AM GONE
WITH OR WITHOUT YOU.

01:54:27.277 --> 01:54:28.779
SHE'S RIGHT.

01:54:33.617 --> 01:54:36.203
CAN I TRUST YOU TO DO
WHAT NEEDS TO HAPPEN HERE?

01:54:36.244 --> 01:54:38.205
I MEAN,
MAL'S GONNA BE DOWN THERE.

01:54:38.246 --> 01:54:40.791
I KNOW WHERE TO FIND HER.
SHE'LL HAVE FISCHER.

01:54:40.833 --> 01:54:42.543
HOW DO YOU KNOW?

01:54:42.584 --> 01:54:44.127
BECAUSE, SHE WANTS ME
TO COME AFTER HIM.

01:54:44.169 --> 01:54:47.172
SHE WANTS ME BACK DOWN THERE
WITH HER.

01:55:13.407 --> 01:55:14.949
YOU ALL RIGHT?

01:55:21.248 --> 01:55:23.417
THIS IS YOUR WORLD?

01:55:23.458 --> 01:55:25.627
IT <i>WAS.</i>

01:55:25.669 --> 01:55:27.713
THIS IS WHERE SHE'LL BE.

01:55:27.755 --> 01:55:30.424
COME ON.

01:56:15.176 --> 01:56:17.220
SAITO.

01:56:17.262 --> 01:56:19.890
SAITO.

01:56:19.932 --> 01:56:21.767
I NEED YOU-- I NEED YOU
TO TAKE CARE OF FISCHER

01:56:21.809 --> 01:56:23.310
WHILE I GO SET
SOME CHARGES, OKAY?

01:56:23.351 --> 01:56:26.020
NO ROOM FOR TOURISTS
ON THESE JOBS.

01:56:29.399 --> 01:56:30.651
DON'T BE SILLY.

01:57:02.223 --> 01:57:05.268
YOU BUILT ALL THIS?

01:57:05.310 --> 01:57:06.520
THIS IS INCREDIBLE.

01:57:06.561 --> 01:57:07.938
WE BUILT FOR YEARS.

01:57:07.980 --> 01:57:10.774
THEN WE STARTED IN
ON THE MEMORIES.

01:57:17.489 --> 01:57:19.741
THIS WAY.

01:58:00.448 --> 01:58:02.325
THIS WAS OUR NEIGHBORHOOD.

01:58:02.367 --> 01:58:05.537
PLACES FROM OUR PAST.

01:58:05.579 --> 01:58:07.539
THAT WAS
OUR FIRST APARTMENT.

01:58:07.581 --> 01:58:09.791
THEN WE MOVED TO THAT BUILDING
RIGHT THERE.

01:58:09.833 --> 01:58:12.502
AFTER MAL BECAME PREGNANT,
THAT BECAME OUR HOME.

01:58:12.544 --> 01:58:14.922
YOU RECONSTRUCTED
ALL OF THIS FROM MEMORY?

01:58:14.963 --> 01:58:17.674
LIKE I TOLD YOU,
WE HAD LOTS OF TIME.

01:58:17.716 --> 01:58:19.009
WHAT IS THAT?

01:58:19.051 --> 01:58:22.429
THAT'S THE HOUSE
MAL GREW UP IN.

01:58:22.470 --> 01:58:24.138
WELL,
WILL SHE BE IN THERE?

01:58:24.180 --> 01:58:27.017
NO. COME ON.

01:58:27.059 --> 01:58:28.769
WE BOTH WANTED
TO LIVE IN A HOUSE,

01:58:28.810 --> 01:58:30.520
BUT WE LOVED THIS TYPE
OF BUILDING.

01:58:30.562 --> 01:58:33.899
IN THE REAL WORLD, WE'D HAVE
TO CHOOSE, BUT NOT HERE.

01:59:14.064 --> 01:59:16.232
HOW ARE WE GONNA BRING
FISCHER BACK?

01:59:16.274 --> 01:59:19.069
WE'RE GONNA HAVE TO COME UP
WITH SOME KIND OF A KICK.

01:59:19.111 --> 01:59:20.988
WHAT?

01:59:21.029 --> 01:59:22.739
I'M GONNA IMPROVISE.

01:59:22.781 --> 01:59:25.158
LISTEN, THERE'S SOMETHING
YOU SHOULD KNOW ABOUT ME.

01:59:25.199 --> 01:59:27.160
ABOUT INCEPTION.

01:59:39.673 --> 01:59:42.843
AN IDEA IS LIKE A VIRUS.

01:59:42.884 --> 01:59:44.552
RESILIENT.

01:59:44.594 --> 01:59:46.930
HIGHLY CONTAGIOUS.

01:59:46.972 --> 01:59:50.475
AND THE SMALLEST SEED
OF AN IDEA CAN GROW.

01:59:50.517 --> 01:59:53.603
IT CAN GROW TO DEFINE...

01:59:53.645 --> 01:59:56.731
OR DESTROY YOU.

01:59:58.650 --> 02:00:02.445
THE SMALLEST IDEA,
SUCH AS...

02:00:02.487 --> 02:00:05.824
"YOUR WORLD IS NOT REAL."

02:00:05.866 --> 02:00:09.243
SIMPLE LITTLE THOUGHT
THAT CHANGES EVERYTHING.

02:00:09.285 --> 02:00:12.706
SO CERTAIN OF YOUR WORLD.

02:00:12.747 --> 02:00:15.042
OF WHAT'S REAL.

02:00:15.083 --> 02:00:17.460
DO YOU THINK <i>HE</i> IS?

02:00:17.502 --> 02:00:21.756
OR DO YOU THINK HE'S AS LOST
AS I WAS?

02:00:21.798 --> 02:00:24.009
I KNOW WHAT'S REAL, MAL.

02:00:26.427 --> 02:00:28.180
NO CREEPING DOUBTS?

02:00:28.221 --> 02:00:31.474
NOT FEELING
PERSECUTED, DOM?

02:00:31.516 --> 02:00:33.351
CHASED AROUND THE GLOBE

02:00:33.393 --> 02:00:35.645
BY ANONYMOUS CORPORATIONS
AND POLICE FORCES?

02:00:35.687 --> 02:00:38.857
THE WAY THE PROJECTIONS
PERSECUTE THE DREAMER?

02:00:40.692 --> 02:00:41.693
ADMIT IT.

02:00:43.444 --> 02:00:45.780
YOU DON'T BELIEVE
IN ONE REALITY ANYMORE.

02:00:45.822 --> 02:00:47.949
SO CHOOSE.

02:00:47.991 --> 02:00:50.160
CHOOSE TO BE HERE.

02:00:50.202 --> 02:00:52.412
CHOOSE ME.

02:00:55.082 --> 02:00:57.417
AAH!

02:00:57.458 --> 02:00:58.710
UNH!

02:01:18.563 --> 02:01:19.773
YOU KNOW
WHAT I HAVE TO DO.

02:01:19.814 --> 02:01:21.066
I HAVE TO GET BACK
TO OUR CHILDREN

02:01:21.108 --> 02:01:22.859
BECAUSE YOU LEFT THEM.

02:01:23.693 --> 02:01:25.237
BECAUSE YOU LEFT <i>US.</i>

02:01:25.278 --> 02:01:27.155
YOU'RE WRONG.
I'M NOT WRONG.

02:01:27.197 --> 02:01:29.490
YOU'RE CONFUSED.

02:01:29.532 --> 02:01:33.161
OUR CHILDREN ARE HERE.

02:01:33.203 --> 02:01:35.747
AND YOU'D LIKE TO SEE THEIR
FACES AGAIN, WOULDN'T YOU?

02:01:36.706 --> 02:01:37.749
YES...

02:01:37.791 --> 02:01:39.834
BUT I'M GONNA SEE THEM
UP ABOVE, MAL.

02:01:52.806 --> 02:01:55.475
"UP ABOVE"?

02:01:55.516 --> 02:01:58.019
LISTEN TO YOURSELF.

02:01:58.061 --> 02:02:00.021
THESE ARE OUR CHILDREN.

02:02:00.063 --> 02:02:02.065
WATCH.

02:02:02.107 --> 02:02:03.733
JAMES? PHILLIPA?

02:02:03.775 --> 02:02:05.902
DON'T DO THIS, MAL.
PLEASE.

02:02:05.944 --> 02:02:07.237
THOSE <i>AREN'T</i> MY CHILDREN.

02:02:07.279 --> 02:02:08.446
YOU KEEP TELLING
YOURSELF THAT,

02:02:08.488 --> 02:02:09.739
BUT YOU DON'T BELIEVE IT.

02:02:09.781 --> 02:02:11.283
NO, I <i>KNOW</i> IT.

02:02:11.324 --> 02:02:14.661
AND WHAT IF YOU'RE WRONG?
WHAT IF <i>I'M</i> WHAT'S REAL?

02:02:14.702 --> 02:02:17.580
YOU KEEP TELLING YOURSELF
WHAT YOU <i>KNOW.</i>

02:02:17.622 --> 02:02:21.584
BUT WHAT DO YOU <i>BELIEVE?</i>

02:02:21.626 --> 02:02:23.586
WHAT DO YOU <i>FEEL?</i>

02:02:25.546 --> 02:02:26.631
GUILT.

02:02:28.175 --> 02:02:30.135
I FEEL GUILT, MAL.

02:02:30.969 --> 02:02:32.929
AND NO MATTER WHAT
I DO, NO...

02:02:33.596 --> 02:02:35.098
NO MATTER
HOW HOPELESS I AM,

02:02:35.140 --> 02:02:37.017
NO MATTER HOW CONFUSED,

02:02:37.058 --> 02:02:39.519
THAT GUILT
IS ALWAYS THERE,

02:02:39.560 --> 02:02:41.980
REMINDING ME
OF THE TRUTH.

02:02:42.022 --> 02:02:43.940
WHAT TRUTH?

02:02:45.566 --> 02:02:49.863
THAT THE IDEA THAT CAUSED YOU
TO QUESTION YOUR REALITY

02:02:49.904 --> 02:02:52.073
CAME FROM ME.

02:02:54.117 --> 02:02:58.205
YOU PLANTED THE IDEA
IN MY MIND?

02:02:58.246 --> 02:03:01.208
WHAT IS SHE TALKING ABOUT?

02:03:01.249 --> 02:03:04.336
THE REASON I KNEW
INCEPTION WAS POSSIBLE

02:03:04.377 --> 02:03:07.380
WAS BECAUSE I...
I DID IT TO HER FIRST.

02:03:07.421 --> 02:03:09.841
I DID IT TO MY OWN WIFE.

02:03:09.883 --> 02:03:11.384
WHY?

02:03:11.425 --> 02:03:13.594
WE WERE LOST IN HERE.

02:03:13.636 --> 02:03:19.559
I KNEW WE NEEDED TO ESCAPE,
BUT SHE WOULDN'T ACCEPT IT.

02:03:22.020 --> 02:03:24.522
SHE HAD LOCKED
SOMETHING AWAY,

02:03:24.564 --> 02:03:28.068
SOMETHING...
SOMETHING DEEP INSIDE.

02:03:28.109 --> 02:03:31.112
THAT TRUTH
THAT SHE HAD ONCE KNOWN,

02:03:31.154 --> 02:03:33.447
BUT CHOSE TO FORGET.

02:03:33.489 --> 02:03:36.034
AND SHE COULDN'T
BREAK FREE.

02:03:38.161 --> 02:03:41.915
SO I DECIDED
TO SEARCH FOR IT.

02:03:41.956 --> 02:03:45.210
I WENT DEEP INTO THE RECESS
OF HER MIND

02:03:45.252 --> 02:03:47.379
AND FOUND
THAT SECRET PLACE.

02:03:47.420 --> 02:03:49.005
AND I BROKE IN...

02:03:49.047 --> 02:03:52.092
AND I PLANTED AN IDEA.

02:03:52.133 --> 02:03:55.636
A SIMPLE LITTLE IDEA
THAT WOULD CHANGE EVERYTHING...

02:04:00.934 --> 02:04:04.145
...THAT HER WORLD
WASN'T REAL.

02:04:15.573 --> 02:04:19.827
THAT DEATH
WAS THE ONLY ESCAPE.

02:04:26.167 --> 02:04:28.420
YOU'RE WAITING
FOR A TRAIN.

02:04:30.130 --> 02:04:33.883
A TRAIN THAT'LL TAKE YOU
FAR AWAY.

02:04:33.925 --> 02:04:37.262
YOU KNOW WHERE YOU HOPE
THIS TRAIN WILL TAKE YOU.

02:04:39.639 --> 02:04:41.724
BUT YOU CAN'T KNOW
FOR SURE!

02:04:42.892 --> 02:04:44.102
YET IT DOESN'T MATTER!

02:04:44.144 --> 02:04:46.687
NOW, TELL ME WHY!

02:04:46.729 --> 02:04:48.689
BECAUSE YOU'LL BE TOGETHER!

02:04:52.652 --> 02:04:54.904
BUT I NEVER KNEW
THAT THAT IDEA

02:04:54.946 --> 02:04:57.531
WOULD GROW IN HER MIND
LIKE A CANCER,

02:04:57.573 --> 02:04:59.909
THAT EVEN
AFTER SHE WOKE...

02:05:02.454 --> 02:05:04.998
THAT EVEN AFTER
YOU CAME BACK TO REALITY...

02:05:07.875 --> 02:05:10.920
...THAT YOU'D CONTINUE TO
BELIEVE YOUR WORLD WASN'T REAL.

02:05:13.589 --> 02:05:16.134
THAT DEATH
WAS THE ONLY ESCAPE.

02:05:16.176 --> 02:05:18.970
MAL, NO! JESUS!

02:05:19.012 --> 02:05:21.348
YOU INFECTED MY MIND.

02:05:21.389 --> 02:05:22.849
I WAS TRYING TO SAVE YOU.

02:05:22.890 --> 02:05:24.392
YOU BETRAYED ME.

02:05:24.434 --> 02:05:26.727
BUT YOU CAN MAKE AMENDS.

02:05:26.769 --> 02:05:28.646
YOU CAN STILL
KEEP YOUR PROMISE.

02:05:28.688 --> 02:05:32.150
WE CAN STILL BE TOGETHER,
RIGHT HERE,

02:05:32.192 --> 02:05:34.735
IN THE WORLD
WE BUILT TOGETHER.

02:06:56.526 --> 02:06:58.445
COBB,
WE NEED TO GET FISCHER.

02:06:58.486 --> 02:07:00.113
YOU CAN'T HAVE HIM.

02:07:00.154 --> 02:07:03.116
IF I STAY HERE,
WILL YOU LET HIM GO?

02:07:03.157 --> 02:07:04.534
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

02:07:08.329 --> 02:07:10.873
FISCHER IS ON THE PORCH.

02:07:10.915 --> 02:07:12.459
GO CHECK HE'S ALIVE,
ARIADNE.

02:07:12.500 --> 02:07:14.043
COBB, YOU CAN'T DO THIS.

02:07:14.085 --> 02:07:17.297
GO CHECK HE'S ALIVE RIGHT NOW.
DO IT.

02:07:33.104 --> 02:07:35.607
HE'S HERE! AND IT'S TIME,
BUT YOU HAVE TO COME NOW!

02:07:35.648 --> 02:07:37.358
TAKE FISCHER WITH YOU,
ALL RIGHT?

02:07:37.400 --> 02:07:39.402
YOU <i>CAN'T</i> STAY HERE TO BE
WITH HER.

02:07:41.070 --> 02:07:43.072
I'M NOT.

02:07:43.114 --> 02:07:44.698
SAITO'S DEAD BY NOW.

02:07:44.740 --> 02:07:46.409
THAT MEANS HE'S DOWN
HERE SOMEWHERE.

02:07:46.451 --> 02:07:48.369
THAT MEANS
I HAVE TO FIND HIM.

02:07:50.163 --> 02:07:51.956
I CAN'T STAY
WITH HER ANYMORE

02:07:51.998 --> 02:07:53.500
BECAUSE SHE
DOESN'T EXIST.

02:07:53.541 --> 02:07:57.044
I'M THE ONLY THING YOU DO
BELIEVE IN ANYMORE.

02:07:58.712 --> 02:08:01.841
I WISH.

02:08:01.882 --> 02:08:06.804
I WISH MORE
THAN ANYTHING, BUT...

02:08:06.846 --> 02:08:09.098
I CAN'T IMAGINE YOU
WITH ALL YOUR COMPLEXITY,

02:08:09.140 --> 02:08:11.809
ALL YOUR PERFECTION,
ALL YOUR IMPERFECTION.

02:08:12.977 --> 02:08:13.520
YOU ALL RIGHT?

02:08:13.561 --> 02:08:14.437
YEAH.

02:08:14.479 --> 02:08:16.439
LOOK AT YOU.

02:08:16.481 --> 02:08:18.483
YOU'RE JUST A SHADE.

02:08:18.525 --> 02:08:22.111
YOU'RE JUST A SHADE
OF MY REAL WIFE.

02:08:22.153 --> 02:08:24.989
AND YOU WERE THE BEST
THAT I COULD DO, BUT...

02:08:25.031 --> 02:08:28.451
I'M SORRY,
YOU'RE JUST NOT GOOD ENOUGH.

02:08:28.493 --> 02:08:30.911
DOES <i>THIS</i> FEEL REAL?!
AAH!

02:08:32.539 --> 02:08:33.581
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?!

02:08:34.415 --> 02:08:35.291
IMPROVISING.

02:08:43.757 --> 02:08:46.386
NO, NO! NO!

02:08:46.427 --> 02:08:49.681
IN THERE, NOW.
GO. GO, GO, GO.

02:09:32.515 --> 02:09:36.477
I WAS DIS...

02:09:36.519 --> 02:09:40.064
I WAS DIS-- DISA...

02:09:40.106 --> 02:09:41.482
I KNOW, DAD.

02:09:41.524 --> 02:09:43.109
DISA...

02:09:48.197 --> 02:09:53.411
I KNOW YOU WERE DISAPPOINTED
I COULDN'T BE YOU.

02:09:53.453 --> 02:09:54.912
NO.

02:09:54.954 --> 02:09:57.206
NO, NO, NO.

02:09:57.248 --> 02:10:00.834
I WAS DISAPPOINTED...

02:10:00.876 --> 02:10:03.713
THAT YOU TRIED.

02:11:49.193 --> 02:11:51.070
THAT'S THE KICK, ARIADNE!

02:11:51.111 --> 02:11:52.363
YOU HAVE TO GO NOW!

02:12:05.125 --> 02:12:08.671
DON'T LOSE YOURSELF!
FIND SAITO AND BRING HIM BACK!

02:12:08.713 --> 02:12:09.839
I WILL!

02:12:49.670 --> 02:12:52.840
YOU REMEMBER
WHEN YOU ASKED ME TO MARRY YOU?

02:12:52.882 --> 02:12:54.675
YES.

02:12:54.717 --> 02:12:57.887
YOU SAID YOU DREAMT
THAT WE'D GROW OLD TOGETHER.

02:12:59.847 --> 02:13:01.933
BUT WE DID.

02:13:04.226 --> 02:13:04.977
WE DID.

02:13:05.018 --> 02:13:05.853
YOU DON'T REMEMBER?

02:13:09.941 --> 02:13:14.987
I MISS YOU MORE
THAN I CAN BEAR, BUT...

02:13:15.028 --> 02:13:18.741
WE HAD OUR TIME
TOGETHER.

02:13:18.783 --> 02:13:22.328
AND I HAVE TO
LET YOU GO.

02:13:22.369 --> 02:13:26.916
I HAVE TO LET YOU GO.

02:14:16.215 --> 02:14:18.133
I'M SORRY, ROBERT.

02:14:44.994 --> 02:14:46.620
YOU KNOW, THE WILL MEANS

02:14:46.662 --> 02:14:49.582
THAT DAD WANTED ME
TO BE MY OWN MAN...

02:14:49.623 --> 02:14:53.293
NOT JUST TO LIVE FOR HIM.

02:14:53.335 --> 02:14:57.297
THAT'S WHAT I'M GONNA DO,
UNCLE PETER.

02:15:05.639 --> 02:15:07.307
WHAT HAPPENED?

02:15:07.349 --> 02:15:08.601
COBB STAYED.

02:15:08.642 --> 02:15:09.936
WITH MAL?

02:15:09.977 --> 02:15:11.311
NO, TO FIND SAITO.

02:15:13.064 --> 02:15:14.523
HE'LL BE LOST.

02:15:16.984 --> 02:15:19.319
NO, HE'LL BE ALL RIGHT.

02:15:34.585 --> 02:15:37.713
HAVE YOU COME TO KILL ME?

02:15:41.884 --> 02:15:43.970
I'M WAITING FOR SOMEONE.

02:15:48.849 --> 02:15:51.560
SOMEONE FROM
A HALF-REMEMBERED DREAM.

02:15:53.729 --> 02:15:55.982
COBB?

02:15:57.817 --> 02:15:59.401
IMPOSSIBLE.

02:15:59.443 --> 02:16:03.614
WE WERE YOUNG MEN
TOGETHER.

02:16:03.656 --> 02:16:06.951
I'M AN OLD MAN.

02:16:06.993 --> 02:16:10.496
FILLED WITH REGRET.

02:16:12.623 --> 02:16:17.336
WAITING TO DIE ALONE.

02:16:17.377 --> 02:16:20.881
I'VE COME BACK FOR YOU.

02:16:23.425 --> 02:16:27.805
TO REMIND YOU...
OF SOMETHING.

02:16:30.641 --> 02:16:34.979
SOMETHING YOU ONCE KNEW.

02:16:35.021 --> 02:16:38.983
THAT THIS WORLD
IS NOT REAL.

02:16:43.320 --> 02:16:48.408
TO CONVINCE ME TO HONOR
OUR ARRANGEMENT?

02:16:48.450 --> 02:16:51.996
TO TAKE A LEAP
OF FAITH, YES.

02:16:57.334 --> 02:16:59.461
COME BACK...

02:17:01.380 --> 02:17:05.592
...SO WE CAN BE YOUNG MEN
TOGETHER AGAIN.

02:17:08.261 --> 02:17:10.430
COME BACK WITH ME.

02:17:13.559 --> 02:17:15.602
COME BACK.

02:17:24.653 --> 02:17:26.906
Flight attendant:
HOT TOWEL, SIR?

02:17:26.947 --> 02:17:30.701
WE'LL BE LANDING IN LOS ANGELES
IN ABOUT 20 MINUTES.

02:17:30.743 --> 02:17:33.328
DO YOU NEED
IMMIGRATION FORMS?

02:17:34.371 --> 02:17:36.498
THANK YOU.

02:17:36.540 --> 02:17:38.959
HOT TOWEL, SIR?

02:17:39.001 --> 02:17:40.335
UH, NO.

02:17:40.377 --> 02:17:42.171
DO YOU NEED
IMMIGRATION FORMS?

02:18:52.992 --> 02:18:55.077
WELCOME HOME, MR. COBB.

02:18:55.119 --> 02:18:57.079
THANK YOU, SIR.

02:19:40.831 --> 02:19:43.250
WELCOME.

02:19:43.292 --> 02:19:45.085
THIS WAY.

02:20:06.190 --> 02:20:09.735
JAMES? PHILLIPA?

02:20:12.654 --> 02:20:14.740
LOOK WHO'S HERE.

02:20:20.453 --> 02:20:21.454
HEY.

02:20:21.496 --> 02:20:23.290
HEY, GUYS!

02:20:23.874 --> 02:20:24.457
DADDY!

02:20:24.499 --> 02:20:25.709
HEY! HOW ARE YOU?

02:20:25.751 --> 02:20:27.711
DADDY!
HOW ARE YOU?

02:20:27.753 --> 02:20:30.130
LOOK WHAT
I'VE BEEN BUILDING!

02:20:30.172 --> 02:20:31.882
WHAT ARE YOU BUILDING?

02:20:31.924 --> 02:20:33.842
WE'RE BUILDING A HOUSE
ON THE CLIFF!

02:20:33.884 --> 02:20:35.677
ON THE CLIFF?

02:20:35.719 --> 02:20:38.013
COME ON,
I WANT YOU TO SHOW ME.

02:26:58.393 --> 02:27:03.940
♪ NON, RIEN DE RIEN ♪

02:27:03.982 --> 02:27:09.446
♪ NON, JE NE REGRETTE RIEN ♪

02:27:09.488 --> 02:27:15.034
♪ NI LE BIEN QU'ON M'A FAIT ♪

02:27:15.076 --> 02:27:21.040
♪ NI LE MAL
TOUT ÇA M'EST BIEN ÉGAL ♪

02:27:21.082 --> 02:27:26.212
♪ NON, RIEN DE RIEN ♪

02:27:26.254 --> 02:27:31.384
♪ NON, JE NE REGRETTE RIEN ♪

02:27:31.426 --> 02:27:37.015
♪ CAR MA VIE, CAR MES JOIES ♪

02:27:37.056 --> 02:27:41.019
♪ AUJOURD'HUI ♪
